vatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"98a62a62ce7e1e6e6100c6e888e9d2bd794378e2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/98a62a62ce7e1e6e6100c6e888e9d2bd794378e2","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/98a62a62ce7e1e6e6100c6e888e9d2bd794378e2"}]},{"sha":"98a62a62ce7e1e6e6100c6e888e9d2bd794378e2","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDk4YTYyYTYyY2U3ZTFlNmU2MTAwYzZlODg4ZTlkMmJkNzk0Mzc4ZTI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Anton Panasenko","email":"apanasenko@openai.com","date":"2026-06-03T00:01:02Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-03T00:01:02Z"},"message":"feat(app-server): add remote control client management RPCs (#25785)\n\n## Why\n\nRemote-control clients need to list and revoke controller-device grants\nwithout enabling or enrolling the local relay. These are signed-in\naccount-management operations, so coupling them to websocket, pairing,\nenrollment, or persisted relay state would prevent clients from managing\nstale grants from the picker.\n\nRelated enhancement request: N/A. This adds the Codex app-server surface\nfor the planned upstream environment-scoped revoke endpoint.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Added experimental app-server v2 RPCs:\n  - `remoteControl/client/list`\n  - `remoteControl/client/revoke`\n- Added picker-oriented protocol types and standard generated schema\nfixtures. The list response intentionally omits backend account id,\nenrollment status, and location fields.\n- Added `app-server-transport/src/transport/remote_control/clients.rs`\nfor environment-scoped GET and DELETE requests. It builds escaped URL\npath segments, forwards optional pagination query fields, sends ChatGPT\nauth plus `chatgpt-account-id`, converts RFC3339 `last_seen_at` values\nto Unix seconds, accepts `204 No Content` revoke responses, and retries\nonce after a `401`.\n- Extracted shared ChatGPT auth loading and recovery into\n`app-server-transport/src/transport/remote_control/auth.rs` so\nwebsocket, pairing, and client management use the same account-auth\nboundary.\n- Retained the configured remote-control base URL on\n`RemoteControlHandle` and resolve management URLs lazily, preserving\ndeferred validation while relay startup is disabled.\n- Registered list as `global_shared_read(\"remote-control-clients\")` and\nrevoke as `global(\"remote-control-clients\")`.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Added transport coverage proving list and revoke work while relay\nstate is disabled, IDs are escaped, picker-only fields are returned,\ntimestamps are converted, revoke accepts `204`, auth headers are\nforwarded, `401` retries exactly once, `403` is not retried, and\nmalformed list payloads retain decode context.\n- Added an app-server integration test proving both JSON-RPC methods\nwork before relay enablement and successful revoke returns `{}`.\n- Regenerated and validated experimental and standard app-server schema\nfixtures.","tree":{"sha":"a3d1e9b7e180dc79dcebf08f3d42250c44f6534a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/a3d1e9b7e180dc79dcebf08f3d42250c44f6534a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/98a62a62ce7e1e6e6100c6e888e9d2bd794378e2","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqH26+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAtwwQAEAWucqkH+a6zBSQnHDuKg8D\nyyg6Fl5Dd64iLOypSCDVcUeVcAe9cW0mDgP7XUtjXzPjgkzYXFzq2OFSTsuDrIG5\nbBUrD8Jdi0dPC7A2YXClW+et7rq5Cb78PY87po683vjf0ej8k9Ys8Jws//OxMLlW\nJ++4B7DrDD+Rmfxxc58/Zuu/wGtG1Mbh+T1aluYZt30Srtk+lbKif7e11C3iyvIg\nB8eDN27JW57+mUUSshWTCfiamlssr4Z+ByibJuMHYy+V7wCBvlr52O1BuVXJbisk\nOYY26hZsTd4MkRp4DwNesCPYh9ui8HZyqF+8aXZwUaAMO6o7efK9jw1tfeJF0gat\njKFTAr19qjvoNlyNUokb9fLG24wQrv1epW/Cf8Ti/X+DA27t9fFThTLsO4BpUuOz\nKyVKTvZe6g33IR2V3/6ppJ+ZOb0WX0ffg2A9/HE8ChA8gc3EZCcduUXgCGMtZDkE\ny0RNERjb5cxEjsMLqjIwP1clAcncW68+alMKyOcI7XSW9yViOYkJs3pO9JJ6EcPX\npBl249kyAfOPSnRPYVBEQc/0X2UArcgrghprFw0ASvAxyFTGfFFRhRda86jfuKAk\nAOSKR23Xa/HkjWHpv00Ad0oO1gtsBf2FqvDkOGCyCovFxAXYS4DUtAEKx9CaKrJo\ns+EeIOB2I8UsZucTUITK\n=cu5R\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a3d1e9b7e180dc79dcebf08f3d42250c44f6534a\nparent 1fd2a6d328017c58f4863b76f430d4000cbfd1b5\nauthor Anton Panasenko <apanasenko@openai.com> 1780444862 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780444862 -0700\n\nfeat(app-server): add remote control client management RPCs (#25785)\n\n## Why\n\nRemote-control clients need to list and revoke controller-device grants\nwithout enabling or enrolling the local relay. These are signed-in\naccount-management operations, so coupling them to websocket, pairing,\nenrollment, or persisted relay state would prevent clients from managing\nstale grants from the picker.\n\nRelated enhancement request: N/A. This adds the Codex app-server surface\nfor the planned upstream environment-scoped revoke endpoint.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Added experimental app-server v2 RPCs:\n  - `remoteControl/client/list`\n  - `remoteControl/client/revoke`\n- Added picker-oriented protocol types and standard generated schema\nfixtures. The list response intentionally omits backend account id,\nenrollment status, and location fields.\n- Added `app-server-transport/src/transport/remote_control/clients.rs`\nfor environment-scoped GET and DELETE requests. It builds escaped URL\npath segments, forwards optional pagination query fields, sends ChatGPT\nauth plus `chatgpt-account-id`, converts RFC3339 `last_seen_at` values\nto Unix seconds, accepts `204 No Content` revoke responses, and retries\nonce after a `401`.\n- Extracted shared ChatGPT auth loading and recovery into\n`app-server-transport/src/transport/remote_control/auth.rs` so\nwebsocket, pairing, and client management use the same account-auth\nboundary.\n- Retained the configured remote-control base URL on\n`RemoteControlHandle` and resolve management URLs lazily, preserving\ndeferred validation while relay startup is disabled.\n- Registered list as `global_shared_read(\"remote-control-clients\")` and\nrevoke as `global(\"remote-control-clients\")`.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Added transport coverage proving list and revoke work while relay\nstate is disabled, IDs are escaped, picker-only fields are returned,\ntimestamps are converted, revoke accepts `204`, auth headers are\nforwarded, `401` retries exactly once, `403` is not retried, and\nmalformed list payloads retain decode context.\n- Added an app-server integration test proving both JSON-RPC methods\nwork before relay enablement and successful revoke returns `{}`.\n- Regenerated and validated experimental and standard app-server schema\nfixtures.","verified_at":"2026-06-03T00:01:03Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/98a62a62ce7e1e6e6100c6e888e9d2bd794378e2","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/98a62a62ce7e1e6e6100c6e888e9d2bd794378e2","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/98a62a62ce7e1e6e6100c6e888e9d2bd794378e2/comments","author":{"login":"apanasenko-oai","id":228802911,"node_id":"U_kgDODaNBXw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228802911?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/apanasenko-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/apanasenko-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apanasenko-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apanasenko-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apanasenko-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apanasenko-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apanasenko-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apanasenko-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apanasenko-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apanasenko-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apanasenko-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"1fd2a6d328017c58f4863b76f430d4000cbfd1b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/1fd2a6d328017c58f4863b76f430d4000cbfd1b5","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/1fd2a6d328017c58f4863b76f430d4000cbfd1b5"}]},{"sha":"1fd2a6d328017c58f4863b76f430d4000cbfd1b5","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDFmZDJhNmQzMjgwMTdjNThmNDg2M2I3NmY0MzBkNDAwMGNiZmQxYjU","commit":{"author":{"name":"joeflorencio-openai","email":"joeflorencio@openai.com","date":"2026-06-02T23:41:48Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-02T23:41:48Z"},"message":"Allow EDU accounts to fetch cloud config bundles (#25963)\n\n## Summary\n\nAllow EDU ChatGPT workspaces to fetch cloud config bundles. The existing\ncloud config eligibility gate only allowed business-like and enterprise\nplans, which meant EDU admins could configure managed policies in the UI\nbut the Codex client would skip fetching them.\n\nThis keeps individual/pro and team-like usage-based plans excluded, and\nadds service-level coverage for both `edu` and `education` plan aliases.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just fmt`\n- `just test -p codex-cloud-config`\n- Built the Codex app locally, created a new EDU ChatGPT workspace, and\nverified config bundles can be fetched and are properly applied.","tree":{"sha":"1f653bf9411872514dad303f759d225f17e7e7e8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/1f653bf9411872514dad303f759d225f17e7e7e8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/1fd2a6d328017c58f4863b76f430d4000cbfd1b5","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqH2o8CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAANwwQABXc5zt70QD3Jrke7ClOVCDX\nVRFxAn7/zH+1HcOVAp9YXK4eHk1tiWuWB4WPojwmbd56D937mqBq2MiYkKTSDqvw\nZstpCVKSutyIKcdCLcH+UDDx55rXSfPlSEtMmai2gu9rTWVJvbKEazanbT4v0rDT\nQzsC0BTDCTotP87Uw4+T3Y3sCDqWpBQCuFBblGX5Cz+LWbvYfKLS4GagJwgqG/ig\n6NGFn6AFJWOi2jB0+GNcqTwBVxKzjS5LbkmunuZeAmJcb51IxxqvMelSvyfRMIS4\nj3pFHTGfYd3zAc7fwzVc/s98zTkCsMcCzfDB+Z5cJ3eUMiabFs9STb+GUVPTOKPm\n+IQ+3UMsLylY826WndrUW9DCK85b3i/MXC02Z1rvz2hyqmkH47RznwY0iphbIEqK\nppcKOn3AwX+djrI4xsFq1J+/tG1nIbFx7iPynLTSEVxWV+6PD17hNFtwXFhBCZVG\noXKMTZI3XOwDXFJBWkfYsffZ3ySuhzOD201ZH2E5VCdf0wHyY2KCf3vuxe9X4iuv\nt1Q035ePw0BEv4uHElWYWIRRRRBadmci5QmAhKk97saCfNwPvw8AekAcMJRBrq3w\nzE7lXTl//S6UM7BoXYxrWx0FexIzCYQIq4bEaE+xVfgbkaOD9jAE3rCTykWRMGo0\nZEsPrXL3L9KCU688Rel1\n=184T\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 1f653bf9411872514dad303f759d225f17e7e7e8\nparent 271d5cecf2e71f9ea171653306cc9ce7c6ec3f19\nauthor joeflorencio-openai <joeflorencio@openai.com> 1780443708 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780443708 -0700\n\nAllow EDU accounts to fetch cloud config bundles (#25963)\n\n## Summary\n\nAllow EDU ChatGPT workspaces to fetch cloud config bundles. The existing\ncloud config eligibility gate only allowed business-like and enterprise\nplans, which meant EDU admins could configure managed policies in the UI\nbut the Codex client would skip fetching them.\n\nThis keeps individual/pro and team-like usage-based plans excluded, and\nadds service-level coverage for both `edu` and `education` plan aliases.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just fmt`\n- `just test -p codex-cloud-config`\n- Built the Codex app locally, created a new EDU ChatGPT workspace, and\nverified config bundles can be fetched and are properly applied.","verified_at":"2026-06-02T23:41:48Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/1fd2a6d328017c58f4863b76f430d4000cbfd1b5","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/1fd2a6d328017c58f4863b76f430d4000cbfd1b5","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/1fd2a6d328017c58f4863b76f430d4000cbfd1b5/comments","author":{"login":"joeflorencio-openai","id":195963627,"node_id":"U_kgDOC64q6w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/195963627?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/joeflorencio-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"271d5cecf2e71f9ea171653306cc9ce7c6ec3f19","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/271d5cecf2e71f9ea171653306cc9ce7c6ec3f19","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/271d5cecf2e71f9ea171653306cc9ce7c6ec3f19"}]},{"sha":"271d5cecf2e71f9ea171653306cc9ce7c6ec3f19","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDI3MWQ1Y2VjZjJlNzFmOWVhMTcxNjUzMzA2Y2M5Y2U3YzZlYzNmMTk","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-02T23:33:31Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-02T23:33:31Z"},"message":"feat: add extension turn-input contributors (#25959)\n\n## Disclaimer\nDo not use for now\n\n## Why\n\nExtensions can already contribute prompt fragments and request same-turn\nitem injection, but there was no host-owned hook for contributing\nstructured `ResponseItem`s while Codex is assembling a new turn's\ninitial model input. This change adds that seam so extensions can attach\nturn-local input that depends on the submitted user input and resolved\nturn environments without routing through prompt text or late injection.\n\n## What changed\n\n- add `TurnInputContributor` to `codex_extension_api` and export the new\n`TurnInputContext` / `TurnInputEnvironment` types it receives\n- teach `ExtensionRegistry` to register and expose turn-input\ncontributors alongside the existing extension hooks\n- call registered turn-input contributors from\n`core/src/session/turn.rs` while building the initial injected input for\na turn, then append their returned `ResponseItem`s after the skill and\nplugin injections","tree":{"sha":"ec0c0f1f9cf71cca6e0d65f4df759f69c49b7f47","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/ec0c0f1f9cf71cca6e0d65f4df759f69c49b7f47"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/271d5cecf2e71f9ea171653306cc9ce7c6ec3f19","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqH2hLCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAhg0QAGSXLdjEz2iCOtwhv8vrj3rU\nCyVi2Wd15uI5eK4Z0D4JQIR17uOgXEgxY/zBcMff9DE3vVPwBhyAemjyAbe4NhV0\npQQyNVMiE4QN5lRqtqQKNo2wzsgeGpK6l1W8sG9Ryzbl6FWhDn/uQft9yyg2t2qJ\n7QSGuBITKqK/IZ5xncwpwfIf1KGOLqgoOHc/WaFa9XWZGG5x8/jIi+IMrQmSBQQW\n4aFPunVl5NDxHGds+YpQCtJFRedyw5TqNk6nJzDyyd0R6o2ok2oTMl5hL6E+ZXH4\nY2hZl8CX2QTqxtOgjuUppN0exQ/k6FMmXPtI253fn/fSrNAruDHY+9Jlc02cKv4z\nkSKPKjq1okEKVsTiPDJT+x+vo5juFJSHhoFSRA99jlvZi5Ihbc5mgJwSuVjXFNc4\nPW24ebrzaHPcU5TWM2CqMconTDy6mXUR0Eub7lq5ssGd+WjuXmqVQyYeXoJLbK7I\nLx041AlYb3D9ifEa7ygQeQSSx2AJ77HzguQNIMvBtXzkOFFN0IDCkTRjwbMZ9HF0\n30IusZZPqJSUmzos8rxJ6MrJjVjDNFha0HjBEz5gZLqNwXJ51Ft6IQq6hUqZimzs\nOjjjCEzHTbsbRaBFvsm0xbctN6Z33aMvyv1YmXmAJkslnwE6ZkwROqNcFoNt1xGV\n7s4c7/AJWIosjVbIupTU\n=nk5h\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree ec0c0f1f9cf71cca6e0d65f4df759f69c49b7f47\nparent a28b32a8357b4bd67aa3ade5bb9a4e2ddb5cae1a\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1780443211 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780443211 +0200\n\nfeat: add extension turn-input contributors (#25959)\n\n## Disclaimer\nDo not use for now\n\n## Why\n\nExtensions can already contribute prompt fragments and request same-turn\nitem injection, but there was no host-owned hook for contributing\nstructured `ResponseItem`s while Codex is assembling a new turn's\ninitial model input. This change adds that seam so extensions can attach\nturn-local input that depends on the submitted user input and resolved\nturn environments without routing through prompt text or late injection.\n\n## What changed\n\n- add `TurnInputContributor` to `codex_extension_api` and export the new\n`TurnInputContext` / `TurnInputEnvironment` types it receives\n- teach `ExtensionRegistry` to register and expose turn-input\ncontributors alongside the existing extension hooks\n- call registered turn-input contributors from\n`core/src/session/turn.rs` while building the initial injected input for\na turn, then append their returned `ResponseItem`s after the skill and\nplugin injections","verified_at":"2026-06-02T23:33:32Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/271d5cecf2e71f9ea171653306cc9ce7c6ec3f19","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/271d5cecf2e71f9ea171653306cc9ce7c6ec3f19","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/271d5cecf2e71f9ea171653306cc9ce7c6ec3f19/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"a28b32a8357b4bd67aa3ade5bb9a4e2ddb5cae1a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a28b32a8357b4bd67aa3ade5bb9a4e2ddb5cae1a","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/a28b32a8357b4bd67aa3ade5bb9a4e2ddb5cae1a"}]},{"sha":"a28b32a8357b4bd67aa3ade5bb9a4e2ddb5cae1a","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGEyOGIzMmE4MzU3YjRiZDY3YWEzYWRlNWJiOWE0ZTJkZGI1Y2FlMWE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Michael Bolin","email":"mbolin@openai.com","date":"2026-06-02T23:26:36Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-02T23:26:36Z"},"message":"config: express implicit sandbox defaults as permission profiles (#25926)\n\n## Why\n\n`PermissionProfile` is becoming the default way to represent Codex\npermissions, but the implicit default behavior should stay the same for\nnow:\n\n- trusted projects use `:workspace`\n- untrusted projects also use `:workspace`\n- roots without a trust decision use `:read-only`\n- unsandboxed Windows falls back to `:read-only`\n\nThis keeps the existing sandbox semantics while making silent config\ndefaults observable as built-in permission profiles instead of treating\nthe legacy `SandboxPolicy` projection as the primary shape.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Refactored legacy sandbox derivation to resolve the configured sandbox\nmode once, then apply the implicit project fallback only when no sandbox\nmode was configured.\n- Preserved the existing trust-decision fallback: trusted and untrusted\nprojects default to workspace-write where supported.\n- Added empty-config coverage asserting that an untrusted project\nresolves to the built-in active permission profile (`:workspace` outside\nunsandboxed Windows).\n\n## Verification\n\n- `just fmt`\n- `just test -p codex-core 'config::'`\n- `just test -p codex-config`\n\n---\n[//]: # (BEGIN SAPLING FOOTER)\nStack created with [Sapling](https://sapling-scm.com). Best reviewed\nwith [ReviewStack](https://reviewstack.dev/openai/codex/pull/25926).\n* __->__ #25926","tree":{"sha":"4cf9c4df493f6fda04352f9bc4964acf3985b758","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/4cf9c4df493f6fda04352f9bc4964acf3985b758"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/a28b32a8357b4bd67aa3ade5bb9a4e2ddb5cae1a","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqH2asCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAF1MQAItQatxVets+PXhHujBJTIJt\nZGOBDA6pkvjH4eXoX/GHKuCjGlB9Z2q250aUfDNxc8v2G2ZBJT2b0xqCvoLkHvXj\n2xIT0PVFYoLpJUeaA0k219sYbuNwN/NuerViprnNI34kbhcCvA2Hq0+g0S6ufixG\ngUPPzviPNJ6LwOU33SEu25lpwqwS52I1roKWdaxPV09rOj/VDh9gO8IxE/QMumVI\njmgd3UiJawBoWk516LR7EQZ32QFuVnI6EuIR9sxu8dCzcnim1/Kt16qRKgVQPmNj\nSU3vQtkXLXqbI9niMVj1BW6cxoM5EZrzSFHi+y5FY1tAZ0LX8lKx+p59jxhoMc1r\nTl37dtU6ig4KD98LBoQ4vJK5uTUqB2yQjN4xSgBE9Q3jRRBnha7DCsmn+aozqaUS\nfHt+qc6bqOQ8psRGCf4XOen61CFUJ8OemeGE3W/uP+Fo32ex6sOBa2LrVqt/2boO\nbSNwxKm6WdLJwWwsGbvO5he+mjbSt/oORiHN3B/68/u/mb+Nt+YGpeoZYcsDYS/+\n64JITtxP5Kf/l0CPyCWLP72y1vYRrpdEBT1fnWpwrUZ7PIg5nVkeRYGkuM5bVh5Z\nuC3R9o/mfAkx8zJa2vdzu4UN/wWLWfZcyYr9Qktppg+hcBbV1vxd4StwZpCcpdgZ\ndyBC01rQBK8affnunDox\n=Burx\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 4cf9c4df493f6fda04352f9bc4964acf3985b758\nparent 6471f8b31aba50c87d5616cc0a203160a80b5322\nauthor Michael Bolin <mbolin@openai.com> 1780442796 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780442796 -0700\n\nconfig: express implicit sandbox defaults as permission profiles (#25926)\n\n## Why\n\n`PermissionProfile` is becoming the default way to represent Codex\npermissions, but the implicit default behavior should stay the same for\nnow:\n\n- trusted projects use `:workspace`\n- untrusted projects also use `:workspace`\n- roots without a trust decision use `:read-only`\n- unsandboxed Windows falls back to `:read-only`\n\nThis keeps the existing sandbox semantics while making silent config\ndefaults observable as built-in permission profiles instead of treating\nthe legacy `SandboxPolicy` projection as the primary shape.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Refactored legacy sandbox derivation to resolve the configured sandbox\nmode once, then apply the implicit project fallback only when no sandbox\nmode was configured.\n- Preserved the existing trust-decision fallback: trusted and untrusted\nprojects default to workspace-write where supported.\n- Added empty-config coverage asserting that an untrusted project\nresolves to the built-in active permission profile (`:workspace` outside\nunsandboxed Windows).\n\n## Verification\n\n- `just fmt`\n- `just test -p codex-core 'config::'`\n- `just test -p codex-config`\n\n---\n[//]: # (BEGIN SAPLING FOOTER)\nStack created with [Sapling](https://sapling-scm.com). Best reviewed\nwith [ReviewStack](https://reviewstack.dev/openai/codex/pull/25926).\n* __->__ #25926","verified_at":"2026-06-02T23:26:36Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a28b32a8357b4bd67aa3ade5bb9a4e2ddb5cae1a","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/a28b32a8357b4bd67aa3ade5bb9a4e2ddb5cae1a","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a28b32a8357b4bd67aa3ade5bb9a4e2ddb5cae1a/comments","author":{"login":"bolinfest","id":655869,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTg2OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/655869?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest","html_url":"https://github.com/bolinfest","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"6471f8b31aba50c87d5616cc0a203160a80b5322","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6471f8b31aba50c87d5616cc0a203160a80b5322","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/6471f8b31aba50c87d5616cc0a203160a80b5322"}]},{"sha":"6471f8b31aba50c87d5616cc0a203160a80b5322","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDY0NzFmOGIzMWFiYTUwYzg3ZDU2MTZjYzBhMjAzMTYwYTgwYjUzMjI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Adam Perry @ OpenAI","email":"anp@openai.com","date":"2026-06-02T23:22:32Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-02T23:22:32Z"},"message":"[codex] Fix Windows BuildBuddy Bazel wrapper execution (#25915)\n\n## Why\n\n#25156 moved Bazel CI launches into a shared Python wrapper. On Windows,\nlaunching Bazel with `os.execvp` can split the spaced\n`--test_env=PATH=...` argument and fail to propagate the eventual Bazel\nexit status, allowing jobs to pass without running tests. This reapplies\nthe wrapper after #25909 with a Windows-safe launch path.\n\n## What changed\n\nUse a waited `subprocess.run` launch on Windows while preserving\n`os.execvp` on Unix. Add a process-level regression test for spaced\narguments and child exit status, and run it on Windows Bazel shard 1.\n\n## Experiment\n\nTo confirm Bazel was actually invoking tests, patch `87b61d0be6`\ntemporarily added an intentionally failing `codex-core` unit test. Bazel\nfailed on that sentinel on all three major platforms:\n\n- [Linux Bazel\ntest](https://github.com/openai/codex/actions/runs/26841132773/job/79151062486)\n- [macOS Bazel\ntest](https://github.com/openai/codex/actions/runs/26841132773/job/79151062362)\n- [Windows Bazel test shard\n1/4](https://github.com/openai/codex/actions/runs/26841132773/job/79151062155)\n\nThe sentinel was removed after collecting this evidence. Windows Bazel\n[clippy](https://github.com/openai/codex/actions/runs/26841132773/job/79151062914)\nand [release\nverification](https://github.com/openai/codex/actions/runs/26841132773/job/79151062739)\nalso passed.\n\n## Validation\n\nAfter removing the sentinel, `just test -p codex-core` no longer\nreported it. The local run retained two unrelated environment-specific\nfailures.","tree":{"sha":"2d25cd88e6551089a64fbfb284a0d4165a0e170a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/2d25cd88e6551089a64fbfb284a0d4165a0e170a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/6471f8b31aba50c87d5616cc0a203160a80b5322","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqH2W4CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAem4QAEI5vn5pjxfUukUgREZzYbV3\n0uVzDO0U/0ZwFTfRfvNtxK8cfw9Et3habBqCiZ0LOMDLONjV9K+UPuoXcCPrYpiu\njsznNoIdGUkjbK5pnYMAEqSn5an0BEvUUrHDs7dvoNhLwNvzM/wBbLA8y0prqH0P\nIr9xNaCJlgUE/qqQdscQLGNl+rpQWUwroOo65yKz5TT+oi/dUYS1hGOElPzbqJgR\nwo38AZgK4ZdOORmKKS2BL3R2R2UN7xmlDth4szfOCTdr+Rj70rmEguiADxX3X6wb\nqn0Tcc5NjBBZaML5N5myzkQNN82LB4VciNxGBJAaNef8YNyaLVg44yc/tCIxg2sx\nPGhWL3AqazKZIZnKY79hTnUZNcEf1wiByM9F2cBKJJLWM0B7JC54oWe4PBECshAx\n81Jzk+stAgNNXgs8Wq3Owrb+hRfWAZaGcmxqTMCHDgRF26bhoEA+YRdiTew34a6a\nvTUFWqtTC1SfaHxbX72fJsprhoBcT0dTcD2RPIkMNdOdM65ClOqyGjTxjPsyDPMo\nPT6YpquJ2tRdhnEhFd7+2aiEk8eBGhNZCHJYRcE+9uc5p+i/7aFPsONGrZ2kOjSX\nvU/PI+gQoVfyo9a9QogclEEOrG6NTJzbxGycxnO72r4hsu9myHc8mJiW7EA3G0Zp\nO1K5pmj7cDtBXqYNILS1\n=UiZ8\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 2d25cd88e6551089a64fbfb284a0d4165a0e170a\nparent 2d385e166c2dff131ca21294216ce61eb62fd3c2\nauthor Adam Perry @ OpenAI <anp@openai.com> 1780442552 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780442552 -0700\n\n[codex] Fix Windows BuildBuddy Bazel wrapper execution (#25915)\n\n## Why\n\n#25156 moved Bazel CI launches into a shared Python wrapper. On Windows,\nlaunching Bazel with `os.execvp` can split the spaced\n`--test_env=PATH=...` argument and fail to propagate the eventual Bazel\nexit status, allowing jobs to pass without running tests. This reapplies\nthe wrapper after #25909 with a Windows-safe launch path.\n\n## What changed\n\nUse a waited `subprocess.run` launch on Windows while preserving\n`os.execvp` on Unix. Add a process-level regression test for spaced\narguments and child exit status, and run it on Windows Bazel shard 1.\n\n## Experiment\n\nTo confirm Bazel was actually invoking tests, patch `87b61d0be6`\ntemporarily added an intentionally failing `codex-core` unit test. Bazel\nfailed on that sentinel on all three major platforms:\n\n- [Linux Bazel\ntest](https://github.com/openai/codex/actions/runs/26841132773/job/79151062486)\n- [macOS Bazel\ntest](https://github.com/openai/codex/actions/runs/26841132773/job/79151062362)\n- [Windows Bazel test shard\n1/4](https://github.com/openai/codex/actions/runs/26841132773/job/79151062155)\n\nThe sentinel was removed after collecting this evidence. Windows Bazel\n[clippy](https://github.com/openai/codex/actions/runs/26841132773/job/79151062914)\nand [release\nverification](https://github.com/openai/codex/actions/runs/26841132773/job/79151062739)\nalso passed.\n\n## Validation\n\nAfter removing the sentinel, `just test -p codex-core` no longer\nreported it. The local run retained two unrelated environment-specific\nfailures.","verified_at":"2026-06-02T23:22:32Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6471f8b31aba50c87d5616cc0a203160a80b5322","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/6471f8b31aba50c87d5616cc0a203160a80b5322","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6471f8b31aba50c87d5616cc0a203160a80b5322/comments","author":{"login":"anp-oai","id":286154589,"node_id":"U_kgDOEQ5fXQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/286154589?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/anp-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"2d385e166c2dff131ca21294216ce61eb62fd3c2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/2d385e166c2dff131ca21294216ce61eb62fd3c2","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/2d385e166c2dff131ca21294216ce61eb62fd3c2"}]},{"sha":"2d385e166c2dff131ca21294216ce61eb62fd3c2","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDJkMzg1ZTE2NmMyZGZmMTMxY2EyMTI5NDIxNmNlNjFlYjYyZmQzYzI","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-02T23:10:26Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-02T23:10:26Z"},"message":"feat: add skills extension scaffold (#25953)\n\n## Disclaimer\nThis is only here for iteration purpose! Do not make any code rely on\nthis\n\n## Why\n\nSkills still live behind `codex-core` discovery and injection paths, but\nthe extension system needs an authority-aware home before that logic can\nmove. This adds that boundary without changing current skills behavior,\nand keeps host, executor, and remote skills distinct so future\nlist/read/search flows do not collapse back to ambient local paths.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Add the `codex-skills-extension` workspace/Bazel crate under\n`ext/skills`.\n- Define the initial catalog, authority, provider, and turn-state types\nfor authority-bound skill packages and resources.\n- Register placeholder thread/config/prompt/turn lifecycle contributors\nplus host, executor, and remote provider aggregation points.\n- Capture the remaining extraction work as TODOs, including the missing\nextension API hooks needed for per-turn catalog construction and typed\nskill injection.\n- Keep plugins outside the runtime skills model: plugin-installed skills\nare treated as materialized host-owned skill sources once available.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Not run locally.","tree":{"sha":"f52d2e7d33a8768405170ba07c72218bf4b4c327","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/f52d2e7d33a8768405170ba07c72218bf4b4c327"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/2d385e166c2dff131ca21294216ce61eb62fd3c2","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqH2LiCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAKBgQAJjM47Wrct0JEFXfNNaHdrR9\n5QUTu+UO/nimTC4Kt7nSQW84DD2H5qFHbEE7uACtzmz3FrD0OMUTjGpZJBjCBfex\nlYAHUiBCqZFYtPuD/gla0lG4RSCfTvUmSzCDTWm8kg7xnpU/F+gXGs+cZu+KTG8T\nAvefaPCfVbXqNCiYWVafA9MEez+M47708QIFB9VZXmPQ7E3nlVThv11yRwznWsIj\n+MiUY7wGrwSbIsXIJjALartnoJCQ2lImjdOs0iIxES9GZBE+d8hBXrwlKBVLZwmc\nm/ewGpA5rPwH7AEhiM3J9PT5T6mDVB93IlnkrA1KKdb7g8u14GMacv0c3AQxFx+G\nl30mkABRV25608fo31FXj7TY0wx8NESDO73ZExCLKo7YrF5fBr0Z/T/JcL1WSosG\nRMcoTWfkIKmAC7EEt/hW+87BdifxxNOZotSa6EnY3g8u2QojbentaBiO5qTppbDm\nmcyfQnMNG8jpXNsy+ZxiBmSe+Nu6DzxQ1Lc2TYv6Q6CyRfar0u54baSe1SnTPJcc\nR+DoT6YhiNoiJYXSA/S2QReiRihnFI7Lf5c1i06SUVVbS9G9TB8Es4X2C6jjHTZ1\nBQVKnHgOTP33bxB0d0x6zIMJjJ790IQh8/pP48KK5ZcdlRZx1VuzJYtSUcaY/wjy\nVFN4XAjpXKw1MT/Npilo\n=LE97\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree f52d2e7d33a8768405170ba07c72218bf4b4c327\nparent 34dc08c21429c613611f661e1ad160d4fbf7e5ec\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1780441826 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780441826 +0200\n\nfeat: add skills extension scaffold (#25953)\n\n## Disclaimer\nThis is only here for iteration purpose! Do not make any code rely on\nthis\n\n## Why\n\nSkills still live behind `codex-core` discovery and injection paths, but\nthe extension system needs an authority-aware home before that logic can\nmove. This adds that boundary without changing current skills behavior,\nand keeps host, executor, and remote skills distinct so future\nlist/read/search flows do not collapse back to ambient local paths.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Add the `codex-skills-extension` workspace/Bazel crate under\n`ext/skills`.\n- Define the initial catalog, authority, provider, and turn-state types\nfor authority-bound skill packages and resources.\n- Register placeholder thread/config/prompt/turn lifecycle contributors\nplus host, executor, and remote provider aggregation points.\n- Capture the remaining extraction work as TODOs, including the missing\nextension API hooks needed for per-turn catalog construction and typed\nskill injection.\n- Keep plugins outside the runtime skills model: plugin-installed skills\nare treated as materialized host-owned skill sources once available.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Not run locally.","verified_at":"2026-06-02T23:10:27Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/2d385e166c2dff131ca21294216ce61eb62fd3c2","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/2d385e166c2dff131ca21294216ce61eb62fd3c2","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/2d385e166c2dff131ca21294216ce61eb62fd3c2/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"34dc08c21429c613611f661e1ad160d4fbf7e5ec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/34dc08c21429c613611f661e1ad160d4fbf7e5ec","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/34dc08c21429c613611f661e1ad160d4fbf7e5ec"}]},{"sha":"34dc08c21429c613611f661e1ad160d4fbf7e5ec","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDM0ZGMwOGMyMTQyOWM2MTM2MTFmNjYxZTFhZDE2MGQ0ZmJmN2U1ZWM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Ahmed Ibrahim","email":"aibrahim@openai.com","date":"2026-06-02T22:41:53Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-02T22:41:53Z"},"message":"[codex] Publish Python runtime wheels with Python SDK releases (#25906)\n\n## Summary\n- stop publishing Python runtime wheels as a side effect of Rust\nreleases\n- publish runtime wheels from the Python SDK release workflow, either\nexplicitly before updating the SDK pin or immediately before a\n`python-v*` SDK release\n- resolve the runtime release from the requested version or the SDK\npackage's exact `openai-codex-cli-bin` pin\n- build two musllinux-tagged wheels from the Rust-release Linux package\narchives alongside the six existing runtime wheels\n- validate SDK beta tags before any PyPI write\n\n## Release configuration\n- update the `openai-codex-cli-bin` PyPI trusted publisher to trust\n`.github/workflows/python-sdk-release.yml` and the\n`publish-python-runtime` job\n\n## Pin update flow\n- run the `python-sdk-release` workflow manually with the new runtime\nversion before opening or updating the SDK pin PR\n- after the pin lands, a `python-v*` SDK tag republishes with\n`skip-existing: true` before publishing the SDK package\n\n## Validation\n- ran `just fmt`\n- validated the edited workflow YAML\n- validated the embedded `publish-python-runtime` Bash with `bash -n`\n- validated manual `0.136.0 -> rust-v0.136.0` mapping\n- validated tag-driven `python-v0.1.0b3 -> 0.132.0 -> rust-v0.132.0`\nmapping\n- validated rejection of an invalid SDK tag before publication\n- confirmed `rust-v0.136.0` contains the two required Linux package\narchives\n- CI will provide the full test signal","tree":{"sha":"f7c3b60de5ef226f15ffca956d01e4d274861386","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/f7c3b60de5ef226f15ffca956d01e4d274861386"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/34dc08c21429c613611f661e1ad160d4fbf7e5ec","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqH1wxCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAYDoQAIlktr8ztNQsre+9KwqobKz2\ntytDMrXiGQJ3SwEEe0TgBHz6dOCbCiJRJvJ8wDm9NX//7v40nlsL3tKWzmNUTW1Q\nDE5ByJU0BeyUKnk1hKx4L3FCGlcdfV3sH/LrLBFVL7sr8DuFNLVcE4gfcJIAhjNf\nywaSeZ4cske6rombWSASGobS5mPJk4FpWZpJG4UVGT+R/3Ddv6FKdmkr+Pxv5ZTJ\nS78n49URw1zyv3wjPV8PmqYBlVmI8HMUp8WssoR2iErx4b6uRXsCMoGEsYtIauwS\nq+1/HADHwamAlMT9srjJRSZ+sMkJJWCGYWW6zfkcep5wwybNI4OyjEwG/CLKTren\noDv09kVezqfRp2l3annE3tmuZ5eCpK5DKYggwdjBtZGd2NeBEeWLrJ+kcyzWdAyo\nrMlXup1rmMMbV+D8NzseAPdqkkglSscl2e01qoNKxMxknnSihGK6JtaHhe6uvwpv\n+e/33xVtL9IEY5S5998SrizMQwTv63nEMHBplECrYHMKMqj2rwaGyxMBAvgx2nls\neoVEtec/+lF9ASXTjGhItgCoCn+nqKcWocLmkMX/3Z9YcjBLP5fyC+VyFXO+THNL\n9+2yZS42L+CPn2kAj2hjzeXrAw5Nsj1q6nYngpLpioKseDf4WjpCvzngZQ2qSy5d\nvttthueU5WgLB7Zf/GQn\n=kkym\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree f7c3b60de5ef226f15ffca956d01e4d274861386\nparent bec21c71142ed44d8eb7d7ca5719c87d961044d0\nauthor Ahmed Ibrahim <aibrahim@openai.com> 1780440113 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780440113 -0700\n\n[codex] Publish Python runtime wheels with Python SDK releases (#25906)\n\n## Summary\n- stop publishing Python runtime wheels as a side effect of Rust\nreleases\n- publish runtime wheels from the Python SDK release workflow, either\nexplicitly before updating the SDK pin or immediately before a\n`python-v*` SDK release\n- resolve the runtime release from the requested version or the SDK\npackage's exact `openai-codex-cli-bin` pin\n- build two musllinux-tagged wheels from the Rust-release Linux package\narchives alongside the six existing runtime wheels\n- validate SDK beta tags before any PyPI write\n\n## Release configuration\n- update the `openai-codex-cli-bin` PyPI trusted publisher to trust\n`.github/workflows/python-sdk-release.yml` and the\n`publish-python-runtime` job\n\n## Pin update flow\n- run the `python-sdk-release` workflow manually with the new runtime\nversion before opening or updating the SDK pin PR\n- after the pin lands, a `python-v*` SDK tag republishes with\n`skip-existing: true` before publishing the SDK package\n\n## Validation\n- ran `just fmt`\n- validated the edited workflow YAML\n- validated the embedded `publish-python-runtime` Bash with `bash -n`\n- validated manual `0.136.0 -> rust-v0.136.0` mapping\n- validated tag-driven `python-v0.1.0b3 -> 0.132.0 -> rust-v0.132.0`\nmapping\n- validated rejection of an invalid SDK tag before publication\n- confirmed `rust-v0.136.0` contains the two required Linux package\narchives\n- CI will provide the full test signal","verified_at":"2026-06-02T22:41:54Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/34dc08c21429c613611f661e1ad160d4fbf7e5ec","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/34dc08c21429c613611f661e1ad160d4fbf7e5ec","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/34dc08c21429c613611f661e1ad160d4fbf7e5ec/comments","author":{"login":"aibrahim-oai","id":219906144,"node_id":"U_kgDODRuAYA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/219906144?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/aibrahim-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"bec21c71142ed44d8eb7d7ca5719c87d961044d0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/bec21c71142ed44d8eb7d7ca5719c87d961044d0","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/bec21c71142ed44d8eb7d7ca5719c87d961044d0"}]},{"sha":"bec21c71142ed44d8eb7d7ca5719c87d961044d0","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGJlYzIxYzcxMTQyZWQ0NGQ4ZWI3ZDdjYTU3MTljODdkOTYxMDQ0ZDA","commit":{"author":{"name":"Won Park","email":"won@openai.com","date":"2026-06-02T22:27:52Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-02T22:27:52Z"},"message":"Expose standalone image generation in code mode (#25923)\n\n## Why\n\nStandalone image generation remained top-level-only in code-mode\nsessions.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Change imagegen exposure from `DirectModelOnly` to `Direct`.\n- Keep direct-mode access while enabling nested code-mode access.\n- Add a focused regression test for the exposure contract.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-image-generation-extension`","tree":{"sha":"5dd282d1c16e95f1ba5ce8622d206f93d6b51ae1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/5dd282d1c16e95f1ba5ce8622d206f93d6b51ae1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/bec21c71142ed44d8eb7d7ca5719c87d961044d0","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqH1joCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA0Q8QAD4bx42LHZ1MhJuNT3vJgMi5\n81bjkOu2I62debHlnBdxafQ7PJ6JKuMjkeql5ChdAJz2tqVvCx1/9o7rk21WUIMo\nkkujJj4ONRa9vBE1GUVSGlyvoGmwrA1sPor5/ib691L3t0Rpr/K6QXWTmzPo9nA+\nKB57L223lLKtc4oi0VHqIb69xxOZLN1UWHJWFik4euVBGQReH4gNodeUMXKxBmJU\ncRywCpxbXJIrgvQcbw+ZnOdQf9y58kN1LE5atX/UuagP9PaOGVQ4eqT0l1tGqhaM\nwDIqTrVeuOpz84Gn1kyw/1P54vzq0UdZN8xomeKhduBm5NyRV0eU2aPSth1Tg6uH\nhzBNYexNQJM3IXHAoe1qyKqA48NQwcIJ2PMCHbvcCKvrf/EqJ3rZB6ODoyG9MXwf\nLEBg6uLoqcvwSP0h9YF1ZxvmUMfjHY1eUypSXmA8cV7KUi4h3ceDYN98Fs+Xkhuy\nmFHZ6kkPD1f0kZK6nkdjGAeUo/Ll/rQ0efS9KMkrfo/z0Emf3oiKBZx7w2H7Jnj9\nQQfvFAJI9q4xklQ6N9JVcu2hyMlw4PHTZBdozOk8maif7azbix0wiYt4rPmQNOPe\nNs02UPs9OGuez6txzF5sVivwbmfP3dO+lyKjMSGF7l5J4D9Ca/1J9RneVUojJfr5\n8ojrcddcklnQQgTw032B\n=5TmO\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 5dd282d1c16e95f1ba5ce8622d206f93d6b51ae1\nparent f752b25fc43d5e79a4f1cd1878a51702e7fea977\nauthor Won Park <won@openai.com> 1780439272 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780439272 +0000\n\nExpose standalone image generation in code mode (#25923)\n\n## Why\n\nStandalone image generation remained top-level-only in code-mode\nsessions.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Change imagegen exposure from `DirectModelOnly` to `Direct`.\n- Keep direct-mode access while enabling nested code-mode access.\n- Add a focused regression test for the exposure contract.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-image-generation-extension`","verified_at":"2026-06-02T22:27:52Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/bec21c71142ed44d8eb7d7ca5719c87d961044d0","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/bec21c71142ed44d8eb7d7ca5719c87d961044d0","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/bec21c71142ed44d8eb7d7ca5719c87d961044d0/comments","author":{"login":"won-openai","id":262224683,"node_id":"U_kgDOD6E7Kw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/262224683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/won-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"f752b25fc43d5e79a4f1cd1878a51702e7fea977","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f752b25fc43d5e79a4f1cd1878a51702e7fea977","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/f752b25fc43d5e79a4f1cd1878a51702e7fea977"}]},{"sha":"f752b25fc43d5e79a4f1cd1878a51702e7fea977","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGY3NTJiMjVmYzQzZDVlNzlhNGYxY2QxODc4YTUxNzAyZTdmZWE5Nzc","commit":{"author":{"name":"Shijie Rao","email":"shijie.rao@openai.com","date":"2026-06-02T22:12:07Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-02T22:12:07Z"},"message":"Revert \"Use environment secrets for Azure signing\" (#25948)\n\nReverts openai/codex#24859","tree":{"sha":"856624c1b85bf03719e647e2515e04c32c8e1a49","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/856624c1b85bf03719e647e2515e04c32c8e1a49"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/f752b25fc43d5e79a4f1cd1878a51702e7fea977","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqH1U3CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAU+MQAIvVSrs2Hlz0S2njnMv4JTxV\nYAJ1Ko0ZT9FTrmfYs2G9a2P4hOg5oLiFQQi52jUZAAxa52yeKYI8I0NCcUjMfRTu\nksCmzNihSIcwVo9OHEUgC2VbfV5MFBKjIIpaKS7cWjIn1D5UkhElhuHyiNbo3U6K\nx2CkJHP5/wRynHvu98ISktkNkb7CYdj4KcpsXlg9tSSvhxayUEf/yPkTM+VtIQM6\nrPehHe6mdH0nLl7f1aNykCr1oeqpGUSn2XNimMgDtl1dok89xm9aedGRMkCqTwUI\nLRBDXNLV1D8sMCUbfVll6jJHiSGlTU3vX6urzZfiQfNn/nyY3NI695OogQOCifbN\nJELDaIL7gRJL/8xPdR9UpkfbE1/eb9D1y+yBMsbtwd8Zfuq4hnbhvi15ArP7so36\nYFfWcggtyyLYg2UIBR3z9N1XnwSA108NBQju1dxOio2ha1lkIBRoAVNJYeI440JK\n6ZGSGizCYXrcMK4YWEO8Tcrw+paYUZSKBljVAWklj3nmzIHT331kIvfm8NrrVNwI\nhnItkYD5xIbprCwcjXphgTZyOQaQHkgunSP5qi85In4aTfIs3qOkzLrcRId0W3v/\nphTQ51sK8+67StDXCZjv2jeqwggMjojfkqvMA3nH9073k0QpEMB1uEnay2nXbpi0\nmCkY7wOsLLEg8DyHk352\n=maTU\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 856624c1b85bf03719e647e2515e04c32c8e1a49\nparent c6d76750e81af8a88dcda078916b4207b354bd83\nauthor Shijie Rao <shijie.rao@openai.com> 1780438327 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780438327 -0700\n\nRevert \"Use environment secrets for Azure signing\" (#25948)\n\nReverts openai/codex#24859","verified_at":"2026-06-02T22:12:08Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f752b25fc43d5e79a4f1cd1878a51702e7fea977","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/f752b25fc43d5e79a4f1cd1878a51702e7fea977","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f752b25fc43d5e79a4f1cd1878a51702e7fea977/comments","author":{"login":"shijie-oai","id":235382242,"node_id":"U_kgDODgel4g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/235382242?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/shijie-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"c6d76750e81af8a88dcda078916b4207b354bd83","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c6d76750e81af8a88dcda078916b4207b354bd83","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/c6d76750e81af8a88dcda078916b4207b354bd83"}]},{"sha":"c6d76750e81af8a88dcda078916b4207b354bd83","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGM2ZDc2NzUwZTgxYWY4YTg4ZGNkYTA3ODkxNmI0MjA3YjM1NGJkODM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Michael Bolin","email":"mbolin@openai.com","date":"2026-06-02T22:05:04Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-02T22:05:04Z"},"message":"config: remove dead profile sandbox fallback (#25943)\n\n## Why\n\n`profile_sandbox_mode` was left over from the old selected legacy\nprofile path. Production now always derives permissions without that\nvalue, and legacy profile contents are ignored, so keeping a parameter\nthat is always `None` makes `derive_permission_profile` look like it\nstill supports a fallback that no longer exists.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Removed the `profile_sandbox_mode` argument from\n`ConfigToml::derive_permission_profile`.\n- Updated the production caller and legacy sandbox-policy test helper to\nmatch.\n- Dropped the stale unselected legacy-profile sandbox test that only\nprotected the removed fallback shape.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `just test -p codex-config`\n- `just test -p codex-core 'config::'`\n\n\n---\n[//]: # (BEGIN SAPLING FOOTER)\nStack created with [Sapling](https://sapling-scm.com). Best reviewed\nwith [ReviewStack](https://reviewstack.dev/openai/codex/pull/25943).\n* #25926\n* __->__ #25943","tree":{"sha":"b0d59003e2099596439fa878991f5eb074d17033","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/b0d59003e2099596439fa878991f5eb074d17033"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/c6d76750e81af8a88dcda078916b4207b354bd83","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqH1OQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAIDQQAKq2jMu+yuTw+RjXyP+XOlL2\nnLWxcBRvdZ4hDIqXW+bzEt24+/IxFYFl1lNMzLhhnQsk4WgmYXs5jO5GViPH843d\n8WxzWxOXapxUXPRuDulkwUYa3s6VXiCKMqTaajqOD52JzDwnzaikYyMNoje1lsAp\ngcjJ+MQ8Lq84eddYp9tSAdir25XsNgGYW7CNFphjYOccCc6JRbXAsxRNzJh4qxEL\n7aYXVaSouFAwPrQ2CIIZOr2u2sSPM5J+WTPyDHZo/XQJyHXFH6Vm7MThb7xLvGPU\nCf0mYKPQFK7wNrEkJ14KbRJmybpFG2g8KBDQNo4mpntSZwTFI+2lLEnf9PR+0KCM\n9++xZb1psYiVzyF7Bc2UfRVCIJI6VRP7obDd6NQeBZxGJZIJ/cqXhArlkfcOr13F\n1AGJKwXULXbhN0Rte2sOd9kwMesgZVFZgEIun0yoK2FJJxNHpPgWhMHImEzKrQt3\no5L801OitM5deunj9zJyjOy0ypp8Jrk4Ce9NlAD/jYaxjBQfsSJPZwQmjXSLR7ut\n6Z99f3FKcoZq6XzMWQTy9w4qckxLMo7c+a30RMjRnPplOzboO8bOqxl8yHOZzpSb\nQO1lbr//HCoqMGQADs4/u82kRyFtlvRaf3UMgmKZ7JACakhIyjQEwv+awqgjmdLT\n/YWJIwnn3INZsQE1nM3O\n=Q3nY\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree b0d59003e2099596439fa878991f5eb074d17033\nparent d55e5a9bde03235fbd796282e839966c5b39ec80\nauthor Michael Bolin <mbolin@openai.com> 1780437904 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780437904 +0000\n\nconfig: remove dead profile sandbox fallback (#25943)\n\n## Why\n\n`profile_sandbox_mode` was left over from the old selected legacy\nprofile path. Production now always derives permissions without that\nvalue, and legacy profile contents are ignored, so keeping a parameter\nthat is always `None` makes `derive_permission_profile` look like it\nstill supports a fallback that no longer exists.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Removed the `profile_sandbox_mode` argument from\n`ConfigToml::derive_permission_profile`.\n- Updated the production caller and legacy sandbox-policy test helper to\nmatch.\n- Dropped the stale unselected legacy-profile sandbox test that only\nprotected the removed fallback shape.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `just test -p codex-config`\n- `just test -p codex-core 'config::'`\n\n\n---\n[//]: # (BEGIN SAPLING FOOTER)\nStack created with [Sapling](https://sapling-scm.com). Best reviewed\nwith [ReviewStack](https://reviewstack.dev/openai/codex/pull/25943).\n* #25926\n* __->__ #25943","verified_at":"2026-06-02T22:05:05Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c6d76750e81af8a88dcda078916b4207b354bd83","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/c6d76750e81af8a88dcda078916b4207b354bd83","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c6d76750e81af8a88dcda078916b4207b354bd83/comments","author":{"login":"bolinfest","id":655869,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTg2OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/655869?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest","html_url":"https://github.com/bolinfest","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"d55e5a9bde03235fbd796282e839966c5b39ec80","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/d55e5a9bde03235fbd796282e839966c5b39ec80","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/d55e5a9bde03235fbd796282e839966c5b39ec80"}]},{"sha":"d55e5a9bde03235fbd796282e839966c5b39ec80","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGQ1NWU1YTliZGUwMzIzNWZiZDc5NjI4MmU4Mzk5NjZjNWIzOWVjODA","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-02T21:55:08Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-02T21:55:08Z"},"message":"Add remote request permissions integration coverage (#25867)\n\n## Stack\n\n1. #25850 - Key request-permission grants by environment: stores and\napplies sticky permission grants per environment id.\n2. #25858 - Add `environmentId` to `request_permissions`: lets the model\ntarget a selected environment and resolves relative permission paths\nagainst it.\n3. #25862 - Propagate permission approval environment id: carries the\nselected environment id through approval events, app-server requests,\nTUI prompts, and delegate forwarding.\n4. This PR (#25867) - Add remote request permissions integration\ncoverage: verifies the selected remote environment across request,\napproval, grant reuse, and exec.\n\nThis PR is stacked on #25862 and should be reviewed after #25850,\n#25858, and #25862.\n\n## Why\n\nThe environment-scoped permission stack needs one end-to-end check that\nexercises the CCA-shaped path, not only unit-level parsing. This\nverifies that a model-sent `environmentId` on `request_permissions`\nreaches the approval event, stores the grant under the selected\nenvironment, and is reused by a later tool call in that same\nenvironment.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Adds a remote executor integration test for `request_permissions` with\n`environmentId: remote` and a relative write root.\n- Asserts the permission event reports the remote environment and cwd,\nand that the normalized grant resolves under the remote cwd.\n- Approves the grant, then runs a remote `exec_command` without explicit\nper-call permissions and verifies it completes without another exec\napproval and writes only in the remote filesystem.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Not run locally per instruction.\n- `git diff --check`","tree":{"sha":"9487f4793dcb308cc89047665b312ca316b1173c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/9487f4793dcb308cc89047665b312ca316b1173c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/d55e5a9bde03235fbd796282e839966c5b39ec80","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqH1E8CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA+9oQAKceRakcH+JT0+oSHH1IR++6\nIsSaw0cmh+rgQVTE1FS4qD7ARGUTpX07Ol+oYYDNGz9CQz5fYCha3ds3vY1q8Kdh\nMZNOZCx/lxCB2gEfFu6NQxpF7aKY/o6AjCQ6LGnc/Cr7qPEe7CjGUmzWscEvYGJf\ncRdq+4LYlUHnlB3Hg0tp3domwhtaxxFd6/sKoM1gb0VECDmj5suz7AqnUb7D942h\neOcNlSuaR1abSNRE+3GBEj71QXR6qCEeYvOqniWUXiyTuGOAS/WKfwIomxT7xACG\n/grMbrWB98qVyS1thiQW7Vq620hnsKrLxeao/zyX9+sovpgQJIF8KzxjDRpUimeh\noMAmUHHqX6jO2ghomkAzW5sQs/yfRx5cINeT7oSPyT6ai9O2FGo8j8Z0qduLXEzu\n2SLomfNwQ0tyMXg8KH2KnAUO2904aZUxR75dwQNb8m9az3Kq/uiIjKueet5MV2FO\n0y3fmK7E+1W4uMKHVff0oQifjADvnnpnGuwOvk4QaLiQL9Nq6bAuVfOoo5mQVvDd\nBR6ei59HaEwfgo6CFkH5aEwEVqezUxfxoR4WZsFnOrnA2cCAVuSWNn/YVDixcguj\nGqRxqq+ZuDAB01F5YVMbYC7uvB6WVwaApz/zNVgm2HFsM0Imj6HccVFPp6bCoOi8\nfLyzMU631WjnMlv566I5\n=3x68\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 9487f4793dcb308cc89047665b312ca316b1173c\nparent 68e2c8ed69ce994a0da02c2dcf8b20a69f43c2b6\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1780437308 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780437308 +0200\n\nAdd remote request permissions integration coverage (#25867)\n\n## Stack\n\n1. #25850 - Key request-permission grants by environment: stores and\napplies sticky permission grants per environment id.\n2. #25858 - Add `environmentId` to `request_permissions`: lets the model\ntarget a selected environment and resolves relative permission paths\nagainst it.\n3. #25862 - Propagate permission approval environment id: carries the\nselected environment id through approval events, app-server requests,\nTUI prompts, and delegate forwarding.\n4. This PR (#25867) - Add remote request permissions integration\ncoverage: verifies the selected remote environment across request,\napproval, grant reuse, and exec.\n\nThis PR is stacked on #25862 and should be reviewed after #25850,\n#25858, and #25862.\n\n## Why\n\nThe environment-scoped permission stack needs one end-to-end check that\nexercises the CCA-shaped path, not only unit-level parsing. This\nverifies that a model-sent `environmentId` on `request_permissions`\nreaches the approval event, stores the grant under the selected\nenvironment, and is reused by a later tool call in that same\nenvironment.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Adds a remote executor integration test for `request_permissions` with\n`environmentId: remote` and a relative write root.\n- Asserts the permission event reports the remote environment and cwd,\nand that the normalized grant resolves under the remote cwd.\n- Approves the grant, then runs a remote `exec_command` without explicit\nper-call permissions and verifies it completes without another exec\napproval and writes only in the remote filesystem.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Not run locally per instruction.\n- `git diff --check`","verified_at":"2026-06-02T21:55:09Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/d55e5a9bde03235fbd796282e839966c5b39ec80","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/d55e5a9bde03235fbd796282e839966c5b39ec80","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/d55e5a9bde03235fbd796282e839966c5b39ec80/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"68e2c8ed69ce994a0da02c2dcf8b20a69f43c2b6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/68e2c8ed69ce994a0da02c2dcf8b20a69f43c2b6","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/68e2c8ed69ce994a0da02c2dcf8b20a69f43c2b6"}]},{"sha":"68e2c8ed69ce994a0da02c2dcf8b20a69f43c2b6","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDY4ZTJjOGVkNjljZTk5NGEwZGEwMmMyZGNmOGIyMGE2OWY0M2MyYjY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Ahmed Ibrahim","email":"aibrahim@openai.com","date":"2026-06-02T21:50:16Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-02T21:50:16Z"},"message":"[codex] Keep hosted tools visible in code-only mode (#25890)\n\n## Why\n\n`code_mode_only` moved ordinary runtime tools behind `exec`, but it also\nhid hosted Responses tools. Hosted `web_search` and `image_generation`\ndo not have a nested `exec` runtime path, so code-only sessions lost\nthose capabilities entirely even when their existing provider, auth,\nmodel, and configuration gates passed.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Keep hosted Responses tools top-level in `code_mode_only` sessions\nafter their existing gates pass.\n- Preserve the existing nested-tool behavior for ordinary runtimes and\nthe direct-only behavior for multi-agent v2 tools.\n- Add planner coverage for `code_mode_only` with default multi-agent v2\nsettings, hosted live web search, and hosted image generation.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Added focused regression coverage in\n`codex-rs/core/src/tools/spec_plan_tests.rs`.\n- Left execution to CI per repository workflow.","tree":{"sha":"b7005c7629ea578d74e6f5540ffa9944514cee37","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/b7005c7629ea578d74e6f5540ffa9944514cee37"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/68e2c8ed69ce994a0da02c2dcf8b20a69f43c2b6","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqH1AYCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAiXQQACXrJGi3tv9cBZmk4RIfpBFs\nQqdWoT4fJeB1WLr5OttlzjtLZiXufWDxMuLzRrhkOQAHC8CZjTNp1JtQ58yktLjh\nOfzTjuPNxLWVbnlr20M3dusTnM6c1rFSX4XHUZIr2oZKko7pDsrYl3XbtUzrCJRw\n+SRYHYkwuF1hTiR3usG5QLXAv6/h7mhNWnBBLenoqjNKS2nggTcIqyz/BgZcpHuq\nJ9iRiuLy/9WlD2dzpWBV4TbQeEq/sm0lNYmWGSd/HcXRJ1eVWMpV7/rHPCZ6myhk\nKR7iv5oMec/I476U0JBPw/M2Mx9HIsSwmG5jtisjkEGVKcjy8vwmHSGLykGAMk+1\nM8RDXHE12jmq0GwhCh0+/S033da72rEpV8oeJYs45Hu4nkm2rGoCzRvT6ELBwW0l\n3GJsJ97huTq09aou4Z5jEduWx1hC0RFhEt3HKgh7kbA5QRl6h8O5pKAQms3fNsll\nYhJoblhb/K8iHOyn+QHshzvazSh5LYoBxYaVzw0O9RkdU65k9z7utmfmz9PN/aHt\nkeB/PROCMAo66YlZMvNLr47eFvYLbJI10pG3QxLR6cYkKbFW+7u84uKpfNSWSl6b\nD/MRO4QegCG/be3no4223Dp9AoGMPbXUeD+vISHtqy8Bh6ZwQOP4+RDTP9zL1Gyz\nzK9mbwkardLPpXBA0X4L\n=3cQS\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree b7005c7629ea578d74e6f5540ffa9944514cee37\nparent e7039f98449d0e39687aab14eda4b4383b3bce31\nauthor Ahmed Ibrahim <aibrahim@openai.com> 1780437016 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780437016 -0700\n\n[codex] Keep hosted tools visible in code-only mode (#25890)\n\n## Why\n\n`code_mode_only` moved ordinary runtime tools behind `exec`, but it also\nhid hosted Responses tools. Hosted `web_search` and `image_generation`\ndo not have a nested `exec` runtime path, so code-only sessions lost\nthose capabilities entirely even when their existing provider, auth,\nmodel, and configuration gates passed.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Keep hosted Responses tools top-level in `code_mode_only` sessions\nafter their existing gates pass.\n- Preserve the existing nested-tool behavior for ordinary runtimes and\nthe direct-only behavior for multi-agent v2 tools.\n- Add planner coverage for `code_mode_only` with default multi-agent v2\nsettings, hosted live web search, and hosted image generation.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Added focused regression coverage in\n`codex-rs/core/src/tools/spec_plan_tests.rs`.\n- Left execution to CI per repository workflow.","verified_at":"2026-06-02T21:50:17Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/68e2c8ed69ce994a0da02c2dcf8b20a69f43c2b6","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/68e2c8ed69ce994a0da02c2dcf8b20a69f43c2b6","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/68e2c8ed69ce994a0da02c2dcf8b20a69f43c2b6/comments","author":{"login":"aibrahim-oai","id":219906144,"node_id":"U_kgDODRuAYA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/219906144?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/aibrahim-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"e7039f98449d0e39687aab14eda4b4383b3bce31","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e7039f98449d0e39687aab14eda4b4383b3bce31","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/e7039f98449d0e39687aab14eda4b4383b3bce31"}]},{"sha":"e7039f98449d0e39687aab14eda4b4383b3bce31","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGU3MDM5Zjk4NDQ5ZDBlMzk2ODdhYWIxNGVkYTRiNDM4M2IzYmNlMzE","commit":{"author":{"name":"joeflorencio-openai","email":"joeflorencio@openai.com","date":"2026-06-02T21:30:12Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-02T21:30:12Z"},"message":"Split cloud config bundle service modules (#25668)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Splits the monolithic `codex-cloud-config` implementation into focused\nmodules.\n- Keeps behavior unchanged from the preceding config bundle runtime\nswitch.\n\n## Details\n\nThis is the reviewability follow-up after the lineage-preserving\nmigration PRs. The split separates backend transport, loader\nconstruction, cache handling, metrics, validation, service\norchestration, and focused tests into named files.\n\nVerification: `just fmt`; `just test -p codex-cloud-config`.","tree":{"sha":"15a4e59811a9d6e22f0f6a1517741cec193d0b0a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/15a4e59811a9d6e22f0f6a1517741cec193d0b0a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/e7039f98449d0e39687aab14eda4b4383b3bce31","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqH0tkCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAYb0QALB87xt3fZkdWn5oGog7MIVv\nr0XFGMWRz29dHQ7SuO3KQYn/USTCgVvFzaMq1dyzYUXj/GTrVXVmo75hA2wbleEW\nK5JiFBc731yayUvUcDuTNFBXm87sBq0n5vxMS+3xViPHoDVIrraFZnoy1zfsjwwI\nO7BEQZE5zJuqhCKxqewniMY52m6WvW3mqSwfqRNyLDYdRMNMtw/GSIDIPi9OKgCV\nWfvgSqDdGBYrIo1Ou8kofaeH3ZXTfgTl04klSooN//dGIejyTQv0W/GC8DHXSI8o\nGZuF7Em6JoJ4j3bwX/dRtYXCHI40+3mi0uj95OyALKU2zHD1Nm0xmo4jDRfU7WfK\nJb3DTJeVFdvEn4iDAt1pdLXDa9vD48hofY2x3nXJh0QWShkL6/KENilAcPc2RMfN\n3LCl37NcoTvS9yNJMRAXRZm7JNCx6hJj0tU9TJJaumJl59aruEeSvneNwUvpX6ch\nrJNMaRRs5W7lw7r83KXS/c08+3jEMkNbXGQYSmJXUpPeEo9ZnmCN9foy4TiPgdZw\n+st48SNxugpoLs5lUwXXP9GF6HJIaKMBBaCzGhI2bhiCbhi/fJ7ixgASmwJ5odBN\nAix9iB2R8rwhr3YroAASqB5oGC1wtVdmhBge3lI9g+K619G9kIgPMEj0KxfYl1BO\nG56yNuhVyaVv1Od9c7He\n=b/TN\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 15a4e59811a9d6e22f0f6a1517741cec193d0b0a\nparent f6d64bd6ab3bf1a9587bbc13a00711029120d3e9\nauthor joeflorencio-openai <joeflorencio@openai.com> 1780435812 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780435812 -0700\n\nSplit cloud config bundle service modules (#25668)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Splits the monolithic `codex-cloud-config` implementation into focused\nmodules.\n- Keeps behavior unchanged from the preceding config bundle runtime\nswitch.\n\n## Details\n\nThis is the reviewability follow-up after the lineage-preserving\nmigration PRs. The split separates backend transport, loader\nconstruction, cache handling, metrics, validation, service\norchestration, and focused tests into named files.\n\nVerification: `just fmt`; `just test -p codex-cloud-config`.","verified_at":"2026-06-02T21:30:13Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e7039f98449d0e39687aab14eda4b4383b3bce31","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/e7039f98449d0e39687aab14eda4b4383b3bce31","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e7039f98449d0e39687aab14eda4b4383b3bce31/comments","author":{"login":"joeflorencio-openai","id":195963627,"node_id":"U_kgDOC64q6w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/195963627?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/joeflorencio-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"f6d64bd6ab3bf1a9587bbc13a00711029120d3e9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f6d64bd6ab3bf1a9587bbc13a00711029120d3e9","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/f6d64bd6ab3bf1a9587bbc13a00711029120d3e9"}]},{"sha":"f6d64bd6ab3bf1a9587bbc13a00711029120d3e9","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGY2ZDY0YmQ2YWIzYmYxYTk1ODdiYmMxM2EwMDcxMTAyOTEyMGQzZTk","commit":{"author":{"name":"Michael Bolin","email":"mbolin@openai.com","date":"2026-06-02T21:16:12Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-02T21:16:12Z"},"message":"core: stop passing legacy SandboxPolicy to guardian reviews (#25911)\n\n## Why\n\nGuardian review turns already submit a read-only `PermissionProfile`,\nwhich is the permissions model the runtime should honor. Passing the\nequivalent legacy `SandboxPolicy` through `ThreadSettingsOverrides`\nkeeps two representations of the same read-only constraint alive on this\npath and makes the guardian flow depend on compatibility plumbing that\nis being phased out.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Set `sandbox_policy` to `None` when the guardian review session\nsubmits its child `Op::UserInput`.\n- Keep `permission_profile: Some(PermissionProfile::read_only())` and\n`approval_policy: Some(AskForApproval::Never)`, so the guardian review\nremains read-only and cannot request approvals.\n- Remove the now-unused `SandboxPolicy` import and redundant comment\nfrom `codex-rs/core/src/guardian/review_session.rs`.\n\n## Verification\n\nNot run locally; this is a narrow cleanup of redundant thread-settings\noverride state.","tree":{"sha":"941f76cbb28bbbf11734d81bb2dd5179404f9b3b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/941f76cbb28bbbf11734d81bb2dd5179404f9b3b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/f6d64bd6ab3bf1a9587bbc13a00711029120d3e9","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqH0gcCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAOU4QAJMkZ/nAhGBU3HEu5Yxs3g1R\nzdcDlumH00YsriK9wZqP9eaKG6WCJ/OStNUvtzbmBaVGwmc7PV3O7J38jLNofYJm\nM1JitPj9UDUekvIEjfHUojClt89kQb19PD5k6VRTqmRLUy3M1aGJNsXkA/PuUb2l\njs0J5vbQhH0DPG1VPxbqEsACDwdcBoo0B80pmlnRs1wlg9pqO105eK5jArlqgfyR\nvgI/P60pH6kqn/G8flfpkqRqVEt5TVicuxKGJ+vbfEvo8qV9ymwLoQfn6kVNxMHm\nylRyj6rVs+Hw8BGcovqk9iLXafN4L/jrMOa08wQiF/k99kCJxNnEIQn08c+DHvWl\nKYrITpOkbJqFpYLJpOVf8dhrO8faE5zBais+ie9nsMaI7gVAvrSEjXH/pfCVcU7M\nGVbC+UT3XjvvUIPnTQJ3DeIm1sMf5SwUe1f4FodCe7eyC2nKeW8e1pCCoWa7DKQq\nA+/iIAuRz9TzIR9IsQuN8F9JDFNhma3Tbp9mheRXVtdWhrfgdxLyNGCCtMfUKge+\nRlb2gB3IDrQrOe94BMjvdHzf9pGnAVTeOL9z/DLK2tebX17pPVmC1m+5N2kiLm0x\nxaUaTcrzxvzTY+kp8mWbJL0aZUtcu+Xvxdve3EF0xtMiXg+REr2qS+XVxWYtU+0i\n1E22pUgfyvc5xV/k9ntB\n=nvsu\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 941f76cbb28bbbf11734d81bb2dd5179404f9b3b\nparent c74be11672cdf90cda60869961075965b02f213a\nauthor Michael Bolin <mbolin@openai.com> 1780434972 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780434972 -0700\n\ncore: stop passing legacy SandboxPolicy to guardian reviews (#25911)\n\n## Why\n\nGuardian review turns already submit a read-only `PermissionProfile`,\nwhich is the permissions model the runtime should honor. Passing the\nequivalent legacy `SandboxPolicy` through `ThreadSettingsOverrides`\nkeeps two representations of the same read-only constraint alive on this\npath and makes the guardian flow depend on compatibility plumbing that\nis being phased out.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Set `sandbox_policy` to `None` when the guardian review session\nsubmits its child `Op::UserInput`.\n- Keep `permission_profile: Some(PermissionProfile::read_only())` and\n`approval_policy: Some(AskForApproval::Never)`, so the guardian review\nremains read-only and cannot request approvals.\n- Remove the now-unused `SandboxPolicy` import and redundant comment\nfrom `codex-rs/core/src/guardian/review_session.rs`.\n\n## Verification\n\nNot run locally; this is a narrow cleanup of redundant thread-settings\noverride state.","verified_at":"2026-06-02T21:16:13Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f6d64bd6ab3bf1a9587bbc13a00711029120d3e9","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/f6d64bd6ab3bf1a9587bbc13a00711029120d3e9","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f6d64bd6ab3bf1a9587bbc13a00711029120d3e9/comments","author":{"login":"bolinfest","id":655869,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTg2OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/655869?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest","html_url":"https://github.com/bolinfest","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"c74be11672cdf90cda60869961075965b02f213a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c74be11672cdf90cda60869961075965b02f213a","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/c74be11672cdf90cda60869961075965b02f213a"}]},{"sha":"c74be11672cdf90cda60869961075965b02f213a","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGM3NGJlMTE2NzJjZGY5MGNkYTYwODY5OTYxMDc1OTY1YjAyZjIxM2E","commit":{"author":{"name":"joeflorencio-openai","email":"joeflorencio@openai.com","date":"2026-06-02T21:11:20Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-02T21:11:20Z"},"message":"fix: update image generation test helper rename (#25938)\n\n## Summary\n- update the app-server image generation integration test to use\n`TestAppServer`\n- completes the test helper rename from #25701 for this newer test file\n\n## Validation\n- `cargo fmt -- --config imports_granularity=Item`\n- `cargo check -p codex-app-server --test all`\n\nNote: `just fmt` ran Rust formatting but failed on Python/SDK formatting\nbecause the sandbox could not access the local `uv` cache.","tree":{"sha":"6ebc903935b8d07293942c177cbb41999b159e18","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/6ebc903935b8d07293942c177cbb41999b159e18"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/c74be11672cdf90cda60869961075965b02f213a","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqH0b4CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAfRoQAEB5cUaZUgFczVOLL2uG867r\n90fb+Z9nk4B6SR0m5wR2ordMchOfu9ThAwyQ/xip1p7jEy1xRdvF/4cNdUCAOInZ\ni8FoF7LqhbXsdiaB0LVwWLXLBFT+b2/krDRIpPqzkCtTj/AOD+dQVGRLX/oEsPNa\nkxyw4zE2jjSOyghDxRQOo9INggzfaICLfVRD8KqzYB+lG5SD96//UwM3okL14VBT\n9ghg87humJEydd3gKNXY2LJ6kZqVtpyeutgkpd+jWXC2EK9Euou/36ah8yVAOSe8\n+WZpd+MDtUph2reyyYAoaH3bYnyoKvbkOqHrPEVdUheCoG4kREVI1S83xVbV/rAn\npaPHMauQIAgMKEIRfpnoZnyfA4niZv8ff5UsnJ4xKfJL+6dB8iDpHgdPM0O1g199\nP14VXWy7l81f5aG1EzaQFF/MBOtxi6fU1hlWUBvfr53GUJvVNA+bnIIMz4ufrpqV\njareAhHhXURi/HTts0rsUCnGlQwONxmYLe2QWdfeUn+7hvtBAHQ8maIE1aNjmTpl\nD8C32wo4fDrt+KCHKDdSp0+DVYOi1AZCSept3Y+0KC6sMSb5WBT3HGYfu1xZnX5j\nSRLELhLct74oDlPp4y06d1XU3o1Ufs9hS8CZNxUtCpzmq5LmFcru0905ST5QOgCI\nlTA9SumuUEXniv88vgOo\n=I7Y4\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 6ebc903935b8d07293942c177cbb41999b159e18\nparent d45cd2624848b185d10ab2f29b40fd581f407ac8\nauthor joeflorencio-openai <joeflorencio@openai.com> 1780434680 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780434680 -0700\n\nfix: update image generation test helper rename (#25938)\n\n## Summary\n- update the app-server image generation integration test to use\n`TestAppServer`\n- completes the test helper rename from #25701 for this newer test file\n\n## Validation\n- `cargo fmt -- --config imports_granularity=Item`\n- `cargo check -p codex-app-server --test all`\n\nNote: `just fmt` ran Rust formatting but failed on Python/SDK formatting\nbecause the sandbox could not access the local `uv` cache.","verified_at":"2026-06-02T21:11:21Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c74be11672cdf90cda60869961075965b02f213a","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/c74be11672cdf90cda60869961075965b02f213a","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c74be11672cdf90cda60869961075965b02f213a/comments","author":{"login":"joeflorencio-openai","id":195963627,"node_id":"U_kgDOC64q6w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/195963627?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/joeflorencio-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"d45cd2624848b185d10ab2f29b40fd581f407ac8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/d45cd2624848b185d10ab2f29b40fd581f407ac8","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/d45cd2624848b185d10ab2f29b40fd581f407ac8"}]},{"sha":"d45cd2624848b185d10ab2f29b40fd581f407ac8","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGQ0NWNkMjYyNDg0OGIxODVkMTBhYjJmMjliNDBmZDU4MWY0MDdhYzg","commit":{"author":{"name":"joeflorencio-openai","email":"joeflorencio@openai.com","date":"2026-06-02T20:18:59Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-02T20:18:59Z"},"message":"Switch runtime to cloud config bundle (#24622)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Adapts the moved `codex-cloud-config` crate from the legacy cloud\nrequirements endpoint to the new config bundle endpoint.\n- Switches runtime consumers from `CloudRequirementsLoader` to\n`CloudConfigBundleLoader` so one shared bundle supplies cloud-delivered\nconfig and requirements.\n- Removes the legacy cloud requirements domain loader path.\n\n## Details\n\nThis intentionally keeps `codex-cloud-config` monolithic for review\nlineage: the previous PR establishes the crate move, and this PR shows\nthe behavior change against that moved implementation. A follow-up PR\nsplits the module back into focused files.\n\nThe new bundle path preserves the important cloud requirements loader\nsemantics where intended: account-scoped signed cache, 30 minute TTL, 5\nminute refresh cadence, retry/backoff, auth recovery, and fail-closed\nstartup loading. The cached payload changes from a single requirements\nTOML string to the backend-delivered bundle, and validation rejects\nmalformed config or requirements fragments before cache write/use.","tree":{"sha":"b93c41ce074e0e7d96891ffc515d2825c5a01243","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/b93c41ce074e0e7d96891ffc515d2825c5a01243"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/d45cd2624848b185d10ab2f29b40fd581f407ac8","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHzqzCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAshwQAFQFbsf0ZlCaj3AnVmolOlc7\nBrscQfyCQhsblaPVLEldSxT+UFMnfY1kYGwpve9evNcSeqOuSZCARqtKP8QwwYIO\n6wt+piVdb6kj2rwiqL+HwHPM4MhZKj5wtIapOsj1XQ9iOjmyjZjmJ1EMvj/nZb1Y\nQ2M1n+0c+DKkLLzIMu+4A2suofkeeN0PJacMUKabVq2ZaWNkEh9WTE9OVV7hnEkP\nImJnLAk84NGwK6A2nSli+8CBbEjexkaUS2rT+mX9XjRDZij0hkvsVD7eRS0jWzIz\nzOtGKhF+BB04jI6UcrCDyc9PVr31o0JiRlR+1gYB02OGPNypjhNurlDNf1d/KR/U\n6bWjYqLIb8f90JqwdCTtWippNasdS71uAOT5WRqMaNGtvxN6E1f/hBpYycgFYqf4\n5REM16nLXZF9wBw61ZdAMmYHiU3ZsF9Un/t8HSyGpeMoWdI4Jdg3jyjrieVUV5p1\nXN4e5Cn+JuQDZ5EfP18XD6icj5J2ruisDTcpa/WCB+4gqHwqtBm/hteFgrWwLPg9\nAI+2jxzRcgK1/KhsW+niRZ86hNE0I47zx6nk9JGGcgsE7N7RwOslfQGbuayl2xVi\njcAL6lnrfKUd+o7V7Typ+5uCt1vsJC1RgszUMc1ZjjyasR5xJh2d5k3WHhBe7zLo\nyi7wJsnm/0YTZS4JyJUp\n=xXOP\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree b93c41ce074e0e7d96891ffc515d2825c5a01243\nparent b794182ea7e57c9bde214bb9fd32040445a8ae38\nauthor joeflorencio-openai <joeflorencio@openai.com> 1780431539 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780431539 -0700\n\nSwitch runtime to cloud config bundle (#24622)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Adapts the moved `codex-cloud-config` crate from the legacy cloud\nrequirements endpoint to the new config bundle endpoint.\n- Switches runtime consumers from `CloudRequirementsLoader` to\n`CloudConfigBundleLoader` so one shared bundle supplies cloud-delivered\nconfig and requirements.\n- Removes the legacy cloud requirements domain loader path.\n\n## Details\n\nThis intentionally keeps `codex-cloud-config` monolithic for review\nlineage: the previous PR establishes the crate move, and this PR shows\nthe behavior change against that moved implementation. A follow-up PR\nsplits the module back into focused files.\n\nThe new bundle path preserves the important cloud requirements loader\nsemantics where intended: account-scoped signed cache, 30 minute TTL, 5\nminute refresh cadence, retry/backoff, auth recovery, and fail-closed\nstartup loading. The cached payload changes from a single requirements\nTOML string to the backend-delivered bundle, and validation rejects\nmalformed config or requirements fragments before cache write/use.","verified_at":"2026-06-02T20:19:00Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/d45cd2624848b185d10ab2f29b40fd581f407ac8","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/d45cd2624848b185d10ab2f29b40fd581f407ac8","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/d45cd2624848b185d10ab2f29b40fd581f407ac8/comments","author":{"login":"joeflorencio-openai","id":195963627,"node_id":"U_kgDOC64q6w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/195963627?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/joeflorencio-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"b794182ea7e57c9bde214bb9fd32040445a8ae38","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/b794182ea7e57c9bde214bb9fd32040445a8ae38","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/b794182ea7e57c9bde214bb9fd32040445a8ae38"}]},{"sha":"b794182ea7e57c9bde214bb9fd32040445a8ae38","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGI3OTQxODJlYTdlNTdjOWJkZTIxNGJiOWZkMzIwNDA0NDVhOGFlMzg","commit":{"author":{"name":"knittel-openai","email":"153027209+knittel-openai@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-02T19:46:14Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-02T19:46:14Z"},"message":"Populate workspace kind on Codex turn events (#25135)\n\n## Summary\n- carry `workspace_kind` from Responses API client metadata into the\nturn resolved analytics fact\n- serialize the optional value on `codex_turn_event`\n- cover both the turn metadata source and turn event serialization\n\nThe `workspace_kind` tells us whether a thread had a project attached vs\nprojectless. this is an indicator for who is adopting Codex for\nknowledge work outside of coding\n\n## Testing\n- `env UV_CACHE_DIR=/private/tmp/uv-cache\n/private/tmp/cargo-tools/bin/just fmt`\n- `env PATH=/private/tmp/cargo-tools/bin:$PATH\nCARGO_HOME=/private/tmp/cargo-home UV_CACHE_DIR=/private/tmp/uv-cache\n/private/tmp/cargo-tools/bin/just test -p codex-analytics`\n- `env PATH=/private/tmp/cargo-tools/bin:$PATH\nCARGO_HOME=/private/tmp/cargo-home UV_CACHE_DIR=/private/tmp/uv-cache\n/private/tmp/cargo-tools/bin/just test -p codex-core turn_metadata`\n\nPaired with openai/openai#970661, which keeps forwarding the same\nmetadata key through Responses API headers.","tree":{"sha":"6c9e03741ce36194232bac662276b7d6fc930236","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/6c9e03741ce36194232bac662276b7d6fc930236"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/b794182ea7e57c9bde214bb9fd32040445a8ae38","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHzMGCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAm2EQAI4qfCAwh1BSd+M0zuD3HL88\n3mmTSLmKWYd6hakzRNHlXvECknOUeDWyVNBZ+vImxwvnWgVT41c9n4VSg+RyD2uG\ngDST8AIJcsHy9ACWuP1yTqr9P5Nc79X2ckn/ojyWhzKte5bq28CWilIk9Q8eYvoq\nWdii8b8E2XmUoCqYxH9ionCOX4ByQwEQ4X3pst0cUcdffLxHRS4/6RW9bmBVcfjp\nlTsOY7Z4feUXQxT89MJ6EvwhA91vbkQ2ZYFEhn+6wFaBk8vNbanQZ8dw9vm/VBf0\nwyZpM1qjJ8REX7sC/Si+kJWWZcZkmrAWrSmHGEV/YI4ou7HQnKFZvvx4OK/c44UD\n4GSBrmFsaee5EcCQ269Qx0dqFKgkA9m/JKlaQbVSBD31FNIcF16Rbq6KkPUA7fji\naBamZDFWhwqhnU6IMdikWw8y5tHcgWpiHYPOXgYJi/IQXCgaP56DgqXnBc6HiRwn\n8OSj3EQho+4GCmNlQDuCt6GSE4rE7nfMBgUQvGHmtgV0Imf7XHX3ZbVU9vKBAJzr\niVHqT89KC6ZGc2X4qkvZBOpZTXNg7prLdKgehl+jMWahvo6hntt92b4TmspUd8QP\nGCV14J/8bR06VLy/Hu7zSwcgAegCj7vit6kNXJsOxxaRf9FY11ADcAwVsc5Lef3i\n1EwTTcnM6E659KVkW346\n=xG4b\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 6c9e03741ce36194232bac662276b7d6fc930236\nparent ad355d4c9641953bb85c242c92f72f924edd4687\nauthor knittel-openai <153027209+knittel-openai@users.noreply.github.com> 1780429574 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780429574 -0700\n\nPopulate workspace kind on Codex turn events (#25135)\n\n## Summary\n- carry `workspace_kind` from Responses API client metadata into the\nturn resolved analytics fact\n- serialize the optional value on `codex_turn_event`\n- cover both the turn metadata source and turn event serialization\n\nThe `workspace_kind` tells us whether a thread had a project attached vs\nprojectless. this is an indicator for who is adopting Codex for\nknowledge work outside of coding\n\n## Testing\n- `env UV_CACHE_DIR=/private/tmp/uv-cache\n/private/tmp/cargo-tools/bin/just fmt`\n- `env PATH=/private/tmp/cargo-tools/bin:$PATH\nCARGO_HOME=/private/tmp/cargo-home UV_CACHE_DIR=/private/tmp/uv-cache\n/private/tmp/cargo-tools/bin/just test -p codex-analytics`\n- `env PATH=/private/tmp/cargo-tools/bin:$PATH\nCARGO_HOME=/private/tmp/cargo-home UV_CACHE_DIR=/private/tmp/uv-cache\n/private/tmp/cargo-tools/bin/just test -p codex-core turn_metadata`\n\nPaired with openai/openai#970661, which keeps forwarding the same\nmetadata key through Responses API headers.","verified_at":"2026-06-02T19:46:14Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/b794182ea7e57c9bde214bb9fd32040445a8ae38","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/b794182ea7e57c9bde214bb9fd32040445a8ae38","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/b794182ea7e57c9bde214bb9fd32040445a8ae38/comments","author":{"login":"knittel-openai","id":153027209,"node_id":"U_kgDOCR8CiQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/153027209?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/knittel-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/knittel-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/knittel-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/knittel-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/knittel-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/knittel-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/knittel-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/knittel-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/knittel-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/knittel-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/knittel-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"ad355d4c9641953bb85c242c92f72f924edd4687","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ad355d4c9641953bb85c242c92f72f924edd4687","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/ad355d4c9641953bb85c242c92f72f924edd4687"}]},{"sha":"ad355d4c9641953bb85c242c92f72f924edd4687","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGFkMzU1ZDRjOTY0MTk1M2JiODVjMjQyYzkyZjcyZjkyNGVkZDQ2ODc","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eric Traut","email":"etraut@openai.com","date":"2026-06-02T19:42:42Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-02T19:42:42Z"},"message":"Fix Windows running thread resume path normalization (#25509)\n\n## Why\n\nFixes #24944.\n\nOn Windows, app-server resume could reject an active running thread when\nthe requested session path used normal `C:\\...` form and the\nalready-running path used verbatim `\\\\?\\C:\\...` form. The paths point at\nthe same JSONL file, but the resume stale-path guard compared raw\n`PathBuf`s, so desktop resume and heartbeat flows could fail with a\nmismatched-path error.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Compare requested and active rollout paths with\n`path_utils::paths_match_after_normalization`.\n- Extend the existing running-thread mismatched-path test with a\nWindows-only same-file resume case before the stale-path rejection.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `just test -p codex-app-server\nthread_resume_rejects_mismatched_path_for_running_thread_id`","tree":{"sha":"ca721a20c0d734c2430856869639b9953d3c6310","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/ca721a20c0d734c2430856869639b9953d3c6310"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/ad355d4c9641953bb85c242c92f72f924edd4687","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHzIyCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAS+MQAJL1F7Zablc7cmjGmhtW6zEY\nZrGR5MEDtVmft2OFDSk8XovgOMMyyUd83p2fTjOnlyPR0s6N37UJN/guMXwgCKsU\no3NUuNvXwZlFGeka1qIv6j0AjIaAvik8AY/BYk2xMez/vpTWdyKuF0JuYS5+hk8y\n4SyqZ0YTfoD+ZTrBv9NDVoaMj4y0ZLv5TZjiRzglzxALFo9r7z3yQBzlvI2k78ac\nDSCS1bD0oEkrbiHGrfXOAeVYmtuajqwyh26+e+F2/APr55CJciFOmZhBFUORe04O\nUZnPXcGy5dsVsBFDhI6SWOfUmLW8aV3UMhGZGK0B6w2aPgQmWs22duaE8g0nIfa3\npTftY3o11lsxsv1qpWOy8gddKsHObFhJFtRJ5aLwQK5/cjU6xC++Oy4NxmfiQmMQ\n0UJI0XNBWOYyeRGMRZ3H15Js2dNeJWC8gw8H701+LEoxvRjTR26H452rG/fcffLR\nnU/beJ3BHXtKjzn06QFeBiGDL1JiZeOLPSmhLpuO8fnhIrvrU8FM4offwqyK6HrA\nHefPsIpeHyCYYcqRxvzeAXOsJBS7v97iWqd64K9h0Bci6pDfAnshwV5YaHwPmPr0\nty0+OqjPy2mNODi4lj9SDkV9sctEqM7pgetod2UOyYS/5rMQZyl/WnrrcrWeMRzv\netD7eO4ge9wtFH7zhUq+\n=uO6N\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree ca721a20c0d734c2430856869639b9953d3c6310\nparent af18e92140f875f042325114108b8720d6836e96\nauthor Eric Traut <etraut@openai.com> 1780429362 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780429362 -0700\n\nFix Windows running thread resume path normalization (#25509)\n\n## Why\n\nFixes #24944.\n\nOn Windows, app-server resume could reject an active running thread when\nthe requested session path used normal `C:\\...` form and the\nalready-running path used verbatim `\\\\?\\C:\\...` form. The paths point at\nthe same JSONL file, but the resume stale-path guard compared raw\n`PathBuf`s, so desktop resume and heartbeat flows could fail with a\nmismatched-path error.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Compare requested and active rollout paths with\n`path_utils::paths_match_after_normalization`.\n- Extend the existing running-thread mismatched-path test with a\nWindows-only same-file resume case before the stale-path rejection.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `just test -p codex-app-server\nthread_resume_rejects_mismatched_path_for_running_thread_id`","verified_at":"2026-06-02T19:42:42Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ad355d4c9641953bb85c242c92f72f924edd4687","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/ad355d4c9641953bb85c242c92f72f924edd4687","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ad355d4c9641953bb85c242c92f72f924edd4687/comments","author":{"login":"etraut-openai","id":223546144,"node_id":"U_kgDODVMLIA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/223546144?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/etraut-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"af18e92140f875f042325114108b8720d6836e96","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/af18e92140f875f042325114108b8720d6836e96","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/af18e92140f875f042325114108b8720d6836e96"}]},{"sha":"af18e92140f875f042325114108b8720d6836e96","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGFmMThlOTIxNDBmODc1ZjA0MjMyNTExNDEwOGI4NzIwZDY4MzZlOTY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Shijie Rao","email":"shijie.rao@openai.com","date":"2026-06-02T19:41:13Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-02T19:41:13Z"},"message":"Use environment secrets for Azure signing (#24859)\n\n## Summary\n- Move Azure Trusted Signing values out of reusable workflow-call\nsecrets and into the `azure-artifact-signing` environment scope\n- Attach the Windows signing job to the `azure-artifact-signing`\nenvironment so it can resolve the signing secrets directly\n- Stop inheriting caller secrets for the Windows release reusable\nworkflow\n\n## Validation\n- `git diff --check -- .github/workflows/rust-release.yml\n.github/workflows/rust-release-windows.yml`\n- `ruby -e 'require \"yaml\"; ARGV.each { |path| YAML.load_file(path);\nputs \"ok #{path}\" }' .github/workflows/rust-release.yml\n.github/workflows/rust-release-windows.yml`","tree":{"sha":"375dd386d6935c4d5174c345f352d3bae6a1a67e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/375dd386d6935c4d5174c345f352d3bae6a1a67e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/af18e92140f875f042325114108b8720d6836e96","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHzHaCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAznMQAEUAABebeEwwOe4GvqYPEFmq\nW9WI6HChxtwPva1UwQqa660hEn4INcMeS6JBGTeg/sOMSp5TNP1NQpyKpBfU1uOz\nQrCJyJM65iV36U6cPHvG1TRqCzgslkQyvvXoCk2r1jI+1g5siBXt0Xf9ItvEBkpI\nXias5ZO+IW7jNvZZO63SbftJNyeMIxDyjwO+docP2xVZuuiczoU8+ffpIkyAV84f\nU3AgQ5FiiUq4jXQUZuzSnhnUJRM+qJg8whvuFFaLfUf0oBfXfNq+NPE2BFR3P6r0\nELorciEdF4gvNBE2H2M7U1JpVVQ5F2KjjCYMxq+pzkre2uEcmyeZRMIoZ0LKwLCB\nrIGV7O2RLVY3R2LTqgyN5eqF1MK69iKl3K8PfVh+Gxr+PHyCQjYeeJuwhg7otww8\natfnzwMJFEeeMbHjD0rjnnDyawDU/K1ildGwpys0rmFHKQccMPDr6FSLbaqZkcDl\nUGdyiJ+R3iZ8opXF4etOuv/LXJr3ms+PQkJHyaDNgm0c0hJ5avh3lk+O8KwfYu+D\n7KFEkmrTBUwTcinPWAfgleOEebGSNBsCXMmlsqXcsv3prq7YxKKJYB08e+Askzsh\ny6a949rdTa066Vl7jgM0kcq7LlxW8XN8iSvBdqa6QroSY+iCmQBjMAMqHYc3Zs6i\n27wNqkN6PlKZPbZgEiAH\n=QmGK\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 375dd386d6935c4d5174c345f352d3bae6a1a67e\nparent bc49677ec8aeed439c45832802918b36b1c04b5f\nauthor Shijie Rao <shijie.rao@openai.com> 1780429273 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780429273 -0700\n\nUse environment secrets for Azure signing (#24859)\n\n## Summary\n- Move Azure Trusted Signing values out of reusable workflow-call\nsecrets and into the `azure-artifact-signing` environment scope\n- Attach the Windows signing job to the `azure-artifact-signing`\nenvironment so it can resolve the signing secrets directly\n- Stop inheriting caller secrets for the Windows release reusable\nworkflow\n\n## Validation\n- `git diff --check -- .github/workflows/rust-release.yml\n.github/workflows/rust-release-windows.yml`\n- `ruby -e 'require \"yaml\"; ARGV.each { |path| YAML.load_file(path);\nputs \"ok #{path}\" }' .github/workflows/rust-release.yml\n.github/workflows/rust-release-windows.yml`","verified_at":"2026-06-02T19:41:14Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/af18e92140f875f042325114108b8720d6836e96","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/af18e92140f875f042325114108b8720d6836e96","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/af18e92140f875f042325114108b8720d6836e96/comments","author":{"login":"shijie-oai","id":235382242,"node_id":"U_kgDODgel4g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/235382242?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/shijie-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"bc49677ec8aeed439c45832802918b36b1c04b5f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/bc49677ec8aeed439c45832802918b36b1c04b5f","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/bc49677ec8aeed439c45832802918b36b1c04b5f"}]},{"sha":"bc49677ec8aeed439c45832802918b36b1c04b5f","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGJjNDk2NzdlYzhhZWVkNDM5YzQ1ODMyODAyOTE4YjM2YjFjMDRiNWY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Ahmed Ibrahim","email":"aibrahim@openai.com","date":"2026-06-02T19:27:01Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-02T19:27:01Z"},"message":"[codex] Pin Python SDK to glibc-compatible runtime (#25907)\n\n## Summary\n- pin the Python SDK runtime package to `openai-codex-cli-bin==0.136.0`\nso Ubuntu/glibc installs resolve a compatible wheel\n- refresh generated SDK artifacts and lock data for the runtime update\n- keep newly generated client-message-id wire models internal to the\ngenerated protocol layer\n\n## Dependency\n- merge #25906 first so the Python SDK release publishes both manylinux\nand musllinux runtime wheels before publishing the package with this pin\n\n## Validation\n- ran `just fmt`\n- regenerated the Python public API helpers\n- validated the edited workflow YAML\n- CI passed 29/29 checks","tree":{"sha":"1c752755788f78f5f8774aa51d485025db26d46c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/1c752755788f78f5f8774aa51d485025db26d46c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/bc49677ec8aeed439c45832802918b36b1c04b5f","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHy6FCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAALkMQAEGvv5QQRyR9i4DXig71xQtz\nt7qF9zcO5xcI5T/Th6l/a0iTLV1JhJd4SmGdKNq26is4h7Noox17ilIfyXsxaaBx\nc1J3umzaZadfiCARS/bhZO1XM/hGp7xmSY/FMXL3VoIBaU/e+k4+aNYjehx+FjON\nkqye2jFkmuQGd9b72fI+uy2xWZOu9iQsAA4K0XM+2gg15QQzmIu3uEAAVt0d2le2\nRGXTCAsgymPEtHJlC9XNv8uwkVgIQ0p/Ul/4XsZ6qS8Ry5e72eiV3gU5++HiuCdD\na2zZHp+4M+hNi+aHCkhqqbd+eglIVZmC9EYqZlNYZqwVRmWq1qESi4BllTYt3DzY\n4aLhgXtw5b7EDBJZhG6XVAY7wavMEBnf7XV4C/zguNbdeGYjIOvxCiKJFHsF/Wcc\nxC4Ddf1wcABidtX8/11F2G+4i1I78h4ZqWtLBghEStM7zGkXvah3UM6jsYn9IsUY\nKBbmh80FGWlTWv+JbCZjjMVaFPEgHleW978khST+ah9IYWO1igAeUDCdKQr6AAvJ\n+vhE68rPdrVfacqH6BzP4rP64wuQ4ku2Aw2EdUBxLJmv/zqo2Vu+xG6CzYIlGOVM\nXbwUvsMi2gYTAORb3tETmsqijl3ZidDLPw5yGjXhQBhIfnzu4d+S/kYAkdWJGsA0\nnN+XhxxR6BAtvC/Lez9O\n=2Er8\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 1c752755788f78f5f8774aa51d485025db26d46c\nparent 9de568372da86141ced85e4153494b0b159f2171\nauthor Ahmed Ibrahim <aibrahim@openai.com> 1780428421 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780428421 -0700\n\n[codex] Pin Python SDK to glibc-compatible runtime (#25907)\n\n## Summary\n- pin the Python SDK runtime package to `openai-codex-cli-bin==0.136.0`\nso Ubuntu/glibc installs resolve a compatible wheel\n- refresh generated SDK artifacts and lock data for the runtime update\n- keep newly generated client-message-id wire models internal to the\ngenerated protocol layer\n\n## Dependency\n- merge #25906 first so the Python SDK release publishes both manylinux\nand musllinux runtime wheels before publishing the package with this pin\n\n## Validation\n- ran `just fmt`\n- regenerated the Python public API helpers\n- validated the edited workflow YAML\n- CI passed 29/29 checks","verified_at":"2026-06-02T19:27:02Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/bc49677ec8aeed439c45832802918b36b1c04b5f","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/bc49677ec8aeed439c45832802918b36b1c04b5f","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/bc49677ec8aeed439c45832802918b36b1c04b5f/comments","author":{"login":"aibrahim-oai","id":219906144,"node_id":"U_kgDODRuAYA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/219906144?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/aibrahim-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"9de568372da86141ced85e4153494b0b159f2171","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/9de568372da86141ced85e4153494b0b159f2171","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/9de568372da86141ced85e4153494b0b159f2171"}]},{"sha":"9de568372da86141ced85e4153494b0b159f2171","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDlkZTU2ODM3MmRhODYxNDFjZWQ4NWU0MTUzNDk0YjBiMTU5ZjIxNzE","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-02T19:09:34Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-02T19:09:34Z"},"message":"Propagate permission approval environment id (#25862)\n\n## Stack\n\n1. #25850 - Key request-permission grants by environment: stores and\napplies sticky permission grants per environment id.\n2. #25858 - Add `environmentId` to `request_permissions`: lets the model\ntarget a selected environment and resolves relative permission paths\nagainst it.\n3. This PR (#25862) - Propagate permission approval environment id:\ncarries the selected environment id through approval events, app-server\nrequests, TUI prompts, and delegate forwarding.\n4. #25867 - Add remote request permissions integration coverage:\nverifies the selected remote environment across request, approval, grant\nreuse, and exec.\n\nThis PR is stacked on #25858, and #25867 is stacked on this PR.\n\n## Why\n\nPR2 lets the model bind a `request_permissions` call to a selected\nenvironment, but the approval event and client-facing request still\nneeded to carry that binding. For CCA, the user-facing prompt and\ndelegated approval path should know which environment the grant applies\nto instead of relying on cwd alone.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Added optional `environmentId` to `RequestPermissionsEvent`.\n- Emit the selected environment id from core permission approval events.\n- Preserve the environment id through delegate forwarding, including\ncwd-based delegated requests.\n- Added `environmentId` to app-server permission approval params,\ngenerated schema/TypeScript artifacts, and README examples.\n- Preserve and display the environment id in TUI permission approval\nprompts.\n- Updated focused core, app-server protocol, and TUI conversion\ncoverage.\n\n## Testing\n\nNot run locally per instruction. Performed read-only `git diff --check`.","tree":{"sha":"995394b8083104db4c87a32038463ac4baa2f3f1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/995394b8083104db4c87a32038463ac4baa2f3f1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/9de568372da86141ced85e4153494b0b159f2171","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHypuCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAzhEQAD9KRPOvyTxkZ/IQtcrvFQx/\nXJ64hD9m2NpQb0BG8wQUIeAdu8BAzIztNaFSr3Ff4Ug2dQqaN1YI08sISZNGVtU2\nO4JL/Bk5Nxcnj4KyYtX6bm+XcAlWJS5OjqQABNMpu2mrMTtrEy8axSr4OOO6GB90\n+/07Qna5RnZBI+mgSdDRUDWtQ+Aq1ZLHdZZCwGHdWIt9O3tHgtn4iowJI3Qyz0u1\noORfduBwHZpagQJY1FMBFDdsA8/zOK/sSuYzg+Lx40hUs3UUPy8L6mvXd/PQCi3y\n9mvIp04i2UH8C7V3fjCDNZQq3Xa5Q9PxXDrOVJmE0PTu08QWYd3jjQ+K+uAdvsBf\nBVKQhNERGfLNjoCf3VpoJTefWow75ujZaIkrvtWvzsl7+nOB1/ATlXjcu+5dwtXp\nEgie1mJDVbCp1X44tQohrNnYeWOK4cYUcuwTFJIKfwS6XePEA991rlal6UqtqHrV\nP/2oflxVwLyQc3zrEJIc8cGoNw/eVc16kyhlnkWWVUWXB9cCFgkC4L7wsr+kzxZ+\nqLrPLh14CmXoJrkSJsZJd1yj2+47GPdGUM2cPuc8Wn3Z1o6IXt3YjNCaEC+YRE8T\ns2DVpSAyVSbtG6KxXbFMd+hzz2MBVuG+shiXCwr04G4fAOD3EpKj6FzkcSvs+bkC\nuw3hjontf/y27Bc8/i/Z\n=39JK\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 995394b8083104db4c87a32038463ac4baa2f3f1\nparent de124c32be47b01e2204269f26bd1f00ab15bb56\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1780427374 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780427374 +0200\n\nPropagate permission approval environment id (#25862)\n\n## Stack\n\n1. #25850 - Key request-permission grants by environment: stores and\napplies sticky permission grants per environment id.\n2. #25858 - Add `environmentId` to `request_permissions`: lets the model\ntarget a selected environment and resolves relative permission paths\nagainst it.\n3. This PR (#25862) - Propagate permission approval environment id:\ncarries the selected environment id through approval events, app-server\nrequests, TUI prompts, and delegate forwarding.\n4. #25867 - Add remote request permissions integration coverage:\nverifies the selected remote environment across request, approval, grant\nreuse, and exec.\n\nThis PR is stacked on #25858, and #25867 is stacked on this PR.\n\n## Why\n\nPR2 lets the model bind a `request_permissions` call to a selected\nenvironment, but the approval event and client-facing request still\nneeded to carry that binding. For CCA, the user-facing prompt and\ndelegated approval path should know which environment the grant applies\nto instead of relying on cwd alone.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Added optional `environmentId` to `RequestPermissionsEvent`.\n- Emit the selected environment id from core permission approval events.\n- Preserve the environment id through delegate forwarding, including\ncwd-based delegated requests.\n- Added `environmentId` to app-server permission approval params,\ngenerated schema/TypeScript artifacts, and README examples.\n- Preserve and display the environment id in TUI permission approval\nprompts.\n- Updated focused core, app-server protocol, and TUI conversion\ncoverage.\n\n## Testing\n\nNot run locally per instruction. Performed read-only `git diff --check`.","verified_at":"2026-06-02T19:09:35Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/9de568372da86141ced85e4153494b0b159f2171","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/9de568372da86141ced85e4153494b0b159f2171","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/9de568372da86141ced85e4153494b0b159f2171/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"de124c32be47b01e2204269f26bd1f00ab15bb56","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/de124c32be47b01e2204269f26bd1f00ab15bb56","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/de124c32be47b01e2204269f26bd1f00ab15bb56"}]},{"sha":"de124c32be47b01e2204269f26bd1f00ab15bb56","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGRlMTI0YzMyYmU0N2IwMWUyMjA0MjY5ZjI2YmQxZjAwYWIxNWJiNTY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Shijie Rao","email":"shijie.rao@openai.com","date":"2026-06-02T19:05:52Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-02T19:05:52Z"},"message":"Fix Windows release PDB staging (#25916)\n\n## Summary\n- Teach the Windows release prebuild staging step to locate Rust/MSVC\nPDBs emitted with crate-style underscore names.\n- Stage PDBs under the shipped hyphenated binary names so the downstream\nsymbol archive step keeps the same artifact contract.\n- Keep a fallback for already-hyphenated PDB names and fail with a clear\ndiagnostic if neither form exists.\n\n## Root cause\nThe recent symbol publishing change in #25649 started copying\n`${binary}.pdb` from `target/<triple>/release` during Windows prebuild\nstaging. Cargo still emits the `.exe` with the hyphenated binary name,\nbut MSVC PDBs for hyphenated Rust crates are emitted with underscores,\nfor example `codex_app_server.pdb` for `codex-app-server.exe`. The\nrelease workflow was still building into the expected directory; the new\nPDB copy step was looking for the wrong filename.\n\n## Impact\nThis unblocks the `rust-release` Windows prebuilt-binary jobs for\nhyphenated binaries while preserving the hyphenated PDB names consumed\nby the final Windows release packaging and symbol archive steps.\n\n## Validation\n- `just fmt` from `codex-rs`\n- `git diff --check -- .github/workflows/rust-release-windows.yml`\n- Parsed `.github/workflows/rust-release-windows.yml` as YAML locally\n- Local bash staging sanity test for both underscore-emitted and\nhyphenated PDB filenames","tree":{"sha":"72d564a3043b1806407fe9faba104b68e6b2b6eb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/72d564a3043b1806407fe9faba104b68e6b2b6eb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/de124c32be47b01e2204269f26bd1f00ab15bb56","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHymQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAMWAQAIQg0kSedWnq7B7SYml7SnmQ\n+N3BYDR5guFTkJnPVjPmaAV6rXVlIOoR6ZIvoO/cUNcW1QID2MHqgpZ3VqaOZ8hI\nIPIUX+XLBv0OsbaXJYzDxob4WacT1kQByFZ8YlgkSkDUv40SORNGtY2JwgN+W1Hq\nBEh9ytDzWvaCTi0NhF0p0+Yj8wx7dx0F+2awoNcQO+u5trLQl44Xz4OUAkUFbJsu\nOWHNzj7tOZ4t4tm5wPRQcT2lAeRAzXvAEopwr9JHqI4hTva0GWAsq2WZPnBm0pjZ\nFDKKboQ1d0R/SZK/yjH2XxqJ3LNRgglEMFo7iaS5tRDoBTGR8QTBELgr2Mdursyk\npRMPlcLHWXNZq7netZBOZj6WCOZF/BKFL/yFjSEMt8bdYnTKSlx7mD2wewsaCY/p\nDS5vWfBLj8GwXP+Dl57NcQ8QrLZG+Cq+tRiiZW9D6kElgT5tswYUobk1RqLqdhF3\n2b7bhMDsrhmHKbFNFdwGjQHtkHraKh93+sqVEwP3n3a80MCW+oZgHbcir7piwFUf\n+YTWMbqtMsi1fhyxVRhTMs9WQMoEUQUw9NwhMrdO+0c+N/rJcZzJh1IlKyX3VmDT\nrW1yUABkJB7M+LbhChx94BUqSwj3EwUvjoe4Q4wqtG2ca37OL0iE4JKzgUi3hKF7\nepSCPpfNgRd1iJOFANX5\n=nysN\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 72d564a3043b1806407fe9faba104b68e6b2b6eb\nparent 57f337a8e90360649112f8fc01d9ee2f9f2afa24\nauthor Shijie Rao <shijie.rao@openai.com> 1780427152 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780427152 -0700\n\nFix Windows release PDB staging (#25916)\n\n## Summary\n- Teach the Windows release prebuild staging step to locate Rust/MSVC\nPDBs emitted with crate-style underscore names.\n- Stage PDBs under the shipped hyphenated binary names so the downstream\nsymbol archive step keeps the same artifact contract.\n- Keep a fallback for already-hyphenated PDB names and fail with a clear\ndiagnostic if neither form exists.\n\n## Root cause\nThe recent symbol publishing change in #25649 started copying\n`${binary}.pdb` from `target/<triple>/release` during Windows prebuild\nstaging. Cargo still emits the `.exe` with the hyphenated binary name,\nbut MSVC PDBs for hyphenated Rust crates are emitted with underscores,\nfor example `codex_app_server.pdb` for `codex-app-server.exe`. The\nrelease workflow was still building into the expected directory; the new\nPDB copy step was looking for the wrong filename.\n\n## Impact\nThis unblocks the `rust-release` Windows prebuilt-binary jobs for\nhyphenated binaries while preserving the hyphenated PDB names consumed\nby the final Windows release packaging and symbol archive steps.\n\n## Validation\n- `just fmt` from `codex-rs`\n- `git diff --check -- .github/workflows/rust-release-windows.yml`\n- Parsed `.github/workflows/rust-release-windows.yml` as YAML locally\n- Local bash staging sanity test for both underscore-emitted and\nhyphenated PDB filenames","verified_at":"2026-06-02T19:05:53Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/de124c32be47b01e2204269f26bd1f00ab15bb56","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/de124c32be47b01e2204269f26bd1f00ab15bb56","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/de124c32be47b01e2204269f26bd1f00ab15bb56/comments","author":{"login":"shijie-oai","id":235382242,"node_id":"U_kgDODgel4g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/235382242?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/shijie-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"57f337a8e90360649112f8fc01d9ee2f9f2afa24","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/57f337a8e90360649112f8fc01d9ee2f9f2afa24","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/57f337a8e90360649112f8fc01d9ee2f9f2afa24"}]},{"sha":"57f337a8e90360649112f8fc01d9ee2f9f2afa24","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDU3ZjMzN2E4ZTkwMzYwNjQ5MTEyZjhmYzAxZDllZTJmOWYyYWZhMjQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Won Park","email":"won@openai.com","date":"2026-06-02T19:00:04Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-02T19:00:04Z"},"message":"Route standalone image generation through host finalization md (#25176)\n\n## Why\n\nStandalone image-generation extensions emitted turn items through the\nlow-level event path, bypassing host-owned finalization such as image\npersistence and contributor processing. At the same time, the\ngenerated-image save-path hint must remain visible to the model through\nthe extension tool's `FunctionCallOutput`, rather than the legacy\nbuilt-in developer-message path.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Extended `ExtensionTurnItem` to support image-generation items while\nkeeping the extension-facing emitter API limited to `emit_started` and\n`emit_completed`.\n- Routed extension completion through core `finalize_turn_item`, so\nstandalone image-generation items receive host-owned processing and\npersisted `saved_path` values before publication.\n- Kept legacy built-in image generation on its existing\ndeveloper-message hint path, while standalone image generation returns\nits deterministic saved-path hint in `FunctionCallOutput`.\n- Shared the image artifact path and output-hint formatting used by core\nand the image-generation extension.\n- Passed thread identity through extension tool calls so standalone\nimage generation can construct the same intended artifact path as core.\n- Added an app-server integration test covering real standalone image\ngeneration, saved artifact publication, model-visible output hint\nwiring, and absence of the legacy developer-message hint.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just fmt`\n- `just test -p codex-image-generation-extension`\n- `just test -p codex-web-search-extension`\n- `just test -p codex-goal-extension`\n- `just test -p codex-memories-extension`\n- Targeted `codex-core` tests for image save history, extension\ncompletion finalization, and contributor execution\n- `just test -p codex-app-server\nstandalone_image_generation_returns_saved_path_hint_to_model`\n- `just fix -p codex-core`\n- `just fix -p codex-image-generation-extension`\n- `just bazel-lock-update`\n- `just bazel-lock-check`","tree":{"sha":"67840c2145fbf59d5aea1d07756968a7963abaa9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/67840c2145fbf59d5aea1d07756968a7963abaa9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/57f337a8e90360649112f8fc01d9ee2f9f2afa24","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHyg0CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAFSsQABF1Qon110wsqHkp9D0Kr2Zy\niPcBCj14vdw7NmdBV7j4aZgY8/gu3MtGTN9k+p1PILRJfdRvAoq91hGFDw7bU7J7\n/4SVLV3ixKyNqKpq7ce/MfvkyKqv2LSM6K97abdQ610xJNb5S460EG3iIlOwb8kc\nSrEi2UeYVfS/B4g0Tav5l0rJHOOBPNBcbBMajqdj3HOmkHLZHIDBdkpIEcDCvtkw\n7XTqTbGG+TbTYBMVg1yN44oyOuBBtjvvm3prTgmqHSud2C7qyfp/K0KtmZYqsunP\nLY5lXqzFjDzXG+8tCLRMd8I7ZBXfcit/s0vGRBpq4AzBxQIa3kcUBTRaIqniyeju\nFZ0zMPwm49dV3vv8Bzo2kBpgD/9yvFkHVKqc+vDK2Qq/eRLsFDamZcHYTMX5OA1C\nvbuEvNb49C2mG/2y2UR2vz66EtU7oWWYo0GRCIRm48Hh98g4wnApEoL9V2ZfStkd\nlCKocbljrdRvG+7Oo/RrQOEOYND3wtPNS/2sb9cvXGxBYVUXzJZvXdiZCVW4Qbhq\nI4w4kRWjHQkZ5OTwteKC93jNHXdxm6wV9VEFPC4ydNp+wRgZWglDu3fF6OcTe/Bn\ngj+B5qf+SPxs9Uwu3qAi4AfrKmE82MccPdZWCn/QsgBY1uG/MJIyh18SVlTE77Qx\njkdoAy45Y5lM01mLsFKA\n=T0P+\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 67840c2145fbf59d5aea1d07756968a7963abaa9\nparent e29071e4c9bf724f9679b7bcf2038d74cc44acd1\nauthor Won Park <won@openai.com> 1780426804 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780426804 -0700\n\nRoute standalone image generation through host finalization md (#25176)\n\n## Why\n\nStandalone image-generation extensions emitted turn items through the\nlow-level event path, bypassing host-owned finalization such as image\npersistence and contributor processing. At the same time, the\ngenerated-image save-path hint must remain visible to the model through\nthe extension tool's `FunctionCallOutput`, rather than the legacy\nbuilt-in developer-message path.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Extended `ExtensionTurnItem` to support image-generation items while\nkeeping the extension-facing emitter API limited to `emit_started` and\n`emit_completed`.\n- Routed extension completion through core `finalize_turn_item`, so\nstandalone image-generation items receive host-owned processing and\npersisted `saved_path` values before publication.\n- Kept legacy built-in image generation on its existing\ndeveloper-message hint path, while standalone image generation returns\nits deterministic saved-path hint in `FunctionCallOutput`.\n- Shared the image artifact path and output-hint formatting used by core\nand the image-generation extension.\n- Passed thread identity through extension tool calls so standalone\nimage generation can construct the same intended artifact path as core.\n- Added an app-server integration test covering real standalone image\ngeneration, saved artifact publication, model-visible output hint\nwiring, and absence of the legacy developer-message hint.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just fmt`\n- `just test -p codex-image-generation-extension`\n- `just test -p codex-web-search-extension`\n- `just test -p codex-goal-extension`\n- `just test -p codex-memories-extension`\n- Targeted `codex-core` tests for image save history, extension\ncompletion finalization, and contributor execution\n- `just test -p codex-app-server\nstandalone_image_generation_returns_saved_path_hint_to_model`\n- `just fix -p codex-core`\n- `just fix -p codex-image-generation-extension`\n- `just bazel-lock-update`\n- `just bazel-lock-check`","verified_at":"2026-06-02T19:00:05Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/57f337a8e90360649112f8fc01d9ee2f9f2afa24","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/57f337a8e90360649112f8fc01d9ee2f9f2afa24","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/57f337a8e90360649112f8fc01d9ee2f9f2afa24/comments","author":{"login":"won-openai","id":262224683,"node_id":"U_kgDOD6E7Kw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/262224683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/won-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"e29071e4c9bf724f9679b7bcf2038d74cc44acd1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e29071e4c9bf724f9679b7bcf2038d74cc44acd1","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/e29071e4c9bf724f9679b7bcf2038d74cc44acd1"}]},{"sha":"e29071e4c9bf724f9679b7bcf2038d74cc44acd1","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGUyOTA3MWU0YzliZjcyNGY5Njc5YjdiY2YyMDM4ZDc0Y2M0NGFjZDE","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-02T18:51:25Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-02T18:51:25Z"},"message":"Add environmentId to request_permissions (#25858)\n\n## Stack\n\n1. #25850 - Key request-permission grants by environment: stores and\napplies sticky permission grants per environment id.\n2. This PR (#25858) - Add `environmentId` to `request_permissions`: lets\nthe model target a selected environment and resolves relative permission\npaths against it.\n3. #25862 - Propagate permission approval environment id: carries the\nselected environment id through approval events, app-server requests,\nTUI prompts, and delegate forwarding.\n4. #25867 - Add remote request permissions integration coverage:\nverifies the selected remote environment across request, approval, grant\nreuse, and exec.\n\nThis PR is stacked on #25850; #25862 and #25867 are stacked on this PR.\n\n## Why\n\nPR1 made request-permission grants internally environment-keyed, but the\nmodel-facing `request_permissions` tool could still only target the\nprimary environment. For CCA and multi-environment turns, the tool needs\nan explicit way to bind a permission request to a selected attached\nenvironment before resolving relative paths.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Added optional `environmentId` to `RequestPermissionsArgs`, with\n`environment_id` accepted as an alias.\n- Exposed `environmentId` in the `request_permissions` tool schema and\ndescription.\n- Resolve the selected environment before parsing filesystem permission\npaths, so relative paths bind to the selected environment cwd.\n- Route validated tool calls through\n`request_permissions_for_environment` directly instead of duplicating\nenvironment lookup in `Session::request_permissions`.\n- Reject unknown environment ids with a model-facing error.\n- Updated focused request-permissions and Guardian call sites for the\nnew optional field.\n\n## Testing\n\nNot run locally per instruction.","tree":{"sha":"649f3de440fe29f5e5e049340707fa74dcdfd485","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/649f3de440fe29f5e5e049340707fa74dcdfd485"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/e29071e4c9bf724f9679b7bcf2038d74cc44acd1","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHyYtCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAd2YQAD5xG5yN4p9w7yQUHCS3MLFH\n1rXJi2xp5P9BRDUW3HMP6srOwp7Osf7ZqQV7UYGkHhC/9XP5To02Ny6ctOdmJrIY\nM1OgRCZ4LvykWLdjbolzeQxqOoRg0XVEzjaIzuwWf6mp0XCT/wRnumG+Wr8tn/kw\n/j8d6HR1SAzvs8obAAIxSt6u20NQSB0i42LfB+xLyADDLupvxpKwuAr+Ol8Suck1\nOdxdv0Q6nuERedWNzM/Rx/4JztciYzoAvUWIpfeTjAeEfolq52NFj1V/LlwQi2j0\nCXU26+bnrEIJNH8fUVauNd4MPDnQT16IOJh1wcDo/iTh46mhTJc1qvay0iMFpRUd\nj2BlOV6Bx6cLoloC242SzOO7X+8XIVHnj9uhm01ocCTVIajnkqX+7XvcGGm611pk\n/08shjwzdpft050h/rstnSLmzbW8uDCWP6SgwmW2Lnqz5O/Q7vQGSFmhhnOqQdEx\n9KTcldJqi1gM+EC6SVth7m83kGb7X7EcZsjrYb0FGokvPYxSMduEh8DCLCtC8fhB\nislW3v9tB2/GlGIQk5rknONC4wAULPw0kEpV5Ce2CtxvX+H+r9qedpCDlWhj4u4y\nm79uTLUxxGqq+G6//X3zwM/E9Sm10hcurePEeQCcaqi/oeupe5hZv0Li9ZXbLHic\nE4d5t2KqfqhrGxuh2MYD\n=TNIX\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 649f3de440fe29f5e5e049340707fa74dcdfd485\nparent 8e4b92d294c087423215a83b0e9c8282eedc9d12\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1780426285 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780426285 +0200\n\nAdd environmentId to request_permissions (#25858)\n\n## Stack\n\n1. #25850 - Key request-permission grants by environment: stores and\napplies sticky permission grants per environment id.\n2. This PR (#25858) - Add `environmentId` to `request_permissions`: lets\nthe model target a selected environment and resolves relative permission\npaths against it.\n3. #25862 - Propagate permission approval environment id: carries the\nselected environment id through approval events, app-server requests,\nTUI prompts, and delegate forwarding.\n4. #25867 - Add remote request permissions integration coverage:\nverifies the selected remote environment across request, approval, grant\nreuse, and exec.\n\nThis PR is stacked on #25850; #25862 and #25867 are stacked on this PR.\n\n## Why\n\nPR1 made request-permission grants internally environment-keyed, but the\nmodel-facing `request_permissions` tool could still only target the\nprimary environment. For CCA and multi-environment turns, the tool needs\nan explicit way to bind a permission request to a selected attached\nenvironment before resolving relative paths.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Added optional `environmentId` to `RequestPermissionsArgs`, with\n`environment_id` accepted as an alias.\n- Exposed `environmentId` in the `request_permissions` tool schema and\ndescription.\n- Resolve the selected environment before parsing filesystem permission\npaths, so relative paths bind to the selected environment cwd.\n- Route validated tool calls through\n`request_permissions_for_environment` directly instead of duplicating\nenvironment lookup in `Session::request_permissions`.\n- Reject unknown environment ids with a model-facing error.\n- Updated focused request-permissions and Guardian call sites for the\nnew optional field.\n\n## Testing\n\nNot run locally per instruction.","verified_at":"2026-06-02T18:51:26Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e29071e4c9bf724f9679b7bcf2038d74cc44acd1","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/e29071e4c9bf724f9679b7bcf2038d74cc44acd1","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e29071e4c9bf724f9679b7bcf2038d74cc44acd1/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"8e4b92d294c087423215a83b0e9c8282eedc9d12","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8e4b92d294c087423215a83b0e9c8282eedc9d12","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/8e4b92d294c087423215a83b0e9c8282eedc9d12"}]},{"sha":"8e4b92d294c087423215a83b0e9c8282eedc9d12","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDhlNGI5MmQyOTRjMDg3NDIzMjE1YTgzYjBlOWM4MjgyZWVkYzlkMTI","commit":{"author":{"name":"rhan-oai","email":"rhan@openai.com","date":"2026-06-02T18:40:35Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-02T18:40:35Z"},"message":"[codex-analytics] Track CodexErr details in turn analytics (#25707)\n\n## Summary\n- add analytics-only `CodexErr` telemetry to `codex_turn_event` while\nleaving existing `turn_error` unchanged\n- record terminal `CodexErr` facts from core immediately before the\nexisting turn error event is sent\n- emit source-truth `codex_error_*` fields for downstream analytics,\nincluding the raw `CodexErr::InvalidRequest(String)` message as\n`codex_error_subreason`\n\n## Validation\n- `just test -p codex-analytics`\n- attempted `just test -p codex-core`, but the local run timed out\nacross unrelated integration suites in this environment and is not being\nused as validation","tree":{"sha":"496b9152725e839fab7192e8c94ca973aa6c3a07","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/496b9152725e839fab7192e8c94ca973aa6c3a07"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/8e4b92d294c087423215a83b0e9c8282eedc9d12","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHyOjCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA8MwQAEP4cd2TZEZ05rhMoOsGpa2n\nAsykmrHgoqcvGWlXG/vFp6+7fLaQTFc3g9aKm706+ZILjqtVd0mDL1lIBgx22AZh\nns5yZVQ9QxFdAoiu+9LLFTnIbmlCGPsSDpMFQ78ngKrsUAHG9wGL5rbxsQCMH7gB\n6jUUP32nV6wT4IKP3dQIoIaIo0Xj/t7kgKPv7tUpL6XYrKmPEtqb5eap4r2xKVB0\ngKL3s5E2AGPo9D87vOhHajYHFQcVs2kCNI6OBoji2mnHfNfzIYMpIFAy9w5f4vmj\nAQgh8oJaDXEZKCy/1CPD/S1w89imHjL88XmpCq7Qm7CPPcWANDmgYensI8FAxURM\nvoRPOS3Xm3ZbZcIZpbuaEZ1YbOlfhUsYgMXv0PeirQSK0p+68wKF/Yq+wEeaPFRk\nqQZrOCPV8t4n9aDdxfLbnu5hZx8LmMRctbDbRTuj72ddAejyDh/cI1TNAZt/tk1j\nHq2ZeG6me4SGsKXmffkB2wqWbAc8KSqLFRuitfLSrbLRSlyIlGeGl4DPdn98ZNMp\nmxHjAnB87+rQCseqlfbwObOZ5m37EDVuaMXUL15VeTFm4zThbh4hXAqOoaWIpPyR\njLcFH6EfVH0L5oXC5xc5dcRiwJDNCkZCxZnVL3qFyiPvS8gSnHnXv6hcgs81541b\nw/Z7gqxd3OrCu5MvM3TA\n=v2ky\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 496b9152725e839fab7192e8c94ca973aa6c3a07\nparent 503ec190a88da1dfa43294a98ef5530769095778\nauthor rhan-oai <rhan@openai.com> 1780425635 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780425635 -0700\n\n[codex-analytics] Track CodexErr details in turn analytics (#25707)\n\n## Summary\n- add analytics-only `CodexErr` telemetry to `codex_turn_event` while\nleaving existing `turn_error` unchanged\n- record terminal `CodexErr` facts from core immediately before the\nexisting turn error event is sent\n- emit source-truth `codex_error_*` fields for downstream analytics,\nincluding the raw `CodexErr::InvalidRequest(String)` message as\n`codex_error_subreason`\n\n## Validation\n- `just test -p codex-analytics`\n- attempted `just test -p codex-core`, but the local run timed out\nacross unrelated integration suites in this environment and is not being\nused as validation","verified_at":"2026-06-02T18:40:35Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8e4b92d294c087423215a83b0e9c8282eedc9d12","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/8e4b92d294c087423215a83b0e9c8282eedc9d12","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8e4b92d294c087423215a83b0e9c8282eedc9d12/comments","author":{"login":"rhan-oai","id":214716640,"node_id":"U_kgDODMxQ4A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/214716640?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/rhan-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"503ec190a88da1dfa43294a98ef5530769095778","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/503ec190a88da1dfa43294a98ef5530769095778","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/503ec190a88da1dfa43294a98ef5530769095778"}]},{"sha":"503ec190a88da1dfa43294a98ef5530769095778","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDUwM2VjMTkwYTg4ZGExZGZhNDMyOTRhOThlZjU1MzA3NjkwOTU3Nzg","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-02T18:16:57Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-02T18:16:57Z"},"message":"Key request-permission grants by environment (#25850)\n\n## Stack\n\n1. This PR (#25850) - Key request-permission grants by environment:\nstores and applies sticky permission grants per environment id.\n2. #25858 - Add `environmentId` to `request_permissions`: lets the model\ntarget a selected environment and resolves relative permission paths\nagainst it.\n3. #25862 - Propagate permission approval environment id: carries the\nselected environment id through approval events, app-server requests,\nTUI prompts, and delegate forwarding.\n4. #25867 - Add remote request permissions integration coverage:\nverifies the selected remote environment across request, approval, grant\nreuse, and exec.\n\n#25858, #25862, and #25867 are stacked on this PR and should be reviewed\nafter it.\n\n## Why\n\nMulti-environment CCA turns can attach both local and remote executors,\nbut request-permission grants were still effectively cwd-only. Pending\npermission requests tracked a cwd, while stored turn/session grants had\nno environment identity, so sticky grants could be reused through the\nwrong executor context.\n\nThis makes the first permission-grant step environment-aware without\nchanging the external `request_permissions` payload shape: omitted\nenvironment targeting remains bound to the primary turn environment.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Store turn- and session-scoped request-permission grants by\n`environment_id`.\n- Keep the selected `TurnEnvironmentSelection` with pending\n`request_permissions` calls so approval responses normalize and record\ngrants against the same environment.\n- Resolve relative `request_permissions` file paths against the primary\nturn environment cwd instead of deprecated `turn.cwd`.\n- Apply sticky grants in `shell`, `exec_command`, and `apply_patch` by\nselected environment id while still using the actual tool cwd for\ncwd-relative permission materialization.\n- Update Guardian and request-permissions coverage for the\nenvironment-keyed grant behavior.\n\n## Testing\n\nNot run locally. Added or updated focused coverage for:\n\n- `request_permission_grants_are_environment_keyed`\n-\n`request_permissions_tool_resolves_relative_paths_against_primary_environment`\n- related Guardian/request-permissions sticky grant tests","tree":{"sha":"f230dfef5f51c75a119ba8774d2490c809848ff5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/f230dfef5f51c75a119ba8774d2490c809848ff5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/503ec190a88da1dfa43294a98ef5530769095778","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHx4ZCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAuOEQAEdPPiL0ktS7lDvILKTXL5PO\nwD+uVWPC6+N814Syy4K4x5Ankc6Egm4TalLlAspqFBlYVG7sDmNepl2gvt3NTxqo\nUs239jcH1pXk1J/e9QqTBWIbNlt98YQmMUVf6wW1l2DCSkSOFQBHoFLlNa64gSjl\nRp1j2GNnedQLhHsb8MLkRUnPOqKJn8iNvYHMCbUkWdFFlJUAlCZyCpjsLwYAJYV/\nBODa1F3o1JUKq8ZQJFMsCzh/CPxDjEQxTwKhcMvjVWqJ/HG6cL/V0gU/clpFNjwm\nfOo4xIa0/Iygw6KxeV18BwW1JgKaNM32H3wo7btAfYmUnqpC5mSngryruYmI4Q9X\nNSytR+H7J7Mk+Fs0M9Vb8qs/wGBW/tyPHpa9nddvfhnxCaG1UZWpVNY/DW03EUNB\nfnEfUQOHzW84mPT4+SRohQ8LqnGTipc5owHCxH+eYp5DJGfiwLdx6qVJ1XXlwlVS\nEeYDppnvfTD3C1UplQzOQLZpUoKyhFC4sMy5XfHGZCEk7SoCxvlsb4e2xBRwJS8p\ncgW80KpPLJ1xjKvSiuCduyqKMl7rzbm46tiWro2JNPPK2+yPlxks9n3IqsXWcHdg\nF1KRWv7ZVkyWBazhG9o9u3oCkTPuNzXf6dpBTo4VNypxsJKlojjSCHYapR4i2Ueg\nMqG49VGqgyJRW3RUyn6K\n=BDud\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree f230dfef5f51c75a119ba8774d2490c809848ff5\nparent 9e3d5f29e2b6e2bcad3b0384e35e1faaa13e8272\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1780424217 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780424217 +0200\n\nKey request-permission grants by environment (#25850)\n\n## Stack\n\n1. This PR (#25850) - Key request-permission grants by environment:\nstores and applies sticky permission grants per environment id.\n2. #25858 - Add `environmentId` to `request_permissions`: lets the model\ntarget a selected environment and resolves relative permission paths\nagainst it.\n3. #25862 - Propagate permission approval environment id: carries the\nselected environment id through approval events, app-server requests,\nTUI prompts, and delegate forwarding.\n4. #25867 - Add remote request permissions integration coverage:\nverifies the selected remote environment across request, approval, grant\nreuse, and exec.\n\n#25858, #25862, and #25867 are stacked on this PR and should be reviewed\nafter it.\n\n## Why\n\nMulti-environment CCA turns can attach both local and remote executors,\nbut request-permission grants were still effectively cwd-only. Pending\npermission requests tracked a cwd, while stored turn/session grants had\nno environment identity, so sticky grants could be reused through the\nwrong executor context.\n\nThis makes the first permission-grant step environment-aware without\nchanging the external `request_permissions` payload shape: omitted\nenvironment targeting remains bound to the primary turn environment.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Store turn- and session-scoped request-permission grants by\n`environment_id`.\n- Keep the selected `TurnEnvironmentSelection` with pending\n`request_permissions` calls so approval responses normalize and record\ngrants against the same environment.\n- Resolve relative `request_permissions` file paths against the primary\nturn environment cwd instead of deprecated `turn.cwd`.\n- Apply sticky grants in `shell`, `exec_command`, and `apply_patch` by\nselected environment id while still using the actual tool cwd for\ncwd-relative permission materialization.\n- Update Guardian and request-permissions coverage for the\nenvironment-keyed grant behavior.\n\n## Testing\n\nNot run locally. Added or updated focused coverage for:\n\n- `request_permission_grants_are_environment_keyed`\n-\n`request_permissions_tool_resolves_relative_paths_against_primary_environment`\n- related Guardian/request-permissions sticky grant tests","verified_at":"2026-06-02T18:16:57Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/503ec190a88da1dfa43294a98ef5530769095778","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/503ec190a88da1dfa43294a98ef5530769095778","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/503ec190a88da1dfa43294a98ef5530769095778/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"9e3d5f29e2b6e2bcad3b0384e35e1faaa13e8272","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/9e3d5f29e2b6e2bcad3b0384e35e1faaa13e8272","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/9e3d5f29e2b6e2bcad3b0384e35e1faaa13e8272"}]},{"sha":"9e3d5f29e2b6e2bcad3b0384e35e1faaa13e8272","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDllM2Q1ZjI5ZTJiNmUyYmNhZDNiMDM4NGUzNWUxZmFhYTEzZTgyNzI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Adam Perry @ OpenAI","email":"anp@openai.com","date":"2026-06-02T18:06:01Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-02T18:06:01Z"},"message":"[codex] Revert shared BuildBuddy Bazel wrapper (#25909)\n\n## Why\n\nPR #25905 intentionally adds a failing `codex-core` unit test, but its\n[Bazel test on Windows\ncheck](https://github.com/openai/codex/actions/runs/26837526950/job/79135369259)\npassed. That shows the Bazel configuration introduced by #25156 is not\nbehaving as expected, so revert it while the configuration can be\ninvestigated separately.\n\n## What changed\n\nRevert #25156 in full, restoring the previous Bazel remote\nconfiguration, CI scripts, workflows, `rusty_v8` handling, and\ndocumentation. This removes the shared BuildBuddy wrapper and its tests.\n\n## Validation\n\nNot run locally; this exact revert was prioritized for a fast rollback.","tree":{"sha":"5fa4e62dd340b506df1eab3f69e0ad661da28204","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/5fa4e62dd340b506df1eab3f69e0ad661da28204"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/9e3d5f29e2b6e2bcad3b0384e35e1faaa13e8272","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHxuJCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAA60QAJE2E0A0DnSELHD3WVyQs+8t\nqIMnQRA71BMJXNjvIS0ZwdVdKslHBKBpCxkNH5Dc/XOeNqs181Tic2+IkVOvYRdc\npYUQQasl5DH9+ll8lpUzBbXdlFxYo2WmrDE88QWABejiwx3GH2fFsPg/9bH8j/Tm\nD0M+w/HdB2VchHzv5ZVxr6qcP7m7An2SZ6bQuuc1SpjEylxoaiFpAExnxhS2QNMq\nGLR9EZzLa4L2HOe2QCY6PDJv9tZFLUr4wJln8tXVrh1Z7LB0e1evNoj2XnbFL1vU\nsAc0PxW/tI89aOprX4hwZOt+5hP6XSZEBOP9ccIwPdiwSSEF+b1EojgfleuWrzGH\nPw+p/kzYxVxvkq11VJr51uGjlOOTBF0tuHfp/RwqkCNkkGep4fdTy7T1538tG9we\ngAZEWrYdlLO8ZkH0FmtZNp9jtTyXeJcPInXNfEfN9AevVwMEbBklyOoKJChHIRsu\nfClD8whiZMR6DXCmXncnBzl7iCA/xguEpKXtxW7jR4owjifnR0Fw0fuIb2G24GsB\nftZoMc6wbt/10ee8crd+/eYbSqL7uKaHEwnxr+iqi9H07GXCY+q1zaSZU2MmoY/8\nraqxMRXLD6AIALB4uw+RoXvt6TMEFeYhHIeFh3Y1XrjR/DL4jYhYSEQfiA5OLOS4\nLXm2ELtsQnms2xE/tGoe\n=ecOD\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 5fa4e62dd340b506df1eab3f69e0ad661da28204\nparent 593df8773d8deeff7d778fe39b59420ce293d7a5\nauthor Adam Perry @ OpenAI <anp@openai.com> 1780423561 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780423561 -0700\n\n[codex] Revert shared BuildBuddy Bazel wrapper (#25909)\n\n## Why\n\nPR #25905 intentionally adds a failing `codex-core` unit test, but its\n[Bazel test on Windows\ncheck](https://github.com/openai/codex/actions/runs/26837526950/job/79135369259)\npassed. That shows the Bazel configuration introduced by #25156 is not\nbehaving as expected, so revert it while the configuration can be\ninvestigated separately.\n\n## What changed\n\nRevert #25156 in full, restoring the previous Bazel remote\nconfiguration, CI scripts, workflows, `rusty_v8` handling, and\ndocumentation. This removes the shared BuildBuddy wrapper and its tests.\n\n## Validation\n\nNot run locally; this exact revert was prioritized for a fast rollback.","verified_at":"2026-06-02T18:06:02Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/9e3d5f29e2b6e2bcad3b0384e35e1faaa13e8272","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/9e3d5f29e2b6e2bcad3b0384e35e1faaa13e8272","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/9e3d5f29e2b6e2bcad3b0384e35e1faaa13e8272/comments","author":{"login":"anp-oai","id":286154589,"node_id":"U_kgDOEQ5fXQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/286154589?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/anp-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"593df8773d8deeff7d778fe39b59420ce293d7a5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/593df8773d8deeff7d778fe39b59420ce293d7a5","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/593df8773d8deeff7d778fe39b59420ce293d7a5"}]},{"sha":"593df8773d8deeff7d778fe39b59420ce293d7a5","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDU5M2RmODc3M2Q4ZGVlZmY3ZDc3OGZlMzliNTk0MjBjZTI5M2Q3YTU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Michael Bolin","email":"mbolin@openai.com","date":"2026-06-02T17:57:35Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-02T17:57:35Z"},"message":"core: derive built-in permission profiles from raw policies (#25739)\n\n## Why\n\nPermission profiles that extend a built-in profile should behave like\nother TOML inheritance: parent entries provide defaults, and child keys\noverride matching fields before the profile is compiled.\n\nThat was not true for `:workspace`. Previously, a profile with `extends\n= \":workspace\"` seeded the compiled runtime\n`PermissionProfile::workspace_write()` policy and then appended child\nfilesystem entries. A child override such as `\":tmpdir\" = \"read\"`\ntherefore left the inherited `\":tmpdir\" = \"write\"` entry in the final\npolicy. Since same-target `write` wins over `read` during runtime\nresolution, the child override was ineffective.\n\nThis also needs a clear source of truth for the built-in profiles. The\nprotocol-level sandbox policy constructors now define the raw built-in\nfilesystem entries, and both `PermissionProfile` presets and\nconfig-profile inheritance derive from those same values.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Add a canonical `FileSystemSandboxPolicy::read_only()` constructor\nwhile keeping the read-only and workspace-write raw filesystem entries\nexplicit and independent.\n- Derive `PermissionProfile::read_only()` from\n`FileSystemSandboxPolicy::read_only()`;\n`PermissionProfile::workspace_write()` continues to derive from\n`FileSystemSandboxPolicy::workspace_write()`.\n- Build extensible `:read-only` and `:workspace` parent profiles by\nprojecting those canonical sandbox policies into\n`PermissionProfileToml`, then merge user overrides at the TOML layer\nbefore compilation.\n- Add config parsing support for `:slash_tmp` so the built-in\n`:workspace` parent can be expressed in the same TOML-shaped filesystem\ntable as user profiles.\n- Document that `PermissionsToml::resolve_profile()` returns an\nalready-merged `PermissionProfileToml`, and return that profile directly\nafter removing the resolved-profile wrapper.\n- Extend the config test for `extends = \":workspace\"` to assert that\ninherited `\":slash_tmp\" = \"write\"` is preserved and that a child\n`\":tmpdir\" = \"read\"` entry replaces the inherited `write` entry.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `just test -p codex-config`\n- `just test -p codex-protocol`\n- `just test -p codex-core\npermissions_profiles_resolve_extends_parent_first_with_child_overrides`\n- `just test -p codex-core\ndefault_permissions_profile_can_extend_builtin_workspace`\n- `just test -p codex-core`\n  - Result: 2596 passed, 4 failed, 1 timed out.\n- The failures were existing sandbox/environment-sensitive tests\nunrelated to this permissions change:\n\n`suite::user_shell_cmd::user_shell_command_does_not_set_network_sandbox_env_var`,\n\n`suite::user_shell_cmd::user_shell_command_history_is_persisted_and_shared_with_model`,\n\n`suite::abort_tasks::interrupt_persists_turn_aborted_marker_in_next_request`,\n    `suite::abort_tasks::interrupt_tool_records_history_entries`, and\n\n`thread_manager::tests::start_thread_uses_all_default_environments_from_codex_home`.","tree":{"sha":"dbea88c2413f1a712f64a9e46b130e72e084a82b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/dbea88c2413f1a712f64a9e46b130e72e084a82b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/593df8773d8deeff7d778fe39b59420ce293d7a5","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHxmPCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAq7oQAHIXhU2eBi/IqQ3Sk2cd+cT8\nFJ+YA4a6NDoKLx1pMEQTWisQbF+r8j0RlokTSIByGFJHQ/mH4qmCwis41W1SuRmv\naMoN/gYH8C8ZZXkRVGb2XTu5BbYA/vKin2zs0AnUYyNSro5ZkEgmlW+T8AmmC0AU\nOJFMpKqSsXRaQtZEbIUSe2lreiAWlFbZ5ZZ8R4UGRQbblfR2tiNF3SahJix7pvnq\nqtLo9q4dWSxS0Ho43z06KCMBJUHRW7U80wCkS0Vy8WghQ3uVcpiCOZADCTWeHCoB\nniGK7NJujeArfiKPIkHWQjhvp301fa2pTxBV94SlwRNtvUEbXYIzP8W9m2wPBBht\nEp+2ICEoWM+yInU+3cjfT8kMB8fFO5z/7ZEzRc/W3xeXC0AFKdJJBdDh1DCejV6S\ntrbcGcb3YZHZPMEETg3f8u3zYolOLJ1Wur3oyV3QwvNxGfSUTbC+spVUvE2QUtoo\nk/LHBuhlqMjs7DB1Q6dcNyFCOinZTg6orZkMFMAQtJNTrwdMd2dUmdxGj1hKJ2rs\nleDMvKN+W5v33P3Mtq5wgN38G7xiUbUhoEv4iqEO64n5cyJLdPgWzmqeJKotfZvY\nLQ9qdmSUfzklrMIqnSI0Lz3EOo+GDTdfyhi8CvslLG+cm7HUS+M3mdQtErE2kfBr\n+sIq4kAk0KRwTek2haZA\n=knq5\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree dbea88c2413f1a712f64a9e46b130e72e084a82b\nparent ebb79803697acee75baf24073ef49af87ad7e483\nauthor Michael Bolin <mbolin@openai.com> 1780423055 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780423055 -0700\n\ncore: derive built-in permission profiles from raw policies (#25739)\n\n## Why\n\nPermission profiles that extend a built-in profile should behave like\nother TOML inheritance: parent entries provide defaults, and child keys\noverride matching fields before the profile is compiled.\n\nThat was not true for `:workspace`. Previously, a profile with `extends\n= \":workspace\"` seeded the compiled runtime\n`PermissionProfile::workspace_write()` policy and then appended child\nfilesystem entries. A child override such as `\":tmpdir\" = \"read\"`\ntherefore left the inherited `\":tmpdir\" = \"write\"` entry in the final\npolicy. Since same-target `write` wins over `read` during runtime\nresolution, the child override was ineffective.\n\nThis also needs a clear source of truth for the built-in profiles. The\nprotocol-level sandbox policy constructors now define the raw built-in\nfilesystem entries, and both `PermissionProfile` presets and\nconfig-profile inheritance derive from those same values.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Add a canonical `FileSystemSandboxPolicy::read_only()` constructor\nwhile keeping the read-only and workspace-write raw filesystem entries\nexplicit and independent.\n- Derive `PermissionProfile::read_only()` from\n`FileSystemSandboxPolicy::read_only()`;\n`PermissionProfile::workspace_write()` continues to derive from\n`FileSystemSandboxPolicy::workspace_write()`.\n- Build extensible `:read-only` and `:workspace` parent profiles by\nprojecting those canonical sandbox policies into\n`PermissionProfileToml`, then merge user overrides at the TOML layer\nbefore compilation.\n- Add config parsing support for `:slash_tmp` so the built-in\n`:workspace` parent can be expressed in the same TOML-shaped filesystem\ntable as user profiles.\n- Document that `PermissionsToml::resolve_profile()` returns an\nalready-merged `PermissionProfileToml`, and return that profile directly\nafter removing the resolved-profile wrapper.\n- Extend the config test for `extends = \":workspace\"` to assert that\ninherited `\":slash_tmp\" = \"write\"` is preserved and that a child\n`\":tmpdir\" = \"read\"` entry replaces the inherited `write` entry.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `just test -p codex-config`\n- `just test -p codex-protocol`\n- `just test -p codex-core\npermissions_profiles_resolve_extends_parent_first_with_child_overrides`\n- `just test -p codex-core\ndefault_permissions_profile_can_extend_builtin_workspace`\n- `just test -p codex-core`\n  - Result: 2596 passed, 4 failed, 1 timed out.\n- The failures were existing sandbox/environment-sensitive tests\nunrelated to this permissions change:\n\n`suite::user_shell_cmd::user_shell_command_does_not_set_network_sandbox_env_var`,\n\n`suite::user_shell_cmd::user_shell_command_history_is_persisted_and_shared_with_model`,\n\n`suite::abort_tasks::interrupt_persists_turn_aborted_marker_in_next_request`,\n    `suite::abort_tasks::interrupt_tool_records_history_entries`, and\n\n`thread_manager::tests::start_thread_uses_all_default_environments_from_codex_home`.","verified_at":"2026-06-02T17:57:36Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/593df8773d8deeff7d778fe39b59420ce293d7a5","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/593df8773d8deeff7d778fe39b59420ce293d7a5","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/593df8773d8deeff7d778fe39b59420ce293d7a5/comments","author":{"login":"bolinfest","id":655869,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTg2OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/655869?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest","html_url":"https://github.com/bolinfest","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"ebb79803697acee75baf24073ef49af87ad7e483","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ebb79803697acee75baf24073ef49af87ad7e483","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/ebb79803697acee75baf24073ef49af87ad7e483"}]},{"sha":"ebb79803697acee75baf24073ef49af87ad7e483","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGViYjc5ODAzNjk3YWNlZTc1YmFmMjQwNzNlZjQ5YWY4N2FkN2U0ODM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Adam Perry @ OpenAI","email":"anp@openai.com","date":"2026-06-02T16:56:20Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-02T16:56:20Z"},"message":"Route Bazel CI through shared BuildBuddy remote config wrapper (#25156)\n\n## Why\n\nBazel remote configuration was selected in several CI scripts and\nworkflow steps. That made the BuildBuddy tenant policy easy to duplicate\nand harder to audit, especially for fork pull requests that must not use\nthe OpenAI tenant.\n\nThis builds on\n[sluongng/buildbuddy-ci-host-routing](https://github.com/openai/codex/compare/main...sluongng:codex:sluongng/buildbuddy-ci-host-routing)\nand consolidates the policy in one place.\n\n## What to do if this breaks you\n\nSee `codex-rs/docs/bazel.md` for details. TLDR:\n\n1. make a BuildBuddy API key and put it in `~/.bazelrc`\n2. if you're an OpenAI employee, add `common\n--config=buildbuddy-openai-rbe` to `user.bazelrc` in the repo root\n\nRun `just bazel-test` to ensure it works.\n\nNote that `just bazel-remote-test` no longer exists, you need to select\na remote configuration as documented to use RBE.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Add `.github/scripts/run_bazel_with_buildbuddy.py` as the shared Bazel\nwrapper and Python library. It selects the OpenAI host only for trusted\nupstream GitHub Actions runs, routes keyed fork runs to the generic\nhost, and falls back to local Bazel execution when no key is available.\n- Move endpoint selection into explicit `.bazelrc` configurations and\nupdate Bazel CI, query helpers, and `rusty_v8` staging to use the shared\npolicy. Loading-phase target-discovery queries remain local.\n- Add wrapper and `rusty_v8` unit coverage, plus `just test-scripts` for\nthe `.github/scripts` Python tests.\n- Document local Bazel usage, `user.bazelrc` setup, BuildBuddy\nconfigurations, and CI behavior in `codex-rs/docs/bazel.md`.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test-scripts`\n- `bash -n .github/scripts/run-bazel-ci.sh\n.github/scripts/run-bazel-query-ci.sh\n.github/scripts/run-argument-comment-lint-bazel.sh\nscripts/list-bazel-clippy-targets.sh`\n- `python3 -m py_compile .github/scripts/run_bazel_with_buildbuddy.py\n.github/scripts/test_run_bazel_with_buildbuddy.py\n.github/scripts/test_rusty_v8_bazel.py\n.github/scripts/rusty_v8_bazel.py`\n- `ruff check .github/scripts/run_bazel_with_buildbuddy.py\n.github/scripts/test_run_bazel_with_buildbuddy.py\n.github/scripts/test_rusty_v8_bazel.py\n.github/scripts/rusty_v8_bazel.py`","tree":{"sha":"2d0a0c554c8ffebe952413a1d1992ae86f55ec52","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/2d0a0c554c8ffebe952413a1d1992ae86f55ec52"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/ebb79803697acee75baf24073ef49af87ad7e483","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHws1CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA6LAQAFPxIEIszY8pYXOKoLbUpCZw\nmwXstuwehrMvvjwq9YwYBWIZ3hwWRYqO2tYY7oaeMERiJHJeAQ57DaHnfrZHI+jr\nXV/yAG2un42g3aUAbG+18S4DdiwzSxWOvrDu1v0QsZdX56o6N1gph1Yb0BUEciKp\nuZp1C8lN7B7esaeeuyaUVQ8HasNm4dR2pv44vceJtr5OF9ePuc7zyDgGKe9yCv30\nwW9I2oOeFc3MisrRahXBLreZ4WCrBgp2GI6c+L1AwwUzsHsyC8L2iUJubwg6ppeI\nMzAWhAjEHoO9bXJbLobCVB+F3HpLv9McGTy/PGMAHlrzCOkmHW6SRdHCvAkuA64Y\nb3KLVQrufN5njH/brrPgoTz3Sp7nI+s5bNRrx2DKhljDimdvokl0jj5C4+1XMPhP\n6lSI7cNyf8Da0oEAkRPelQbfgqNIX1S8WRtK74E4Rt4eypNwfXqZcjHcJUASaZKw\nZAx7lAn5JJWQ1hi2M8sBC3V35AlEmi35YrYuLy/h4kZnujP7Swfu/ihsXv+mQVBj\n3u/F3gQawVq9Vhck3mMrEZiNELZVzctfGmHRMrWLELgiPuhnxUyFWT4iPd8ffzxK\nuw5NGPTt8b8FyhnXbHHIhdBZf5wzN+zpjO3RxuABAaSwF4kV4HywiDgfGEI3M1Ab\n9SoxYu088JV95CySG6Wq\n=Dhjv\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 2d0a0c554c8ffebe952413a1d1992ae86f55ec52\nparent 859dbe27616c593238bad63be63e13a2d80579d9\nauthor Adam Perry @ OpenAI <anp@openai.com> 1780419380 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780419380 -0700\n\nRoute Bazel CI through shared BuildBuddy remote config wrapper (#25156)\n\n## Why\n\nBazel remote configuration was selected in several CI scripts and\nworkflow steps. That made the BuildBuddy tenant policy easy to duplicate\nand harder to audit, especially for fork pull requests that must not use\nthe OpenAI tenant.\n\nThis builds on\n[sluongng/buildbuddy-ci-host-routing](https://github.com/openai/codex/compare/main...sluongng:codex:sluongng/buildbuddy-ci-host-routing)\nand consolidates the policy in one place.\n\n## What to do if this breaks you\n\nSee `codex-rs/docs/bazel.md` for details. TLDR:\n\n1. make a BuildBuddy API key and put it in `~/.bazelrc`\n2. if you're an OpenAI employee, add `common\n--config=buildbuddy-openai-rbe` to `user.bazelrc` in the repo root\n\nRun `just bazel-test` to ensure it works.\n\nNote that `just bazel-remote-test` no longer exists, you need to select\na remote configuration as documented to use RBE.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Add `.github/scripts/run_bazel_with_buildbuddy.py` as the shared Bazel\nwrapper and Python library. It selects the OpenAI host only for trusted\nupstream GitHub Actions runs, routes keyed fork runs to the generic\nhost, and falls back to local Bazel execution when no key is available.\n- Move endpoint selection into explicit `.bazelrc` configurations and\nupdate Bazel CI, query helpers, and `rusty_v8` staging to use the shared\npolicy. Loading-phase target-discovery queries remain local.\n- Add wrapper and `rusty_v8` unit coverage, plus `just test-scripts` for\nthe `.github/scripts` Python tests.\n- Document local Bazel usage, `user.bazelrc` setup, BuildBuddy\nconfigurations, and CI behavior in `codex-rs/docs/bazel.md`.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test-scripts`\n- `bash -n .github/scripts/run-bazel-ci.sh\n.github/scripts/run-bazel-query-ci.sh\n.github/scripts/run-argument-comment-lint-bazel.sh\nscripts/list-bazel-clippy-targets.sh`\n- `python3 -m py_compile .github/scripts/run_bazel_with_buildbuddy.py\n.github/scripts/test_run_bazel_with_buildbuddy.py\n.github/scripts/test_rusty_v8_bazel.py\n.github/scripts/rusty_v8_bazel.py`\n- `ruff check .github/scripts/run_bazel_with_buildbuddy.py\n.github/scripts/test_run_bazel_with_buildbuddy.py\n.github/scripts/test_rusty_v8_bazel.py\n.github/scripts/rusty_v8_bazel.py`","verified_at":"2026-06-02T16:56:21Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ebb79803697acee75baf24073ef49af87ad7e483","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/ebb79803697acee75baf24073ef49af87ad7e483","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ebb79803697acee75baf24073ef49af87ad7e483/comments","author":{"login":"anp-oai","id":286154589,"node_id":"U_kgDOEQ5fXQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/286154589?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/anp-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"859dbe27616c593238bad63be63e13a2d80579d9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/859dbe27616c593238bad63be63e13a2d80579d9","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/859dbe27616c593238bad63be63e13a2d80579d9"}]},{"sha":"859dbe27616c593238bad63be63e13a2d80579d9","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDg1OWRiZTI3NjE2YzU5MzIzOGJhZDYzYmU2M2UxM2EyZDgwNTc5ZDk","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-02T15:27:30Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-02T15:27:30Z"},"message":"Skip startup prewarm when websockets are disabled (#25868)\n\n## Summary\n- skip startup websocket prewarm setup when the model client has\nResponses-over-WebSocket disabled\n- avoid making HTTP-only sessions build prewarm prompt/tool state that\ncannot produce a reusable websocket session\n\n## Why\nRecent macOS timing flakes were timing out while waiting for first-turn\nevents in HTTP-only core tests. Startup prewarm is only useful for\nwebsocket-capable providers, but it was scheduled for every session. For\nHTTP-only test providers this added unnecessary async startup work\nbefore the regular turn could reach the mocked response flow.\n\n## Testing\n- bazel test //codex-rs/core:core-all-test\n--test_filter=suite::auto_review::remote_model_override_uses_catalog_model_for_strict_auto_review\n--test_output=errors\n- bazel test //codex-rs/core:core-all-test\n--test_filter=suite::request_permissions_tool::approved_folder_write_request_permissions_unblocks_later_apply_patch\n--test_output=errors","tree":{"sha":"a123e064fc8a24098cc4c5cd560f87d02567d7ca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/a123e064fc8a24098cc4c5cd560f87d02567d7ca"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/859dbe27616c593238bad63be63e13a2d80579d9","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHvZiCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAANJ8QAEtWHc793Jq+OENAXueSGsFv\nh2xCTZaQLoRQ0Xlz6ngIfXGpOxHA/1h2TUmgw2pJjr/9BWnzrvRncxlozoNceTtd\nhKYmffxmv1+bUb7hTvcqbpUQsRpXL208CkPdtSkIBvTrdh70woAEHIvpMRXvzXv1\nzNKbFGJ6Tuzwi8k/g7sHBEVYA/k97BKetlJ6FBGoF5qgpNZy4EnrZzB+ly9w9aSF\n6cGwcX8af2pf9+PyRUcMYaQBfNJdFXFzYaywWh29SzceyfNlt/B+JdkxpcGq1oXG\nQYC/kFm9J6UUqyhrZJn4E2vkexeh3wTvK/SzHiX7tt10tyAHQA7/ySJl1cAB8zg+\nMELr1QdGZPMkwR3vhvCt8yZ8/f7RjBZ1wnMRL1kY7oIjhYb+qc32yNTc4CDzzHWI\nMTNN/zOASVDlhhOewNInv5i/qCazi3SkdLrbAUajCxuNdf6Mvq5qKVYdzw8NRnO9\n67rF0OixXLHp+LQynYkdGQchHQdoXGU/8RJ6KE9mNaQ7hsFd5Z+FfTmj4SwhvzA5\ntnl1mdN4ZfiUKT+J2LzWjzf2qIB9CJHUDURvHksrQOBSN4F/1pkrW0yCBlhgiWpS\npyf85DjBe7R/ILpaLoEb3MKuA7CkKiu0G3Wztt/En9kLFsPci0TteACcO9O6517S\nYfL35KIKSqB/M6l8vXy0\n=lbX5\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a123e064fc8a24098cc4c5cd560f87d02567d7ca\nparent 4d80d808b4425fa31e086985264385b02e98932e\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1780414050 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780414050 +0200\n\nSkip startup prewarm when websockets are disabled (#25868)\n\n## Summary\n- skip startup websocket prewarm setup when the model client has\nResponses-over-WebSocket disabled\n- avoid making HTTP-only sessions build prewarm prompt/tool state that\ncannot produce a reusable websocket session\n\n## Why\nRecent macOS timing flakes were timing out while waiting for first-turn\nevents in HTTP-only core tests. Startup prewarm is only useful for\nwebsocket-capable providers, but it was scheduled for every session. For\nHTTP-only test providers this added unnecessary async startup work\nbefore the regular turn could reach the mocked response flow.\n\n## Testing\n- bazel test //codex-rs/core:core-all-test\n--test_filter=suite::auto_review::remote_model_override_uses_catalog_model_for_strict_auto_review\n--test_output=errors\n- bazel test //codex-rs/core:core-all-test\n--test_filter=suite::request_permissions_tool::approved_folder_write_request_permissions_unblocks_later_apply_patch\n--test_output=errors","verified_at":"2026-06-02T15:27:31Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/859dbe27616c593238bad63be63e13a2d80579d9","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/859dbe27616c593238bad63be63e13a2d80579d9","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/859dbe27616c593238bad63be63e13a2d80579d9/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"4d80d808b4425fa31e086985264385b02e98932e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4d80d808b4425fa31e086985264385b02e98932e","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/4d80d808b4425fa31e086985264385b02e98932e"}]},{"sha":"4d80d808b4425fa31e086985264385b02e98932e","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDRkODBkODA4YjQ0MjVmYTMxZTA4Njk4NTI2NDM4NWIwMmU5ODkzMmU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Alex Zamoshchin","email":"alexz@openai.com","date":"2026-06-02T15:04:11Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-02T15:04:11Z"},"message":"[app-server][core] Add connector-level Guardian reviewer overrides (#25167)\n\nContext: https://openai.slack.com/archives/C0B4JAF0Q2C/p1779912328647229\n\n```\napprovals_reviewer = \"auto_review\"\n\n[apps.connector_5f3c8c41a1e54ad7a76272c89e2554fa]\nenabled = true\napprovals_reviewer = \"user\"\ndefault_tools_approval_mode = \"prompt\"\n```\n\n<img width=\"230\" height=\"84\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-05-31 at 11 56 34 AM\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e319f8f7-0983-42a7-98cd-3302732fa406\"\n/>\n\n<img width=\"841\" height=\"233\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-05-31 at 11 52 42 AM\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7ac76645-4e90-4d00-8242-f031146a22a5\"\n/>\n\n-------\n\n```\napprovals_reviewer = \"user\"\n\n[apps.connector_5f3c8c41a1e54ad7a76272c89e2554fa]\nenabled = true\napprovals_reviewer = \"auto_review\"\ndefault_tools_approval_mode = \"prompt\"\n```\n<img width=\"195\" height=\"83\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-05-31 at 12 02 27 PM\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3d374dc8-8aa2-466f-a13f-e4ed8567aa2e\"\n/>\n<img width=\"771\" height=\"207\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-05-31 at 12 05 42 PM\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/105c2575-68d6-4ca6-8e69-dc8c82da36a2\"\n/>\n\n\n\n## Summary\n- add `apps.<connector_id>.approvals_reviewer` to override Guardian or\nuser review routing per connected app\n- apply overrides across direct app MCP calls, delegated MCP prompts,\nand app-server MCP elicitation review while preserving global behavior\nfor non-app MCP servers\n- expose and document the config through app-server v2 and generated\nschemas, while honoring global managed reviewer requirements\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: jif-oai <jif@openai.com>","tree":{"sha":"8facf8e1abd57632aa34995436523cf7854c409a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/8facf8e1abd57632aa34995436523cf7854c409a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/4d80d808b4425fa31e086985264385b02e98932e","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHvDrCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAIKIQAJVncJswXRvrMAUzWKCCmBVS\nb+DMSKMnhp0qk0cz5gs1WU5Zq8ymnQLjGeRc14ScJYuYZQdLnJVEs0MZFikH22Ze\ni1HZUsXp+QQEajdVk3iqVJ0JxI6rCjfLp9vRyDsFpkqbH3l8ULH3LOmXGbzhbdYv\nI8G8xRLmwku6uU/+w6Ujay4zmrFvuu71fbfc1TfaZBlAD54DM+ivGEQk7BSX/9fg\n4at1uYRjEDwtMpsHXgj4rsOnEFCqRyhcxOAQ3g3vyKlpVwsY2eBkBjFVLupsuK5K\nvIx4bU90vgYuL8z5MuEb8EahgF6X1iDdp/te627VK0wwOZsjhJQG6Oo3lsVkLJlY\ndFQhTuXKQ1SGXoeFmP8fYBlRmxMJBUwTCLqY3emmBbmChNLpLa1PGuP3UPC9YvmS\nWqjs37JFZwcoadiQbB9XC38BzzgF7mBqMjg47/kddsfYpPsKVOcHkTPCLoF+lehZ\ndqTDSBo+GAG+RgqU9w7e2o+fWajUy+awQPemSx/vJ8Jw9wd44RJ0gYGp5AHFCuDL\nvCwaOrB2B0QP3lx2hrxp0SvWTLR9zzz6PNTQjSel0U/JvL+AB660e0mY5O6+UlGP\nD4/vwn1Tt6+bZIrTcHuGmA9VG/n1htAdTMPKoOJCszhRghBDBwH/QZFN8Hv674nb\nbHJDV9Paug4lbSPapur4\n=JvKG\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 8facf8e1abd57632aa34995436523cf7854c409a\nparent c097ad3e9e78f38699c6bec18f84b628f3fcde03\nauthor Alex Zamoshchin <alexz@openai.com> 1780412651 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780412651 +0200\n\n[app-server][core] Add connector-level Guardian reviewer overrides (#25167)\n\nContext: https://openai.slack.com/archives/C0B4JAF0Q2C/p1779912328647229\n\n```\napprovals_reviewer = \"auto_review\"\n\n[apps.connector_5f3c8c41a1e54ad7a76272c89e2554fa]\nenabled = true\napprovals_reviewer = \"user\"\ndefault_tools_approval_mode = \"prompt\"\n```\n\n<img width=\"230\" height=\"84\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-05-31 at 11 56 34 AM\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e319f8f7-0983-42a7-98cd-3302732fa406\"\n/>\n\n<img width=\"841\" height=\"233\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-05-31 at 11 52 42 AM\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7ac76645-4e90-4d00-8242-f031146a22a5\"\n/>\n\n-------\n\n```\napprovals_reviewer = \"user\"\n\n[apps.connector_5f3c8c41a1e54ad7a76272c89e2554fa]\nenabled = true\napprovals_reviewer = \"auto_review\"\ndefault_tools_approval_mode = \"prompt\"\n```\n<img width=\"195\" height=\"83\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-05-31 at 12 02 27 PM\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3d374dc8-8aa2-466f-a13f-e4ed8567aa2e\"\n/>\n<img width=\"771\" height=\"207\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-05-31 at 12 05 42 PM\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/105c2575-68d6-4ca6-8e69-dc8c82da36a2\"\n/>\n\n\n\n## Summary\n- add `apps.<connector_id>.approvals_reviewer` to override Guardian or\nuser review routing per connected app\n- apply overrides across direct app MCP calls, delegated MCP prompts,\nand app-server MCP elicitation review while preserving global behavior\nfor non-app MCP servers\n- expose and document the config through app-server v2 and generated\nschemas, while honoring global managed reviewer requirements\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: jif-oai <jif@openai.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-02T15:04:11Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4d80d808b4425fa31e086985264385b02e98932e","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/4d80d808b4425fa31e086985264385b02e98932e","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4d80d808b4425fa31e086985264385b02e98932e/comments","author":{"login":"zamoshchin-openai","id":185120305,"node_id":"U_kgDOCwi2MQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/185120305?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zamoshchin-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/zamoshchin-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zamoshchin-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zamoshchin-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zamoshchin-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zamoshchin-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zamoshchin-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zamoshchin-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zamoshchin-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zamoshchin-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zamoshchin-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"c097ad3e9e78f38699c6bec18f84b628f3fcde03","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c097ad3e9e78f38699c6bec18f84b628f3fcde03","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/c097ad3e9e78f38699c6bec18f84b628f3fcde03"}]},{"sha":"c097ad3e9e78f38699c6bec18f84b628f3fcde03","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGMwOTdhZDNlOWU3OGYzODY5OWM2YmVjMThmODRiNjI4ZjNmY2RlMDM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Adam Perry @ OpenAI","email":"anp@openai.com","date":"2026-06-02T14:39:41Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-02T14:39:41Z"},"message":"[codex] Use git CLI for Cargo fetches across Rust workflows (#25775)\n\n## Why\nCargo's libgit2 transport has intermittently failed while fetching git\ndependencies with nested submodules.\n[#25644](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/25644) applied\n`CARGO_NET_GIT_FETCH_WITH_CLI=true` to the main Rust release build after\nmacOS SecureTransport/libgit2 failures while cloning `libwebrtc`'s\nnested `libyuv` submodule. Similar flakes can affect other Cargo-bearing\nRust jobs.\n\n## What changed\nConfigure `CARGO_NET_GIT_FETCH_WITH_CLI=true` at workflow scope for the\nremaining Cargo-bearing Rust workflows:\n\n- fast Rust CI and `cargo-deny`\n- reusable Windows and argument-comment-lint release workflows\n- `rusty-v8-release` and `v8-canary` Cargo builds and smoke tests\n\nThe full Rust CI, reusable nextest workflow, and primary Rust release\nbuild already had the override. Bazel-only workflows are unchanged\nbecause they use a different dependency fetch path.\n\n## Validation\n- Parsed all `.github/workflows/*.yml` files as YAML.\n- Scanned Cargo-bearing workflows to confirm they configure\n`CARGO_NET_GIT_FETCH_WITH_CLI`.","tree":{"sha":"7f85ee9d2e4ea259b8e744000ca2ae87744349a4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/7f85ee9d2e4ea259b8e744000ca2ae87744349a4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/c097ad3e9e78f38699c6bec18f84b628f3fcde03","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHustCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA0f8QAEyNJlF0lqtozediMFVyZh5p\nYca0BFqZ3eQBhP+VHJjrRtOS7WhNMh7Yz/7IJusHwj7EY7t5a1e66gbgFXaDfK0S\nz9DQFbd15BxKp8FUlyKtqTwCF0IJIIxK33SYQ113eIsZT+ANALHC2nhdU34Y0aCd\nb1RSP0BjoL3xrP5RPe9RANpzKs/sPM2XGcodNA6kl7wT804HbwJYnpNugZDTD2VI\nxishx9g07ZDFPq5gLV1aMqz2Q8CcNBTaEeqkj0raECupUi6oIVz2j3Gxw/M8giFe\n0wYWjp3xXfmYnaJ+mBligOmISZWbtJqi1BQ8iNOmQeloOsLxToh2Yk0wALibGgqc\n9lhClqUMgm4OZOZITCwtx3L74Nn+qOSUJZD8EZ1NU0+VjSJQiZeWONbW4VnbmTwx\nuh9F2Vmw1iPYSWtD3niITzxoNz3ytPBTVCr6kWFxMZZPa7iMleskdWJevbvquj5H\nL06FuxBs/R3Jl8lP0FJkde4Ep8kN6C2FhGfyDxv+ME3Ko2LWNkDfQaNYloUumFcb\nNxjmQywUeDpodnty04hGKJ0kiK5BT0rFGzG+mAuDbBKDnMSEN6cQFquuHXCCnv/K\nVOWdM/rY340NfIioA7ti/Lh290Q2ABbPsM3BQ9WlcZvU6W/4NK6JNeBZz1uFJA1p\n4/RhBT6QMG+CQYxra9cY\n=43jL\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 7f85ee9d2e4ea259b8e744000ca2ae87744349a4\nparent 3766941161b7a2e3cb4fed1441963e4317b7fb11\nauthor Adam Perry @ OpenAI <anp@openai.com> 1780411181 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780411181 -0700\n\n[codex] Use git CLI for Cargo fetches across Rust workflows (#25775)\n\n## Why\nCargo's libgit2 transport has intermittently failed while fetching git\ndependencies with nested submodules.\n[#25644](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/25644) applied\n`CARGO_NET_GIT_FETCH_WITH_CLI=true` to the main Rust release build after\nmacOS SecureTransport/libgit2 failures while cloning `libwebrtc`'s\nnested `libyuv` submodule. Similar flakes can affect other Cargo-bearing\nRust jobs.\n\n## What changed\nConfigure `CARGO_NET_GIT_FETCH_WITH_CLI=true` at workflow scope for the\nremaining Cargo-bearing Rust workflows:\n\n- fast Rust CI and `cargo-deny`\n- reusable Windows and argument-comment-lint release workflows\n- `rusty-v8-release` and `v8-canary` Cargo builds and smoke tests\n\nThe full Rust CI, reusable nextest workflow, and primary Rust release\nbuild already had the override. Bazel-only workflows are unchanged\nbecause they use a different dependency fetch path.\n\n## Validation\n- Parsed all `.github/workflows/*.yml` files as YAML.\n- Scanned Cargo-bearing workflows to confirm they configure\n`CARGO_NET_GIT_FETCH_WITH_CLI`.","verified_at":"2026-06-02T14:39:42Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c097ad3e9e78f38699c6bec18f84b628f3fcde03","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/c097ad3e9e78f38699c6bec18f84b628f3fcde03","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c097ad3e9e78f38699c6bec18f84b628f3fcde03/comments","author":{"login":"anp-oai","id":286154589,"node_id":"U_kgDOEQ5fXQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/286154589?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/anp-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"3766941161b7a2e3cb4fed1441963e4317b7fb11","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/3766941161b7a2e3cb4fed1441963e4317b7fb11","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/3766941161b7a2e3cb4fed1441963e4317b7fb11"}]},{"sha":"3766941161b7a2e3cb4fed1441963e4317b7fb11","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDM3NjY5NDExNjFiN2EyZTNjYjRmZWQxNDQxOTYzZTQzMTdiN2ZiMTE","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-02T14:34:48Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-02T14:34:48Z"},"message":"Run Codex async main on a sized stack (#25847)\n\n## Why\n\n`Runtime::block_on` executes the top-level future on the caller's OS\nthread, not on one of Tokio's worker threads. That matters for the\ninteractive CLI because the Tokio runtime already configures larger\nworker stacks, while the process main thread can still have a smaller\nplatform default stack.\n\nThis showed up as a `/clear` crash on macOS: starting a fresh TUI thread\nreloads config, and the stack-heavy TOML deserialization path can\noverflow before the new session is actually started.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Run the regular `arg0_dispatch_or_else` async entrypoint on a named\n`codex-main` thread.\n- Give that thread the same `TOKIO_WORKER_STACK_SIZE_BYTES` stack budget\nalready used for Tokio worker threads.\n- Keep `Arg0DispatchPaths` and the arg0 alias guard lifetime behavior\nthe same.\n- Resume panics from the spawned main thread so panic behavior is\npreserved.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `cargo check -p codex-cli` currently fails because the top-level\nCLI/TUI future is not `Send` under the new thread boundary.","tree":{"sha":"e733472e14215de1430ef6dfc741543da33386e5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/e733472e14215de1430ef6dfc741543da33386e5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/3766941161b7a2e3cb4fed1441963e4317b7fb11","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHuoICRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAnTAQAG0mlhpF9+8lCZb+wTxQZkB9\nskrTgkCe0hcstif+B39U559rW5dQzw/o5cffOTDQQFEPEkNiyK9WFFu68mW/kLJ+\n9rKxz7EOV56gihALrxN85acThw0n5nsFv/AzynkqBnqJ8iYXLuNtSmxWJxYHqBW1\nCGWkdll9k+qRTe5pl8l8bHmepUWhw9AvBy+joS55nMa8OWmNhX/DgeybnyHwzwI4\nTee/8g5GUEIJRgEBlLPuy7rZl7ZCuKng/+Rn0jHPAI6M+pwWpe1J44Vzv+dTFxwr\nUotaRgTfVjw5du+ZQUDyH0/O/MfApleX4vn0Dc7x93GMhYWwqNlvxmKGYzvg5qVA\ndNOBWkOWE3Pk4KjVYveuJ7mFHCJfZPg+mKzPOt1Zjo7RHHaZXr4w7+/BcTGKz323\nv53RpiFgkB40spPoyceozqZxngQqHkNpPxarAaHtFmBlUVpXCf9T81J+dcji4Fus\nQadRm4L9n+YYSRR0k52DCaMMPBV/aTPmNJFnVikROM1tjj/GPrviPxo17jsrx/KX\nsako+AllnXzKR0lG9CftIn20IBlgyAIFdWz9Pu9TyygoSA3jXXQ2Ac1anbzfd/Z9\n51z1u1VtQyIEsKtS0SDpZJfjrFxhpoJj7KSZw+/itWYclNb0gCfo2mKgmpedCdYn\nMSItlDvxoKthjF8tlAaS\n=Ib5I\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree e733472e14215de1430ef6dfc741543da33386e5\nparent b9af5d1234429fa0c3de856b20200335330bb882\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1780410888 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780410888 +0200\n\nRun Codex async main on a sized stack (#25847)\n\n## Why\n\n`Runtime::block_on` executes the top-level future on the caller's OS\nthread, not on one of Tokio's worker threads. That matters for the\ninteractive CLI because the Tokio runtime already configures larger\nworker stacks, while the process main thread can still have a smaller\nplatform default stack.\n\nThis showed up as a `/clear` crash on macOS: starting a fresh TUI thread\nreloads config, and the stack-heavy TOML deserialization path can\noverflow before the new session is actually started.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Run the regular `arg0_dispatch_or_else` async entrypoint on a named\n`codex-main` thread.\n- Give that thread the same `TOKIO_WORKER_STACK_SIZE_BYTES` stack budget\nalready used for Tokio worker threads.\n- Keep `Arg0DispatchPaths` and the arg0 alias guard lifetime behavior\nthe same.\n- Resume panics from the spawned main thread so panic behavior is\npreserved.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `cargo check -p codex-cli` currently fails because the top-level\nCLI/TUI future is not `Send` under the new thread boundary.","verified_at":"2026-06-02T14:34:49Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/3766941161b7a2e3cb4fed1441963e4317b7fb11","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/3766941161b7a2e3cb4fed1441963e4317b7fb11","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/3766941161b7a2e3cb4fed1441963e4317b7fb11/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"b9af5d1234429fa0c3de856b20200335330bb882","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/b9af5d1234429fa0c3de856b20200335330bb882","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/b9af5d1234429fa0c3de856b20200335330bb882"}]},{"sha":"b9af5d1234429fa0c3de856b20200335330bb882","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGI5YWY1ZDEyMzQ0MjlmYTBjM2RlODU2YjIwMjAwMzM1MzMwYmI4ODI","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-02T14:21:22Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-02T14:21:22Z"},"message":"flake: Keep plugin test homes alive (#25857)\n\n## Summary\n\nKeep the full `TestCodex` harness alive in plugin integration tests\ninstead of returning only the `CodexThread`.\n\n## Why\n\nThe helper was moving a temporary `codex_home` into `TestCodex`, then\nimmediately dropping the harness and returning only the thread. For\nplugin MCP tests, the MCP server cwd is inside that temporary home. If\nthe temp directory is removed while MCP startup is still racing, the\nserver launch can fail with `No such file or directory`.\n\nKeeping the harness in scope keeps the temp home alive for the test\nduration and removes the lifetime race behind the recent\n`explicit_plugin_mentions_inject_plugin_guidance` flake.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just fmt`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nexplicit_plugin_mentions_inject_plugin_guidance`","tree":{"sha":"52591e5382c8125928e52c91ba1589775bc3c699","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/52591e5382c8125928e52c91ba1589775bc3c699"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/b9af5d1234429fa0c3de856b20200335330bb882","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHubiCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAArBIQAFvu7HQiK6NR5cRHKEdZ3cqK\nIy+/hg8ZVPqa7Mqc+VUdCyLxNQMSRJ/dcDkFJX5hCZHbIv0UCqcjm5TcpX9FCd8z\nIZMmmWXjpqI5JPIRVgACsB6c2JerQKZbd2PH8sm6BWATYIX0YeaRbLrjf/mvC0by\njmhd0FkbNSbRR5cWuR8Lztc+NxPIvY7+9SSXsKVIMfpXMeVpfF94HcKCf0dipsvf\nnzO9/1BUng7c/0IZgpCmyRgwapKjberQWg0YAen2sXFo0zD4Yf7ET+iBuL8kXBgZ\n9NA8yetEwWlLWqjym5pet8ECDou0TtTrMaffa90it27Q3majc5mXXCsFci/WoBq0\ndmc1Pb7g61P/pbGO140LzEOdh8bAemuOnOAp3jko3uubJJUuUzSWnR6yKfee7HQL\ngj7+p/0vVrhZMaVbAJzytlcyvYlG4jcWWyvY/QzHqQ1NGuyJm22w/Tr/+6uOqJi0\nUx64ZxeevvmpUII9jye69buMql1Yy6WMHll4ceVLJMQL90RrXG/TRuMwhBPh5U0w\nlh52vLXgJGT3TiLYRjsKBndryJYXrHcqwMlecF2oM7cekVpCpQIIoYdIXB5fozgm\nN2z22xtjcvI/nOrzf8Z+mRdRFoLuAx0mQjxEr4VwvCZ8syIvnIqyVerCiQHZESBJ\nv7xSmgAgSlRj2oJS2yPs\n=ifFS\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 52591e5382c8125928e52c91ba1589775bc3c699\nparent 1dd731305ad709b792fb3bf345733d932ee426ed\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1780410082 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780410082 +0200\n\nflake: Keep plugin test homes alive (#25857)\n\n## Summary\n\nKeep the full `TestCodex` harness alive in plugin integration tests\ninstead of returning only the `CodexThread`.\n\n## Why\n\nThe helper was moving a temporary `codex_home` into `TestCodex`, then\nimmediately dropping the harness and returning only the thread. For\nplugin MCP tests, the MCP server cwd is inside that temporary home. If\nthe temp directory is removed while MCP startup is still racing, the\nserver launch can fail with `No such file or directory`.\n\nKeeping the harness in scope keeps the temp home alive for the test\nduration and removes the lifetime race behind the recent\n`explicit_plugin_mentions_inject_plugin_guidance` flake.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just fmt`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nexplicit_plugin_mentions_inject_plugin_guidance`","verified_at":"2026-06-02T14:21:29Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/b9af5d1234429fa0c3de856b20200335330bb882","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/b9af5d1234429fa0c3de856b20200335330bb882","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/b9af5d1234429fa0c3de856b20200335330bb882/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"1dd731305ad709b792fb3bf345733d932ee426ed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/1dd731305ad709b792fb3bf345733d932ee426ed","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/1dd731305ad709b792fb3bf345733d932ee426ed"}]},{"sha":"1dd731305ad709b792fb3bf345733d932ee426ed","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDFkZDczMTMwNWFkNzA5Yjc5MmZiM2JmMzQ1NzMzZDkzMmVlNDI2ZWQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif-oai","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-02T13:42:47Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-02T13:42:47Z"},"message":"Reduce stack pressure in session startup and config rebuilds (#25844)\n\n## Why\n\n`/clear` starts a fresh thread with `InitialHistory::Cleared`, which\nre-enters the thread/session startup path. That path now builds large\nasync futures through `ThreadManagerState::spawn_thread_with_source`,\n`Codex::spawn`, and `Session::new`. Separately, TUI config rebuilds for\ncwd and permission-profile changes build a similarly heavy\n`ConfigBuilder::build()` future inside the app task. In debug and Bazel\nruns, those call chains can put enough state on the caller stack to\nabort before startup or config refresh completes.\n\nThis change keeps the behavior the same while moving the heaviest future\nframes off the caller stack.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Box `Codex::spawn(...)` in `codex-rs/core/src/thread_manager.rs`\nbefore awaiting it from `spawn_thread_with_source`.\n- Box `Session::new(...)` in `codex-rs/core/src/session/mod.rs` before\nawaiting it from `Codex::spawn_internal`.\n- Route `ConfigBuilder::build()` through a small `tokio::spawn` helper\nin `codex-rs/tui/src/app/config_persistence.rs` so cwd and\npermission-profile config rebuilds run on a runtime worker stack while\npreserving error context.\n\n## Verification\n\nCI is running on the PR.\n\nNo new targeted tests were added. This is a mechanical stack-pressure\nreduction that keeps the existing behavior and error propagation intact.","tree":{"sha":"bf260b385bdefba1dc63b9dabc87a568e9ab32bd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/bf260b385bdefba1dc63b9dabc87a568e9ab32bd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/1dd731305ad709b792fb3bf345733d932ee426ed","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHt3XCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAx8IQADu6vC5A6GeSrNv+d6ZQ/V7I\nLs9pHyZZuLE7le3R1reNYdCsZpURXafQ/n1y57/U+/VryX8qgzAPJal0KdrRqkF4\nQ2VUPiF0i1YNSCzQ4ouiDYOXX1IcVMjZHv10jE1RPbp4BUSg/pfxJ/3sJeLSS2M5\npGuVQmG6e9uWYQXFGRBJE7QWZbHQUkw7QkZ9dle/UQQINIiEMMBVWItodzWUs4bT\njmYV50m23YWYSDL34XJka/GCN/JP/jtF/Iq1ZG7mErWSKlCLkkhdPGQ6UeYWSx/P\nuQOlPPMaAZ4SrI+ZmoUKFIZ2nAJZt4eA2XShLCa6QzIWTKaYWCh6r/sQ5SInn6pv\nXg1T11ZBKMHPfi/DFjjU1QZIBNT5QlXA6PeJid5a8ahK0td1Nl44fidZ5clbQT3z\nCOo2tBbcIf/2CBCrFMXtuBk8CGCa07H0ZO7ZRjANgwXkL01EkDVVc7MTX2mww75Y\n30LjGBoRNiDegiG99Sl5VAS/+4e9CjdCGmNPiNrpieEnZwjbFD+TR2LP3LRe+d6U\n2UhfWHYpwbvt+KSlruyA9w3Mu/ouyV2VB2E5aID0rAAh8NxUrbbIbVKgIkvvZ7Rc\nt0ysZxBv3hcjznTlnoE8dF28Tnh4t3q0ZQleUSj774Z4JkWpJzizudzSUviXRD3h\nzCo1dQ9ycUbsKaDVnhEt\n=gaMz\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree bf260b385bdefba1dc63b9dabc87a568e9ab32bd\nparent 33273e4258386ad1a073827b32a6346e37536adc\nauthor jif-oai <jif@openai.com> 1780407767 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780407767 +0200\n\nReduce stack pressure in session startup and config rebuilds (#25844)\n\n## Why\n\n`/clear` starts a fresh thread with `InitialHistory::Cleared`, which\nre-enters the thread/session startup path. That path now builds large\nasync futures through `ThreadManagerState::spawn_thread_with_source`,\n`Codex::spawn`, and `Session::new`. Separately, TUI config rebuilds for\ncwd and permission-profile changes build a similarly heavy\n`ConfigBuilder::build()` future inside the app task. In debug and Bazel\nruns, those call chains can put enough state on the caller stack to\nabort before startup or config refresh completes.\n\nThis change keeps the behavior the same while moving the heaviest future\nframes off the caller stack.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Box `Codex::spawn(...)` in `codex-rs/core/src/thread_manager.rs`\nbefore awaiting it from `spawn_thread_with_source`.\n- Box `Session::new(...)` in `codex-rs/core/src/session/mod.rs` before\nawaiting it from `Codex::spawn_internal`.\n- Route `ConfigBuilder::build()` through a small `tokio::spawn` helper\nin `codex-rs/tui/src/app/config_persistence.rs` so cwd and\npermission-profile config rebuilds run on a runtime worker stack while\npreserving error context.\n\n## Verification\n\nCI is running on the PR.\n\nNo new targeted tests were added. This is a mechanical stack-pressure\nreduction that keeps the existing behavior and error propagation intact.","verified_at":"2026-06-02T13:42:48Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/1dd731305ad709b792fb3bf345733d932ee426ed","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/1dd731305ad709b792fb3bf345733d932ee426ed","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/1dd731305ad709b792fb3bf345733d932ee426ed/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"33273e4258386ad1a073827b32a6346e37536adc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/33273e4258386ad1a073827b32a6346e37536adc","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/33273e4258386ad1a073827b32a6346e37536adc"}]},{"sha":"33273e4258386ad1a073827b32a6346e37536adc","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDMzMjczZTQyNTgzODZhZDFhMDczODI3YjMyYTYzNDZlMzc1MzZhZGM","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif-oai","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-02T13:01:10Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-02T13:01:10Z"},"message":"Test runtime selector before first turn (#25724)\n\nStack split from #25708. Original PR intentionally left open. This fifth\nPR adds coverage that a remotely selected multi-agent runtime is applied\nwhen the model is selected before the first turn.","tree":{"sha":"73c2dc06a990300a6b6f16b8122f537efbcb4c46","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/73c2dc06a990300a6b6f16b8122f537efbcb4c46"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/33273e4258386ad1a073827b32a6346e37536adc","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHtQWCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAwMwQACrUc8o1e6fisyaDIHLXQjd8\nrWIIncEpr5/CINW+cL8RHFb19+nrcS+DAjvgpbMLdaAsmTrSqmMuzq0Boa6/GclU\nEpSMvFB0jVqvph5uvMzAMx+qT+Pazavp0zBihEFJTQ4twxUuNxjoV91yV9gHLnav\nmnlJiGEWrR21tjFBQinX+lXweq9/q2Tg4azhcuaF65G6En2PL5cG+DSOfw11ReeM\nkktzNhxuC++8IhjGgKQViBWrQR+IBBToqCzZXFwj09kerLijUsHepGsXWI30rhik\nHRL+BaA/e6vKFmJJgKHUYDrGOBz1Z4m0r1EPmE0XZWk6xBMjA0LMxiGyza95jQ7P\nF8K73iJPb87tJgV8MaO36zLqNUhLTHZIkCX3SRo1FCfq1wKUx9av0o9iMS/4T42L\nWoaY3hq/FPkaYY68NIZ460EC2bQdB+z+YPWpU49Y4kVxNUJmWOvXsR1K1JTbOlyX\n8TpdbI06NQ56ku7lLdioedAP37Kw4nzzJioXnYVvAw32Rw51NTiUT73eOeNmviGi\nFB5ph8KbUEdDXaTuA86UQDdnwrsmT2o+AMqxct8HhjT6g8cC7ykNJiiE6hPKu+Tm\n5U1d9+Kxif/SBxFrrlLE645xCz2teIhl0zkH1W3DKxz+73/5l7h93cYB36kFh8bn\nhjqxrgYEl7UiVHd4z995\n=Vyp2\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 73c2dc06a990300a6b6f16b8122f537efbcb4c46\nparent 66991c949f4352577d7d3bf83aa63abd8af15b95\nauthor jif-oai <jif@openai.com> 1780405270 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780405270 +0200\n\nTest runtime selector before first turn (#25724)\n\nStack split from #25708. Original PR intentionally left open. This fifth\nPR adds coverage that a remotely selected multi-agent runtime is applied\nwhen the model is selected before the first turn.","verified_at":"2026-06-02T13:01:11Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/33273e4258386ad1a073827b32a6346e37536adc","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/33273e4258386ad1a073827b32a6346e37536adc","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/33273e4258386ad1a073827b32a6346e37536adc/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"66991c949f4352577d7d3bf83aa63abd8af15b95","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/66991c949f4352577d7d3bf83aa63abd8af15b95","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/66991c949f4352577d7d3bf83aa63abd8af15b95"}]},{"sha":"66991c949f4352577d7d3bf83aa63abd8af15b95","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDY2OTkxYzk0OWY0MzUyNTc3ZDdkM2JmODNhYTYzYWJkOGFmMTViOTU","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif-oai","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-02T12:48:13Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-02T12:48:13Z"},"message":"Test remote multi-agent runtime selector override (#25723)\n\nStack split from #25708. Original PR intentionally left open. This\nfourth PR adds coverage that remote model multi-agent runtime selectors\noverride local feature flag defaults.","tree":{"sha":"43c63b9dad778ea38a0f1429c5577978a71366e6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/43c63b9dad778ea38a0f1429c5577978a71366e6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/66991c949f4352577d7d3bf83aa63abd8af15b95","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHtENCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAntIQACI9BvP3ncL2eGdP+RzYcuJO\nFM0JpJGw+R13H7WdD7UCdlYBz46W6AeaQ37qwkl