":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"45912a6dc69ed04f1e7ef8ec3ecb4c9dc0860b6d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/45912a6dc69ed04f1e7ef8ec3ecb4c9dc0860b6d","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/45912a6dc69ed04f1e7ef8ec3ecb4c9dc0860b6d"}]},{"sha":"45912a6dc69ed04f1e7ef8ec3ecb4c9dc0860b6d","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDQ1OTEyYTZkYzY5ZWQwNGYxZTdlZjhlYzNlY2I0YzlkYzA4NjBiNmQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif-oai","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-02T09:32:36Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-02T09:32:36Z"},"message":"feat: reuse compressed rollout search snippets (#25814)\n\n## Summary\n- teach rollout search to return precomputed snippets for compressed\nrollouts\n- reuse those snippets in local thread search instead of reopening\nmatching compressed files\n- keep the no-`rg` fallback single-pass and add regression coverage for\nthe compressed path\n\n## Why\n`thread/search` currently decodes matching compressed rollouts twice:\nonce to discover the matching path and again to extract the snippet\nshown in results. That defeats a meaningful part of the compressed-read\noptimization work.\n\n## Impact\nCompressed rollout hits now pay one decode pass on the search path while\nplain `.jsonl` hits keep the existing ripgrep-driven flow.\n\n## Validation\n- `just test -p codex-rollout`\n- `just test -p codex-thread-store`\n- `just fix -p codex-rollout`\n- `just fix -p codex-thread-store`\n- `just fmt`","tree":{"sha":"91426772b985a2cd1264becd82ff3530d932f028","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/91426772b985a2cd1264becd82ff3530d932f028"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/45912a6dc69ed04f1e7ef8ec3ecb4c9dc0860b6d","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHqM0CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAucEQAKHUfwYahx+tnLzowJ97graI\nUXo1VTgIcHDQgIU+zDuJhg7fUgnwHu4o5tEDEXa6DYp/UW5MH5LUMJr9B2L3osnZ\nYPT29Bx2sCdCydXvg9fdDmpn/tm9UTaJvXqq1ihMwj7uwtz4MT58pzNhJupFpsvm\nf2yENl0B1k6bn7bm5BN3ekxsxEyHI+RLZ38WddnswLt/f4xhjxrDL7J1+kqs3k/8\nHoNkcTZpWDmF/30im6zKA+8NmaaRUyV4ZjO/ZxxKL9iHLxJITqy2ufe5v1s20lCU\n/XmFZ4JmfqCs74D2ha9Mg/cL5xoI/mK77BUJoFOtQOPtno2QU6TOZKJc5GIw6pZx\nHvQYaiwJE4uy7xHPPRKE6PW8HGPbWJdQ9WSwyuT6xla1PM3bCSHzVnKkhDsFcMQq\nbPYrSuUQv7PaXBDFzNlHn9YSBqR/F/Ak94E66GySh66vrV0jYJswKFXK2LacePqo\nIDzN2MlDDjzFASoLB/Mwp0XvM9qfQR/QG6giqmy1FGNG4fQA0lcWQmkY+IRStZI2\ngXkpMBJHHI1IbgwXl6m1h/QlikhFpFCjJABFuoyvQA9VIRoKr3a85HaHhhbpYhZM\nuTA0N3mfo4Yf/KLx0KXNqAEykuXSEx8Ng/8YFcQ4yrT5Khjs0BDfxgnaDN2+2YGB\nsepyP+FhI6fGfXdCPIM6\n=qcW7\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 91426772b985a2cd1264becd82ff3530d932f028\nparent 67b805fc111706aca5b32d465c94d95659bab6aa\nauthor jif-oai <jif@openai.com> 1780392756 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780392756 +0200\n\nfeat: reuse compressed rollout search snippets (#25814)\n\n## Summary\n- teach rollout search to return precomputed snippets for compressed\nrollouts\n- reuse those snippets in local thread search instead of reopening\nmatching compressed files\n- keep the no-`rg` fallback single-pass and add regression coverage for\nthe compressed path\n\n## Why\n`thread/search` currently decodes matching compressed rollouts twice:\nonce to discover the matching path and again to extract the snippet\nshown in results. That defeats a meaningful part of the compressed-read\noptimization work.\n\n## Impact\nCompressed rollout hits now pay one decode pass on the search path while\nplain `.jsonl` hits keep the existing ripgrep-driven flow.\n\n## Validation\n- `just test -p codex-rollout`\n- `just test -p codex-thread-store`\n- `just fix -p codex-rollout`\n- `just fix -p codex-thread-store`\n- `just fmt`","verified_at":"2026-06-02T09:32:36Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/45912a6dc69ed04f1e7ef8ec3ecb4c9dc0860b6d","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/45912a6dc69ed04f1e7ef8ec3ecb4c9dc0860b6d","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/45912a6dc69ed04f1e7ef8ec3ecb4c9dc0860b6d/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"67b805fc111706aca5b32d465c94d95659bab6aa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/67b805fc111706aca5b32d465c94d95659bab6aa","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/67b805fc111706aca5b32d465c94d95659bab6aa"}]},{"sha":"67b805fc111706aca5b32d465c94d95659bab6aa","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDY3YjgwNWZjMTExNzA2YWNhNWIzMmQ0NjVjOTRkOTU2NTliYWI2YWE","commit":{"author":{"name":"xl-openai","email":"xl@openai.com","date":"2026-06-02T06:33:02Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-02T06:33:02Z"},"message":"[codex] Validate plugin skill base names (#25782)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Validate skill base name length before plugin namespacing.\n- Bound the composed `plugin:skill` qualified name to 128 characters.\n- Keep plugin skill runtime names in the existing `plugin:skill` form.\n- Add regression tests for the max qualified-name boundary and rejection\npath.\n\n## Root Cause\n\nPlugin skills are represented as `plugin_name:skill_name`, but the\nloader previously applied the 64-character skill name limit after adding\nthe plugin namespace. Moving that check to the base name fixes valid\nplugin skills with longer namespaces, and the separate 128-character\nqualified-name limit keeps model-visible skill names bounded.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just fmt`\n- `just test -p codex-core-skills plugin_skill_name_length_limit`\n- `git diff --check`","tree":{"sha":"773426993705a26ffc06af02b93c73bcfa83da1a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/773426993705a26ffc06af02b93c73bcfa83da1a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/67b805fc111706aca5b32d465c94d95659bab6aa","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHnkeCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAd8wQAH0WU2GF6wtz/2lJcm5ZlNsP\nC/UTdkuBWmZqnLbUDvs554pVPsOT6FUqpFWdA4ach4LK55ituv5p2DdY5aeYVa78\nFA3BpCvHMS+J9tmlJQHrGAXw5ZRyBylVyW35hiC6FyxNyPN5nmaJ34dnsgn2LP4l\nfRp0ca2Ppr808Okf8VXzPOwdoPq/5yytFUjS/PgKegjiULlAnQv/iutwsDp6OcVT\nziMuqtzniQg5/lV1yH3MRB0k4k8M0uk/1LrnztCZCcGN7GToAl3SUZztS7/PNYeB\nngu/FmhLdR14yVi7NeZ4yFjwpYYlqLRQZ6/lbiwk+a8nJHESi3R6xgyfBGkXcd3M\nDnVzyGu61Fv96DM8LMlTaSpcsDq46tx9BjV7cz4HJQLcJmldeu16VL6q5IE46JLm\n0wPxG5L2k6ibE/Eucq78AAkq2NW4ni5B/Bjemyt4Qixq+ikkhd+rtzJhwvsCxU1i\nxkPptD5nmLfPf/jv7hAEbtfM78okLTBAlQ5jXNBdEOdh4Q5mXCXsGFAWWw/5ont0\nsGe+srUTW4V+SDLG0tkb/nQBI1Duf3iY3gzBxE1FZOe48ZZcp/3vXrunoSb62U4V\n7lGVUlSSrGyrU4IukDBAKTgHn2DJhi48nRgDqDygVivmavK/gNVFB1nUBVDTGYbU\nuRi8rmHmppPqcJHlqX96\n=6aCi\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 773426993705a26ffc06af02b93c73bcfa83da1a\nparent 07f04cc3c7d1ddb4289469fdfa4740be0d0a82d2\nauthor xl-openai <xl@openai.com> 1780381982 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780381982 +0000\n\n[codex] Validate plugin skill base names (#25782)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Validate skill base name length before plugin namespacing.\n- Bound the composed `plugin:skill` qualified name to 128 characters.\n- Keep plugin skill runtime names in the existing `plugin:skill` form.\n- Add regression tests for the max qualified-name boundary and rejection\npath.\n\n## Root Cause\n\nPlugin skills are represented as `plugin_name:skill_name`, but the\nloader previously applied the 64-character skill name limit after adding\nthe plugin namespace. Moving that check to the base name fixes valid\nplugin skills with longer namespaces, and the separate 128-character\nqualified-name limit keeps model-visible skill names bounded.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just fmt`\n- `just test -p codex-core-skills plugin_skill_name_length_limit`\n- `git diff --check`","verified_at":"2026-06-02T06:33:02Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/67b805fc111706aca5b32d465c94d95659bab6aa","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/67b805fc111706aca5b32d465c94d95659bab6aa","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/67b805fc111706aca5b32d465c94d95659bab6aa/comments","author":{"login":"xl-openai","id":184293535,"node_id":"U_kgDOCvwYnw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/184293535?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/xl-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"07f04cc3c7d1ddb4289469fdfa4740be0d0a82d2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/07f04cc3c7d1ddb4289469fdfa4740be0d0a82d2","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/07f04cc3c7d1ddb4289469fdfa4740be0d0a82d2"}]},{"sha":"07f04cc3c7d1ddb4289469fdfa4740be0d0a82d2","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDA3ZjA0Y2MzYzdkMWRkYjQyODk0NjlmZGZhNDc0MGJlMGQwYTgyZDI","commit":{"author":{"name":"xl-openai","email":"xl@openai.com","date":"2026-06-02T06:25:37Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-02T06:25:37Z"},"message":"[codex] Move plugin discoverable logic into core-plugins (#25783)\n\n## Summary\n- Move plugin discoverable recommendation filtering from `codex-core`\ninto `codex-core-plugins` behind `ToolSuggestPluginDiscoveryInput`.\n- Keep `codex-core` as a thin adapter from `Config` to the core-plugins\nAPI and back to `DiscoverablePluginInfo`.\n- Keep the existing discoverable allowlist private to the core-plugins\nimplementation.\n\n## Validation\n- `just fmt`\n- `just test -p codex-core list_tool_suggest_discoverable_plugins`\n- `git diff --check`\n- Read-only subagent review: no findings","tree":{"sha":"e299c12c92966778ff00d62b1ba258c70c99027d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/e299c12c92966778ff00d62b1ba258c70c99027d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/07f04cc3c7d1ddb4289469fdfa4740be0d0a82d2","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHndhCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWPIQADwhujcD4Q66j6sr8df7rEk+\nJoCpr9zOBiDPaWNmKgnHCoszKMkd71kdZ1KOM5dEtEvaGlPa3C/JTNu9/9s1B09a\ns7SD5NlfP+ELenVGQNm0TR503S+FPWENUZN3JzEyzG3AYMLp1CXf4b6Yebvk5fm2\na3yFndpTXq6jZgeWl2SpI75PHlB07mnx/WYsntbsVEoEn+KGHTqNEFRFd+PyDh0R\n7X98Ux6a4GrDfYlKlg4c4vEBWrBLkjLoB90ffeoO/AqOjZdwsjtEqpDprFE+LKeO\naAL7905+xiaBiPGVBm34ZLVZ+rkBmSn5zdDPaLcm7c0IPem/1EnzVCrGVTM/Cem9\ne33UacM5wtZTMB0UDMFl6hNAfRjHWH7F4m1izDfRGM9rLQnSvWmJDbw45oxCBfEA\njhlpS5brOoqGmK8bvIykFTzOk1PwjSXFSQygKlTuyxPeUqI+TGVahyoDF54VBNtg\nwwiTXo3Wmp68RgnycU42A