commit":{"author":{"name":"xl-openai","email":"xl@openai.com","date":"2026-06-02T04:27:06Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-02T04:27:06Z"},"message":"[codex] Add plugin list JSON output (#25330)\n\n## Summary\n- add `--json` output to `codex plugin list` with `installed` and\n`available` arrays\n- add `--available` for JSON output only; using it without `--json` is\nrejected\n- keep the existing non-JSON table output unchanged\n- add CLI coverage for JSON installed/available output and the\n`--available`/`--json` requirement\n\n## Validation\n- `just test -p codex-cli plugin_list`\n- `just fix -p codex-cli`\n- `git diff --check`\n\nNote: `just fmt` ran Rust formatting first, then failed in the Python\nruff step because `openai-codex-cli-bin==0.132.0` has no wheel for this\nLinux platform.","tree":{"sha":"c60cce83575fa7dbbdb5feb7c43b47e61cc1ca8f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/c60cce83575fa7dbbdb5feb7c43b47e61cc1ca8f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/cb63ee7f5d077a625fe93d292bbcf5a4b9dfc6a3","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHluaCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAXacQAJgKPl9SLTYxJ2MQ33DFBUnN\noRu7DPtmYis0jaQpfa9gy8UHMipDcsB8cfj+ntElDXAzNI4rbQRMRxmwyizKS12d\nFBEpoud14wo2r78GqUM3XqykduzuktgRL/r6DcCMAUrV614F6yG5KArwf0F9OqoO\niEoog7OwzYxZ0FHplC4DqDwmFGysOGZWFojNGo+F2uXtkreRUyKFHtD/ozJs3QrX\n4LasZTO2ho4ii6S47Pja3c7sn9zKsX+fyYoY7LYdk8MneADWiI/4mM9Kw/ImOzlM\nzCR2b7adUBClSsXIP6fnw73HqV6T61fCc5AzawX4d9ZQqEVlbxfIr+mSbKkAYhYp\nRlf5N7mEnM9pGfsiJWO4zejFfTA1J5JU24eR1yIyDh8ji3WPjW8gx5F7YF/yX5lj\nyqXpB8TyEUvRONcki21ncpMpoUfCHcp3J9jdTGoYmYmzI5E4jxetaQrT/cWkx7cU\ndVz1GsYpZ4SFTTZfdH/ywgRtxAPcQ97IX5/ZG90O7+A4KTiEnV0BFxINqDKhBWLS\nLVI6APSrTK8nU15kpnUadguJOMyqNXMKdCke6hHzM+iG73fdB7MlkEo2FranprqT\n8H5eO9ij+AqmxvKBkN5Z/et6XPawJRWcpmIF7rXs97wnIP+xcvz2IWJwQlDFKGBO\nonGh4/bAGX6ePkM3/rKD\n=0iZc\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree c60cce83575fa7dbbdb5feb7c43b47e61cc1ca8f\nparent c8e5db16c9994affe8e1959fb76d58c3775d4075\nauthor xl-openai <xl@openai.com> 1780374426 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780374426 -0700\n\n[codex] Add plugin list JSON output (#25330)\n\n## Summary\n- add `--json` output to `codex plugin list` with `installed` and\n`available` arrays\n- add `--available` for JSON output only; using it without `--json` is\nrejected\n- keep the existing non-JSON table output unchanged\n- add CLI coverage for JSON installed/available output and the\n`--available`/`--json` requirement\n\n## Validation\n- `just test -p codex-cli plugin_list`\n- `just fix -p codex-cli`\n- `git diff --check`\n\nNote: `just fmt` ran Rust formatting first, then failed in the Python\nruff step because `openai-codex-cli-bin==0.132.0` has no wheel for this\nLinux platform.","verified_at":"2026-06-02T04:27:06Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/cb63ee7f5d077a625fe93d292bbcf5a4b9dfc6a3","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/cb63ee7f5d077a625fe93d292bbcf5a4b9dfc6a3","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/cb63ee7f5d077a625fe93d292bbcf5a4b9dfc6a3/comments","author":{"login":"xl-openai","id":184293535,"node_id":"U_kgDOCvwYnw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/184293535?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/xl-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"c8e5db16c9994affe8e1959fb76d58c3775d4075","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c8e5db16c9994affe8e1959fb76d58c3775d4075","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/c8e5db16c9994affe8e1959fb76d58c3775d4075"}]},{"sha":"c8e5db16c9994affe8e1959fb76d58c3775d4075","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGM4ZTVkYjE2Yzk5OTRhZmZlOGUxOTU5ZmI3NmQ1OGMzNzc1ZDQwNzU","commit":{"author":{"name":"efrazer-oai","email":"efrazer@openai.com","date":"2026-06-02T04:25:42Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-02T04:25:42Z"},"message":"feat: show enterprise monthly credit limits in status (#24812)\n\n## Summary\n\nEnterprise users can have an effective monthly credit limit, but Codex\n`/status` currently drops that metadata from the account-usage response.\n\nThis change adds the optional `spend_control.individual_limit`\nprojection to the existing rate-limit snapshot flow. The backend client\nreads the monthly limit, app-server exposes it as `individualLimit`, and\nthe TUI renders a `Monthly credit limit` row through the existing\nprogress-bar renderer.\n\nWhen the backend does not return an effective monthly limit, existing\nrate-limit behavior is unchanged.\n\n## Existing backend state\n\nThe account-usage backend already returns the effective monthly limit\nand current usage together:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"spend_control\": {\n    \"reached\": false,\n    \"individual_limit\": {\n      \"limit\": \"25000\",\n      \"used\": \"8000\",\n      \"remaining\": \"17000\",\n      \"used_percent\": 32,\n      \"remaining_percent\": 68,\n      \"reset_after_seconds\": 86400,\n      \"reset_at\": 1778137680\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nBefore this change, Codex projected rolling `primary` and `secondary`\nwindows plus `credits`. It ignored `spend_control.individual_limit`, so\napp-server clients and `/status` could not render the monthly cap.\n\nThe updated flow is:\n\n```text\naccount usage backend\n  -> backend-client reads spend_control.individual_limit\n  -> existing rate-limit snapshot carries optional individual_limit\n  -> app-server exposes optional individualLimit\n  -> TUI renders Monthly credit limit\n```\n\n## App-server contract\n\n`account/rateLimits/read` and sparse `account/rateLimits/updated`\nnotifications now include an additive nullable\n`rateLimits.individualLimit` field:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"individualLimit\": {\n    \"limit\": \"25000\",\n    \"used\": \"8000\",\n    \"remainingPercent\": 68,\n    \"resetsAt\": 1778137680\n  }\n}\n```\n\nIn an `account/rateLimits/read` response, `null` means no monthly limit\nis available. `account/rateLimits/updated` remains a sparse rolling\nnotification: clients merge available values into their most recent\n`account/rateLimits/read` snapshot or refetch. Nullable account metadata\nin a rolling notification does not clear a previously observed value.\n\n## Design decisions\n\n- Extend the existing rate-limit snapshot instead of introducing a\nseparate request or wire-level update protocol.\n- Keep the Codex projection narrow: `/status` needs the effective limit,\ncurrent usage, remaining percentage, and reset timestamp.\n- Render the monthly row through the existing progress-bar renderer,\nwith one optional detail line for `8,000 of 25,000 credits used`.\n- Keep the backend response optional so existing accounts and older\nusage states preserve their current behavior.\n- Preserve cached monthly metadata when sparse rolling notifications\nomit it. Live account-usage reads remain authoritative and can clear a\nremoved limit.\n\n## Visual evidence\n\n```text\n Monthly credit limit:   [██████████████░░░░░░] 68% left (resets 07:08 on 7 May)\n                         8,000 of 25,000 credits used\n```\n\nSnapshot:\n`codex-rs/tui/src/status/snapshots/codex_tui__status__tests__status_snapshot_includes_enterprise_monthly_credit_limit.snap`\n\n## Testing\n\nTests: generated app-server schema verification, protocol tests,\nbackend-client tests, app-server integration coverage, TUI snapshot\ncoverage, formatting, and workspace lint cleanup.","tree":{"sha":"d2a385b03032fe529d1bbece8513ce8b25d8190a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/d2a385b03032fe529d1bbece8513ce8b25d8190a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/c8e5db16c9994affe8e1959fb76d58c3775d4075","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHltGCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjewQAIy8/kZBaPbp/M38o0I6MkvH\nZ8i5l604EB2+cFOyfNQt/6WMVcqMJBAgvLqkpVGyM/hoajuk0h9kuDGn0Jdh1XHq\n3SgpIVMz14VqIPDzWyfPa4iGWBPxhFQKZVVXj2mxsFVvA9y5nYS/qsqzwnn7oqHB\nTtLLJ4plnXHpuNIhLbHHXeXfrszmFx1vIpdGug3vKwKjy5OFYZjhd2jaRZrnj3ze\nlhVYaD1VnWjbqmHFb5rowDcN5INhO/Jkmfu4JLrzc9O/aW9JvXtJ8IEhyUOT3u3U\n3CAfHPiubq+nrQ1WR+7bKCANYYfJXVxE5iD6CjJHB3QwQ2aD8OY10JsaeLoqnrsN\nUw8UBmHErTgC3ZIfqFhwrn2bQPWjqOMTPoY4i3uLUu2LLCpb3frzA4n4NSomtfNH\nunc2ZRBmpDwhpDqo5hujvc4y1oDyUUQWtFuSWd+67J66vXEb1EhnOO3SZ+jadp10\ni7UVA/sLJuUnb9AyQGbK/bt8RLPsEYOorEi43/Udt+Nppptu7XvEZJzYuilIb6wU\njcD3sCiog8TmV7W6ZJiVUzgkrZwDYciUq1N/D7suf3rYvc3B6m83DMKbMRDB5C8Q\nK4Pz2ofZEGAYQX3G3oV/IAgW3emDBuNSZBWO473nbxvSi4HkE6QM27bxNuYR0g8i\nanNOo/d1k5/02j6CId1H\n=nevx\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree d2a385b03032fe529d1bbece8513ce8b25d8190a\nparent c955f730781da63bf1d29480f5cb43b012ef430a\nauthor efrazer-oai <efrazer@openai.com> 1780374342 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780374342 -0700\n\nfeat: show enterprise monthly credit limits in status (#24812)\n\n## Summary\n\nEnterprise users can have an effective monthly credit limit, but Codex\n`/status` currently drops that metadata from the account-usage response.\n\nThis change adds the optional `spend_control.individual_limit`\nprojection to the existing rate-limit snapshot flow. The backend client\nreads the monthly limit, app-server exposes it as `individualLimit`, and\nthe TUI renders a `Monthly credit limit` row through the existing\nprogress-bar renderer.\n\nWhen the backend does not return an effective monthly limit, existing\nrate-limit behavior is unchanged.\n\n## Existing backend state\n\nThe account-usage backend already returns the effective monthly limit\nand current usage together:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"spend_control\": {\n    \"reached\": false,\n    \"individual_limit\": {\n      \"limit\": \"25000\",\n      \"used\": \"8000\",\n      \"remaining\": \"17000\",\n      \"used_percent\": 32,\n      \"remaining_percent\": 68,\n      \"reset_after_seconds\": 86400,\n      \"reset_at\": 1778137680\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nBefore this change, Codex projected rolling `primary` and `secondary`\nwindows plus `credits`. It ignored `spend_control.individual_limit`, so\napp-server clients and `/status` could not render the monthly cap.\n\nThe updated flow is:\n\n```text\naccount usage backend\n  -> backend-client reads spend_control.individual_limit\n  -> existing rate-limit snapshot carries optional individual_limit\n  -> app-server exposes optional individualLimit\n  -> TUI renders Monthly credit limit\n```\n\n## App-server contract\n\n`account/rateLimits/read` and sparse `account/rateLimits/updated`\nnotifications now include an additive nullable\n`rateLimits.individualLimit` field:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"individualLimit\": {\n    \"limit\": \"25000\",\n    \"used\": \"8000\",\n    \"remainingPercent\": 68,\n    \"resetsAt\": 1778137680\n  }\n}\n```\n\nIn an `account/rateLimits/read` response, `null` means no monthly limit\nis available. `account/rateLimits/updated` remains a sparse rolling\nnotification: clients merge available values into their most recent\n`account/rateLimits/read` snapshot or refetch. Nullable account metadata\nin a rolling notification does not clear a previously observed value.\n\n## Design decisions\n\n- Extend the existing rate-limit snapshot instead of introducing a\nseparate request or wire-level update protocol.\n- Keep the Codex projection narrow: `/status` needs the effective limit,\ncurrent usage, remaining percentage, and reset timestamp.\n- Render the monthly row through the existing progress-bar renderer,\nwith one optional detail line for `8,000 of 25,000 credits used`.\n- Keep the backend response optional so existing accounts and older\nusage states preserve their current behavior.\n- Preserve cached monthly metadata when sparse rolling notifications\nomit it. Live account-usage reads remain authoritative and can clear a\nremoved limit.\n\n## Visual evidence\n\n```text\n Monthly credit limit:   [██████████████░░░░░░] 68% left (resets 07:08 on 7 May)\n                         8,000 of 25,000 credits used\n```\n\nSnapshot:\n`codex-rs/tui/src/status/snapshots/codex_tui__status__tests__status_snapshot_includes_enterprise_monthly_credit_limit.snap`\n\n## Testing\n\nTests: generated app-server schema verification, protocol tests,\nbackend-client tests, app-server integration coverage, TUI snapshot\ncoverage, formatting, and workspace lint cleanup.","verified_at":"2026-06-02T04:25:43Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c8e5db16c9994affe8e1959fb76d58c3775d4075","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/c8e5db16c9994affe8e1959fb76d58c3775d4075","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c8e5db16c9994affe8e1959fb76d58c3775d4075/comments","author":{"login":"efrazer-oai","id":263771262,"node_id":"U_kgDOD7jUfg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/263771262?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/efrazer-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/efrazer-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/efrazer-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/efrazer-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/efrazer-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/efrazer-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/efrazer-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/efrazer-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/efrazer-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/efrazer-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/efrazer-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"c955f730781da63bf1d29480f5cb43b012ef430a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c955f730781da63bf1d29480f5cb43b012ef430a","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/c955f730781da63bf1d29480f5cb43b012ef430a"}]},{"sha":"c955f730781da63bf1d29480f5cb43b012ef430a","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGM5NTVmNzMwNzgxZGE2M2JmMWQyOTQ4MGY1Y2I0M2IwMTJlZjQzMGE","commit":{"author":{"name":"pakrym-oai","email":"pakrym@openai.com","date":"2026-06-02T01:41:04Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-02T01:41:04Z"},"message":"Move code review rules into AGENTS (#25738)\n\n## Why\nCodex Review now supports repository-specific review rules in AGENTS.md.\nAdding the review prompts there makes the guidance available as\nrepository review rules next to the code it governs while keeping the\nexisting local review skills intact.\n\n## What changed\n- Added a `## Code Review Rules` section to `AGENTS.md` with the\nexisting review prompts for model context, breaking changes, test\nauthoring, and change size.\n- Preserved the existing `.codex/skills/code-review*` skill files.\n\n## Verification\n- `git diff --check origin/main...HEAD`","tree":{"sha":"35a13c0cf60b59278b15a77eb619a69d49e850d6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/35a13c0cf60b59278b15a77eb619a69d49e850d6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/c955f730781da63bf1d29480f5cb43b012ef430a","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHjSwCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAI+oQAGgKmsZ1f3Bj1Y8tvVSxtPUW\npcocgmLJjkby8guWXrwBFnk9L9bgMuG4g6YsZFsGkv46pJLDmH3DgAJFGlVK6326\nIVj9w+qEOunGLdcHsWON9d3P2qqmqvK+ZOmCIscFrkQTeRIQ52nbAZo+EnvYvG16\nX5bZTiJ1y83n63qV3HpacA59d80L2aKB4UKWvbn/pGuRApFf9ye6QiQ52A2V+q16\nOpd8mwAHBycT4yXVowabW58Ti0wwRj8MJPRGduv6YiJDWWwysFFEzH7+XNoMcjEL\n3PmrMopSDqtGNFU3Ib+SlkMqr3IEx33bDmw+uXNjnUfzRQ8x8g85szfSElC9jVVm\ns5Dvkn3sy0QG1ZB/lFdny9hDcg+h+9N8pVyIo4+IJVglI5v4vc3hoJ06gDTJYun6\nOGMREMaMlsREFMpaZySudh9eR70GI3MLseWrzmoPw+8x5LpBMxMYZZGOJThNXy2t\neS43Nzaax+8TQoauXgz/iUPEenZFyb/JiHzY55PSRxuYF33U9dtibYtIe1ImGqzX\nnO9LCSM872CYBAIJvKPLCReChqMJ0Rw6FVEtU521+OfMr/5FEPqnJUviJMYc63WY\nrQNfftVazJFlZKYUqk2iIgkAmG+ZuKT8mukrGDjcG45fxALKLyOe+gjczemIyJ9V\n2T1l5LI9x8FDJ9wBFR1/\n=Jo0Z\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 35a13c0cf60b59278b15a77eb619a69d49e850d6\nparent 747f1003ddf734b97b550d44b13c63ed71dc7986\nauthor pakrym-oai <pakrym@openai.com> 1780364464 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780364464 +0000\n\nMove code review rules into AGENTS (#25738)\n\n## Why\nCodex Review now supports repository-specific review rules in AGENTS.md.\nAdding the review prompts there makes the guidance available as\nrepository review rules next to the code it governs while keeping the\nexisting local review skills intact.\n\n## What changed\n- Added a `## Code Review Rules` section to `AGENTS.md` with the\nexisting review prompts for model context, breaking changes, test\nauthoring, and change size.\n- Preserved the existing `.codex/skills/code-review*` skill files.\n\n## Verification\n- `git diff --check origin/main...HEAD`","verified_at":"2026-06-02T01:41:05Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c955f730781da63bf1d29480f5cb43b012ef430a","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/c955f730781da63bf1d29480f5cb43b012ef430a","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c955f730781da63bf1d29480f5cb43b012ef430a/comments","author":{"login":"pakrym-oai","id":204937752,"node_id":"U_kgDODDcaGA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/204937752?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/pakrym-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"747f1003ddf734b97b550d44b13c63ed71dc7986","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/747f1003ddf734b97b550d44b13c63ed71dc7986","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/747f1003ddf734b97b550d44b13c63ed71dc7986"}]},{"sha":"747f1003ddf734b97b550d44b13c63ed71dc7986","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDc0N2YxMDAzZGRmNzM0Yjk3YjU1MGQ0NGIxM2M2M2VkNzFkYzc5ODY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Adam Perry @ OpenAI","email":"anp@openai.com","date":"2026-06-02T01:20:25Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-02T01:20:25Z"},"message":"[codex] Add comprehensive root formatting check (#25683)\n\n## Why\n\nThe root formatting entrypoints could drift: `just fmt` did not format\nthe Justfile itself, and the CI-facing check recipe only checked Python\nscripts instead of matching everything formatted by `just fmt`.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Add a shared cross-platform Python formatter driver used by both `just\nfmt` and `just fmt-check`.\n- Run Justfile, Rust, Python SDK, and internal-script formatter groups\nconcurrently while buffering each formatter group's output until it\nfinishes.\n- Log formatter starts immediately, then print each formatter group's\nlabeled output when it completes.\n- Keep the SDK lint-fix and Ruff formatting passes ordered, with source\ncomments explaining their distinct roles and the check-mode equivalents.\n- Run Ruff through shared `uv run --no-sync --with ruff` overlays so\nformatting works on clean glibc Linux checkouts without installing the\nplatform-specific SDK runtime wheel.\n- Show `fmt-check` help text in `just -l` and simplify CI to call the\nshared driver through `just fmt-check`.\n- Pin the general CI workflow to `just@1.51.0` so its formatter agrees\nwith the checked-in Justfile.\n- Add regression coverage for the thin Just recipes and the driver's\nformatter graph.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just fmt`\n- `just fmt-check`\n- `python3 -m pytest\nsdk/python/tests/test_artifact_workflow_and_binaries.py -k 'root_fmt or\nroot_format' -q`\n- `pnpm run format`\n- `git diff --check`\n- `just -l | rg -n '^    fmt|fmt-check'`\n- `uvx --from uv==0.7.22 uv run --frozen --project sdk/python --no-sync\n--with ruff ruff check --diff sdk/python`","tree":{"sha":"33c03f16aae2dad87ebfda263d1105069e194c37","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/33c03f16aae2dad87ebfda263d1105069e194c37"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/747f1003ddf734b97b550d44b13c63ed71dc7986","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHi/ZCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAGiQQADMifbvg8SS2A9PUuRSm0UbN\nQcOwzuP08cqVlqc+tIXfF0wzoSDLSkQBtb97PUs4piteioU/ODjG7aW5kGIoKm5R\ne2uMI6rvyxVjazUN+po65kTBt7hOIE5qfrmT8ZYE77k/OAhG1r8evy3Xfr0sgUf1\nboweYABHwnJMmmNqoKsChw03ZXIwGhjj45ipiI6g3L79aWdSe+Fg6WVqlNBdcK+N\ncOEiiuWAJlvbqPfjiSKZ6q2MglskzIyDwjMzQt4TJ//Pu82fbnz9QtDuPcPj82JE\n3GpyvUNC7Kd1CGG2Dt7hLpsBxGr07rp3gocTPKwC6+Q95J5g7tgRnu09YUzzJABb\nYQa//OVshIUMLS2wRpB+kWsf/WIq4EDVuM6j/9mdcxklb6Wdlzf6SazQloneIiXB\nYQhTU8THhDwn6GWP58Wiuzv2GJTvGnFAap6R6TW29xlOIh8J+2TwCcvGXUhuQaNR\n+WJwGbG8seTsJNmHODe6Z4PVnMJa72GTtp6keJWEEQ7Y2z+Na0PkVk1vIborRGJ3\n1zYoS6Pesw/9XwC9E32yJyWOGe/K4o2L5pGyE+Gwn2zfH95Q+SZrBat3CmDphhLw\nyFoLJTd0rMGjKzfs/gTwoiYmSFtm18khD6LH86PoZtwiPBPb19g0QAl7n1JXkS/l\nS6VfqpQg6h1O/ayZeI9T\n=d+Cr\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 33c03f16aae2dad87ebfda263d1105069e194c37\nparent 0002316687f63f3b9b0155cb9272eca13aae63e3\nauthor Adam Perry @ OpenAI <anp@openai.com> 1780363225 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780363225 +0000\n\n[codex] Add comprehensive root formatting check (#25683)\n\n## Why\n\nThe root formatting entrypoints could drift: `just fmt` did not format\nthe Justfile itself, and the CI-facing check recipe only checked Python\nscripts instead of matching everything formatted by `just fmt`.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Add a shared cross-platform Python formatter driver used by both `just\nfmt` and `just fmt-check`.\n- Run Justfile, Rust, Python SDK, and internal-script formatter groups\nconcurrently while buffering each formatter group's output until it\nfinishes.\n- Log formatter starts immediately, then print each formatter group's\nlabeled output when it completes.\n- Keep the SDK lint-fix and Ruff formatting passes ordered, with source\ncomments explaining their distinct roles and the check-mode equivalents.\n- Run Ruff through shared `uv run --no-sync --with ruff` overlays so\nformatting works on clean glibc Linux checkouts without installing the\nplatform-specific SDK runtime wheel.\n- Show `fmt-check` help text in `just -l` and simplify CI to call the\nshared driver through `just fmt-check`.\n- Pin the general CI workflow to `just@1.51.0` so its formatter agrees\nwith the checked-in Justfile.\n- Add regression coverage for the thin Just recipes and the driver's\nformatter graph.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just fmt`\n- `just fmt-check`\n- `python3 -m pytest\nsdk/python/tests/test_artifact_workflow_and_binaries.py -k 'root_fmt or\nroot_format' -q`\n- `pnpm run format`\n- `git diff --check`\n- `just -l | rg -n '^    fmt|fmt-check'`\n- `uvx --from uv==0.7.22 uv run --frozen --project sdk/python --no-sync\n--with ruff ruff check --diff sdk/python`","verified_at":"2026-06-02T01:20:25Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/747f1003ddf734b97b550d44b13c63ed71dc7986","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/747f1003ddf734b97b550d44b13c63ed71dc7986","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/747f1003ddf734b97b550d44b13c63ed71dc7986/comments","author":{"login":"anp-oai","id":286154589,"node_id":"U_kgDOEQ5fXQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/286154589?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/anp-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"0002316687f63f3b9b0155cb9272eca13aae63e3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/0002316687f63f3b9b0155cb9272eca13aae63e3","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/0002316687f63f3b9b0155cb9272eca13aae63e3"}]},{"sha":"0002316687f63f3b9b0155cb9272eca13aae63e3","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDAwMDIzMTY2ODdmNjNmM2I5YjAxNTVjYjkyNzJlY2ExM2FhZTYzZTM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Anton Panasenko","email":"apanasenko@openai.com","date":"2026-06-02T01:05:50Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-02T01:05:50Z"},"message":"feat(remote-control): add pairing start (#25675)\n\n## Why\n\nRemote control enrollment authorizes a desktop server, but app-server v2\ndid not expose the follow-up pairing operation needed to mint a\nshort-lived controller pairing artifact from that enrolled server.\nClients need a narrow RPC that starts pairing without exposing the\nbackend `serverId` or conflating pairing with websocket connection\nstate.\n\nIssue: N/A; internal remote-control pairing API change.\n\n## What Changed\n\nAdded experimental app-server v2 `remoteControl/pairing/start` with\n`manualCode` input and `pairingCode`, nullable `manualPairingCode`,\n`environmentId`, and Unix-seconds `expiresAt` output. The method\nserializes under its own `global(\"remote-control-pairing\")` scope and is\ndocumented in `app-server/README.md`.\n\nExtended the remote-control transport with private `/server/pair`\nrequest/response types and normalized `pair_url` handling. Pairing uses\nthe current enrolled server bearer, refreshes that bearer when needed,\nkeeps backend `server_id` private, validates returned `server_id` and\n`environment_id` against the current enrollment, and preserves backend\nstatus/header/body context for failures and malformed responses.\n\nWired the request through `RemoteControlRequestProcessor` and\n`MessageProcessor`, mapping unavailable/disabled pairing to\n`invalid_request` and backend failures to internal errors.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `just test -p codex-app-server-transport`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server\nremote_control_pairing_start_returns_pairing_artifacts`","tree":{"sha":"4a988d7b35d4b07b8f8eb83c4c410bce3085c78d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/4a988d7b35d4b07b8f8eb83c4c410bce3085c78d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/0002316687f63f3b9b0155cb9272eca13aae63e3","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHixuCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAYZcQAA2Z1za02qXpd9lhGyd1SkXZ\nGJ6Lfxwr01nKhEWioWKpKDDNpvtAKux4EM2s5HtGffdf0jBsgOmXAZg4Geyeecy3\nbUbCcfR5NaZuUeqzFQHer8+iE4eTWaNdbZ1AQpADSm7nCV3jEFEPnOX6wkHnACNj\nFI1rjQ0BMhAMRdCtp04DYf1Emo8Z8ocM6SLQixkSZ4Nth6nfD0NenqN4Hea8CLAo\nYjsGUVyQiTnkn0yEPpBMEL2sj7MJNHDvjecl0Z6zIi2ThyZVA50955q/DpDgdJfD\nXej44ZzPnzxFyega15G6nB6Q+yen/y+P9AdCYl9OCx6HBpsZg78FxPH+eClSoOKM\ngEK8UNbJC659auMMX+qu6CUWTjy2XgYOP71RmZEnI8zAHoyAHKGlbosHqboFuoGC\nIlH3zXAzR4Btx4paV3909s+swhyACThbsRzJlm5Dm8gI8HLcLo968XjkLlUZn/vd\nFvr7SYl/UEJgRvTzhwhTDmk4d4Pzj/hgfvj4F0EfY+1Nz77sg9l5Yu5PyNpyhCKH\nkp95tFsUelpqAMxIEQjAsc3mys5lagdK6cxGN2TXi0B3OLowhkzWVylhbU6Dffj9\n7ymq5chsqwBqH/17qm/GgAoowo0EjMOhkWZaT/FmBqL2pcxlndJqy5vvaHBoI64Z\nE9cv64ETlmrXm+wiZ7dz\n=QTtu\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 4a988d7b35d4b07b8f8eb83c4c410bce3085c78d\nparent 1ad0d7aa4b92b8bfcae0272a29609b27fc334ad9\nauthor Anton Panasenko <apanasenko@openai.com> 1780362350 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780362350 +0000\n\nfeat(remote-control): add pairing start (#25675)\n\n## Why\n\nRemote control enrollment authorizes a desktop server, but app-server v2\ndid not expose the follow-up pairing operation needed to mint a\nshort-lived controller pairing artifact from that enrolled server.\nClients need a narrow RPC that starts pairing without exposing the\nbackend `serverId` or conflating pairing with websocket connection\nstate.\n\nIssue: N/A; internal remote-control pairing API change.\n\n## What Changed\n\nAdded experimental app-server v2 `remoteControl/pairing/start` with\n`manualCode` input and `pairingCode`, nullable `manualPairingCode`,\n`environmentId`, and Unix-seconds `expiresAt` output. The method\nserializes under its own `global(\"remote-control-pairing\")` scope and is\ndocumented in `app-server/README.md`.\n\nExtended the remote-control transport with private `/server/pair`\nrequest/response types and normalized `pair_url` handling. Pairing uses\nthe current enrolled server bearer, refreshes that bearer when needed,\nkeeps backend `server_id` private, validates returned `server_id` and\n`environment_id` against the current enrollment, and preserves backend\nstatus/header/body context for failures and malformed responses.\n\nWired the request through `RemoteControlRequestProcessor` and\n`MessageProcessor`, mapping unavailable/disabled pairing to\n`invalid_request` and backend failures to internal errors.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `just test -p codex-app-server-transport`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server\nremote_control_pairing_start_returns_pairing_artifacts`","verified_at":"2026-06-02T01:05:50Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/0002316687f63f3b9b0155cb9272eca13aae63e3","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/0002316687f63f3b9b0155cb9272eca13aae63e3","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/0002316687f63f3b9b0155cb9272eca13aae63e3/comments","author":{"login":"apanasenko-oai","id":228802911,"node_id":"U_kgDODaNBXw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228802911?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/apanasenko-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/apanasenko-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apanasenko-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apanasenko-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apanasenko-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apanasenko-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apanasenko-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apanasenko-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apanasenko-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apanasenko-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apanasenko-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https: