27fc334ad9","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHiGWCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAATfwQACG76WCzRuDQ/s0sDpxE03zd\ndPvLpdt+eIC7cVAWvuh3Xcf4av1kwWoU2NMUSMTQBMKcDGO3CBMXyado/Yl8eoMV\nFf/iaATks2lkb/XdZteDdEsD4iMrkz99HENGtPnYhsTRDgX45c9Qxdeli1K0lrL5\n3mUoSbSHqpMNRX9g9YW46cWKbJTSdHWh9vHpCdmQlYblmIWbuG4Te782cXatVn2s\nAQ9+jbzDbN196bzgFBw/00JFhpljhff84wgVtc8FffJhDqD4BEMdGFl19makxkX+\ncNFHw5O0/XCUYDjowZ/BNd69m7HhKbBf+g6Jt4bNmgT+YSjKK05X3eKSwKaQ8DMC\n/28CWqOJc2gy0THt3wEoJphe1XDZGGt17yclKYI3SSwsdixdM4hmQsyYAzU5HcLB\nr2PH1AAlxXx+3fU7gfSIKSF9DvLWAR+bDNLfrucY/yGzV0O8bVi2B4SdW9EFJlnJ\n/TdfuALM2TeJFaz/FuUjH0mwF5oHfiE0Vc/Z3uhW1WboLQM+TjaKCPWnqt3E6epw\n7esvThJNWha5bAAylN2L6J0dnGf7cQqRQdqX1wydBuxDPjcRN8GGl6EBqsoeKsSk\nWs0oiHY1moBrahZCjrBvPpkLp+eaVeFpMJorw2MCm0YtADQVmfunbNrvhLD9vcV8\nTOHcSL8xdNrCYyXWYXBJ\n=SrS2\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree b1ffd08b7c8c8568b6b8a6e634755417be0a1108\nparent 0b3a6f71850daf6414670e1893638acb809bc0b8\nauthor xli-oai <xli@openai.com> 1780359574 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780359574 -0700\n\nHandle invalid plugin skills manifest field (#25717)\n\n## Summary\n- Treat invalid `plugin.json` `skills` shapes as a field-level warning\ninstead of rejecting the whole manifest\n- Keep valid string path behavior unchanged and continue falling back to\nthe default `skills/` root\n- Add regression coverage for array-shaped `skills`\n\n## Tests\n- `just fmt`\n- `cargo test -p codex-core-plugins`","verified_at":"2026-06-02T00:19:35Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/1ad0d7aa4b92b8bfcae0272a29609b27fc334ad9","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/1ad0d7aa4b92b8bfcae0272a29609b27fc334ad9","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/1ad0d7aa4b92b8bfcae0272a29609b27fc334ad9/comments","author":{"login":"xli-oai","id":270779301,"node_id":"U_kgDOECPDpQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/270779301?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/xli-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/xli-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xli-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xli-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xli-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xli-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xli-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xli-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xli-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xli-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xli-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"0b3a6f71850daf6414670e1893638acb809bc0b8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/0b3a6f71850daf6414670e1893638acb809bc0b8","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/0b3a6f71850daf6414670e1893638acb809bc0b8"}]},{"sha":"0b3a6f71850daf6414670e1893638acb809bc0b8","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDBiM2E2ZjcxODUwZGFmNjQxNDY3MGUxODkzNjM4YWNiODA5YmMwYjg","commit":{"author":{"name":"joeflorencio-openai","email":"joeflorencio@openai.com","date":"2026-06-01T23:43:52Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-01T23:43:52Z"},"message":"Move cloud requirements crate to cloud config (#24621)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Moves the existing `codex-cloud-requirements` crate to\n`codex-cloud-config`.\n- Updates workspace dependencies and imports to the new crate name.\n- Intentionally keeps runtime behavior unchanged: this still fetches the\nlegacy cloud requirements endpoint.\n\n## Details\n\nThis PR exists to make the lineage obvious before the bundle migration.\nGitHub should show the old `codex-rs/cloud-requirements/src/lib.rs`\nimplementation as moved to `codex-rs/cloud-config/src/lib.rs`, rather\nthan as unrelated new code.\n\nThe follow-up PR adapts this moved crate to the new config bundle API\nand switches runtime consumers over.","tree":{"sha":"6458cccb8c64c96484f4dee803aedce88b93ca01","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/6458cccb8c64c96484f4dee803aedce88b93ca01"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/0b3a6f71850daf6414670e1893638acb809bc0b8","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHhk4CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA96cQAHitdFQ81uCep7QhpbtoBL+o\n4zsh+wYLLU3cR/HAiJxNZdGepTdQt1trpSAyS1JMil6WJanaCOI0kd/FMVbxBncX\nUp2WTLctaPZht2hD8VD1mDd0C6rzenaGgtHU4LQqmJjrVVIUjl0nhPgG7pv60AsB\nopRWls0xO6KimncsBwyYkr98IT4IDdC7Nu3+DYhkcOAh+bqd+M1TZfqJMPkYRay2\nK3taEYIhoZR2EnfeMVxQDeBvkJA7iwv+aGRacs9nagyWuWtITtz1lrW4dpZT0bA+\nFAU9CA2fpC5urP50jntMb6dUxPMSmjmWA7k0aH/d8oJ8LCwqkkqi76Db1gGZLfjA\n/PkMdaBUf6dHUwPJ+RPRgBG/WloFovfxYkt0/RQDEeUqPrTJOLnYCR3phfmlAnTV\nyx7mfZjJFG9n0vx9XyhYERG90p5bjjERkhLsS/6aV2mPYAq7jmioJTSYzAaR3lg7\n9w3JdwXiSGkYn838HSaLpovA2gYVHYq3Qo1XNezcnZI/l1Y6Lr4kTZT2UD4R7Jc4\neZ95YIr18CLhEJvE/EX7/xEl8vC+K4sdQIZsfai8ZyH2jvMUbk3jDaNc1bH3Fn/o\nUxvIPO8zU4UikNVHYhLUJxFu0zQ+ogqACdao+qY9G5WxuTsY9TKChT51eY2+TjnZ\nY9Xqiz4tzUb1h9HhgIhB\n=dkPg\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 6458cccb8c64c96484f4dee803aedce88b93ca01\nparent 11e0f3d3aecf631715b18581095d16c8b8f101e7\nauthor joeflorencio-openai <joeflorencio@openai.com> 1780357432 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780357432 -0700\n\nMove cloud requirements crate to cloud config (#24621)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Moves the existing `codex-cloud-requirements` crate to\n`codex-cloud-config`.\n- Updates workspace dependencies and imports to the new crate name.\n- Intentionally keeps runtime behavior unchanged: this still fetches the\nlegacy cloud requirements endpoint.\n\n## Details\n\nThis PR exists to make the lineage obvious before the bundle migration.\nGitHub should show the old `codex-rs/cloud-requirements/src/lib.rs`\nimplementation as moved to `codex-rs/cloud-config/src/lib.rs`, rather\nthan as unrelated new code.\n\nThe follow-up PR adapts this moved crate to the new config bundle API\nand switches runtime consumers over.","verified_at":"2026-06-01T23:43:52Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/0b3a6f71850daf6414670e1893638acb809bc0b8","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/0b3a6f71850daf6414670e1893638acb809bc0b8","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/0b3a6f71850daf6414670e1893638acb809bc0b8/comments","author":{"login":"joeflorencio-openai","id":195963627,"node_id":"U_kgDOC64q6w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/195963627?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/joeflorencio-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"11e0f3d3aecf631715b18581095d16c8b8f101e7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/11e0f3d3aecf631715b18581095d16c8b8f101e7","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/11e0f3d3aecf631715b18581095d16c8b8f101e7"}]},{"sha":"11e0f3d3aecf631715b18581095d16c8b8f101e7","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDExZTBmM2QzYWVjZjYzMTcxNWIxODU4MTA5NWQxNmM4YjhmMTAxZTc","commit":{"author":{"name":"Owen Lin","email":"owenlin0@gmail.com","date":"2026-06-01T23:33:42Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-01T23:33:42Z"},"message":"app-server: remove experimental persist_extended_history bool flag (#25712)\n\n## Summary\n\nRemove the dead experimental `persistExtendedHistory` app-server flag\nand collapse rollout persistence to the single policy app-server already\nused.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Removed `persistExtendedHistory` from v2 thread start/resume/fork\nparams and deleted its deprecation notice path.\n- Removed the persistence-mode enums and plumbing through core, rollout,\nand thread-store.\n- Made rollout filtering mode-free, keeping the existing limited\npersisted-history behavior.\n\n## Test Plan\n\n- `just write-app-server-schema`\n- `cargo nextest run --no-fail-fast -p codex-app-server-protocol\nschema_fixtures`\n- `cargo nextest run --no-fail-fast -p codex-app-server\nthread_shell_command_history_responses_exclude_persisted_command_executions`\n- `cargo nextest run --no-fail-fast -p codex-rollout -p\ncodex-thread-store`\n- final `rg` for removed flag/type names","tree":{"sha":"a48592961d3b8df7b5b185939c103e9418630e29","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/a48592961d3b8df7b5b185939c103e9418630e29"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/11e0f3d3aecf631715b18581095d16c8b8f101e7","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHhbWCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAOlwQAFFvzXtyfM+t/UN/a6sbdihw\n8flKkcP4z1LzvyT/traA0cvr0twVrcUv2NsCSDsSM3hafUcJdLyKfg+Q7opCe0WG\n8hErqtw+mdsxDDFa3rsI5fTgeOCU+KT7P3wibKalxxjsN6is4p8BiDcVsmEeZbjG\nFkcY9P6h9rSRXyFBpHuI+t1eNn07Yu/NWZAij97wo0O5nXMRxuAfO9Ktzzx9GVpM\nXYf+jecDMW2uB6NBLy2r3NnQck5TqsTcikWTSLtJjM86aiEnvm6I3TH9jeIxlb2C\niO2BDeG/MeOZ5CkxRA0ORL2X6cxvMmXjW4iNjQCXmZ8UtGHiiaIj5ZykaZFcrKS5\n+AWS5Yt9RfUJP7mQg34D5G6vzJIZFhH2iDoJk31UBilU3o7ocnPl9Fiyw6OKSKbY\nQrJsROMPNOO/UJx7TLqSz4o05GDlFr5MrBnjMhs0aHO+Pn8UsG8cNeYlUWu3HBmV\naBG5YO+9D/OUw6yRcA+c76tKB/sTCw+3a6LpU8C5Cb+F70mpqUY0tA0uECFsxsDf\nMaQryx7Zu/BaK5ybzjiP4vdbQbFodiCn0eoWHjA47zUSS9joycZ1xO37xxs6TaqC\n1hdqa5cRAd2L2Cu3pXbmhJRlP8G0Pcsu8CyxR4//mDrHTCZ1ohWkGR7zx2n+gOVy\n8/xfEa3wAvu9lXNQjakO\n=mxS9\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a48592961d3b8df7b5b185939c103e9418630e29\nparent bca18cba40a601bc462b7079a06ae486e41a3afa\nauthor Owen Lin <owenlin0@gmail.com> 1780356822 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780356822 +0000\n\napp-server: remove experimental persist_extended_history bool flag (#25712)\n\n## Summary\n\nRemove the dead experimental `persistExtendedHistory` app-server flag\nand collapse rollout persistence to the single policy app-server already\nused.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Removed `persistExtendedHistory` from v2 thread start/resume/fork\nparams and deleted its deprecation notice path.\n- Removed the persistence-mode enums and plumbing through core, rollout,\nand thread-store.\n- Made rollout filtering mode-free, keeping the existing limited\npersisted-history behavior.\n\n## Test Plan\n\n- `just write-app-server-schema`\n- `cargo nextest run --no-fail-fast -p codex-app-server-protocol\nschema_fixtures`\n- `cargo nextest run --no-fail-fast -p codex-app-server\nthread_shell_command_history_responses_exclude_persisted_command_executions`\n- `cargo nextest run --no-fail-fast -p codex-rollout -p\ncodex-thread-store`\n- final `rg` for removed flag/type names","verified_at":"2026-06-01T23:33:43Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/11e0f3d3aecf631715b18581095d16c8b8f101e7","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/11e0f3d3aecf631715b18581095d16c8b8f101e7","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/11e0f3d3aecf631715b18581095d16c8b8f101e7/comments","author":{"login":"owenlin0","id":947871,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk0Nzg3MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/947871?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0","html_url":"https://github.com/owenlin0","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"bca18cba40a601bc462b7079a06ae486e41a3afa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/bca18cba40a601bc462b7079a06ae486e41a3afa","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/bca18cba40a601bc462b7079a06ae486e41a3afa"}]},{"sha":"bca18cba40a601bc462b7079a06ae486e41a3afa","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGJjYTE4Y2JhNDBhNjAxYmM0NjJiNzA3OWEwNmFlNDg2ZTQxYTNhZmE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Winston Howes","email":"winston@openai.com","date":"2026-06-01T23:23:59Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-01T23:23:59Z"},"message":"Wire managed MITM CA trust into child env (#22668)\n\n## Stack\n1. Parent PR: #18240 uses named MITM permissions config.\n2. This PR wires managed MITM CA trust into spawned child processes.\n\n## Why\nWhen Codex terminates HTTPS for limited mode or MITM hooks, child HTTPS\nclients need to trust Codex's managed MITM CA. Exporting proxy URLs\nalone is not enough, but blindly replacing user CA settings would be\nwrong: it can break custom enterprise/test roots, leak unreadable CA\nfiles into generated bundles, or make the child env disagree with its\nsandbox policy.\n\n## Summary\n1. Build immutable managed CA bundles under `$CODEX_HOME/proxy` that\ninclude native roots, the managed MITM CA, and only inherited or\ncommand-scoped CA bundles the child is allowed to read.\n2. Export curated CA env vars alongside managed proxy env vars while\npreserving user CA override semantics, including nested Codex\n`SSL_CERT_FILE` precedence.\n3. Thread generated CA bundle paths into child sandbox readable roots,\nincluding debug sandbox execution, so the exported env vars work inside\nsandboxed commands.\n4. Remove only Codex-generated MITM CA bundle env when a child\nintentionally drops managed proxying for escalation or no-proxy retry.\n5. Document the managed CA bundle behavior and cover env injection,\nper-child bundle generation, sandbox readable roots, and no-proxy\ncleanup in tests.\n\n## Validation\n1. Ran `just test -p codex-network-proxy`.\n2. Ran `just test -p codex-protocol`.\n3. Ran `just fix -p codex-network-proxy -p codex-protocol`.\n4. Tried focused `codex-core` validation, but the crate currently fails\nto compile in `core/tests/suite/guardian_review.rs` because an existing\n`Op::UserInput` initializer is missing `additional_context`.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Eva Wong <evawong@openai.com>","tree":{"sha":"ed1e585123d6bef5dc460b3b8d745273bbb19ef9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/ed1e585123d6bef5dc460b3b8d745273bbb19ef9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/bca18cba40a601bc462b7079a06ae486e41a3afa","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHhSPCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAgtkQAK7Jq7snmLhjlpe6gIfw5mjn\n+mJr0s3cJjdyrazU5u1ujtZCUuGiJzI9rZN+i3CGWTM3R2pHfH9gdHL1lZTVTBiW\n/eslz7QxnNP77I0jbxkU3UN/1Q6uwUHB7YoLVm15d7Pq9hG67QK5NSFI33O239T3\nZAf/HDQIYEkp2bDjNCuBr6+LdQntQnVO9W+xeW0WOjmjc4e1Atri1q9YxkLEy6U0\n0fI53rEPEzyRQH1Iu48RI6mI//sukXCgiEA6657Ws3HxGV3OQ3RvUdnEkgPF9QG3\nSDGE+a3e5CmTeQaxvEnGTyoCsBOcDCRylZCs9qq3NBE4i5/qFGVu1KXw1/xLJ1EB\nZQmL/fiVk/3unkXqz61wxRz1JfAMZ0zMNPdNJvFNvb+RqhC7PmMLZBtALT3VE0yj\n+D+KIp5lH/+CwAsLlK5evrThPLvAuiG7+ZyQlIobDVv3avmXpl3zVDeTQBEJ+Ekg\nBajz5qzif7UX1zuHJK8wJ/w9eqJ5rUI5gXKnFKdPr/DM4H6vdnTtN02ZmC1zTztA\ng7cJeWcdGKPPDjez3lPdbCqtVfoReY16B9xpb8Ikn8wbsxLEe1wB1syBG2qiekFE\n21mrGSh+vbV7qMBby0j3jOwU6L2qOWGcstnFDHjGhZ1AFWJXzm+9CPfqGlpOfLCX\n4y+W6IrJX9sU0wPQXJ4k\n=ffwA\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree ed1e585123d6bef5dc460b3b8d745273bbb19ef9\nparent b89bf1ef47240cff4d646caca6f8f9ca223c5ca4\nauthor Winston Howes <winston@openai.com> 1780356239 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780356239 +0000\n\nWire managed MITM CA trust into child env (#22668)\n\n## Stack\n1. Parent PR: #18240 uses named MITM permissions config.\n2. This PR wires managed MITM CA trust into spawned child processes.\n\n## Why\nWhen Codex terminates HTTPS for limited mode or MITM hooks, child HTTPS\nclients need to trust Codex's managed MITM CA. Exporting proxy URLs\nalone is not enough, but blindly replacing user CA settings would be\nwrong: it can break custom enterprise/test roots, leak unreadable CA\nfiles into generated bundles, or make the child env disagree with its\nsandbox policy.\n\n## Summary\n1. Build immutable managed CA bundles under `$CODEX_HOME/proxy` that\ninclude native roots, the managed MITM CA, and only inherited or\ncommand-scoped CA bundles the child is allowed to read.\n2. Export curated CA env vars alongside managed proxy env vars while\npreserving user CA override semantics, including nested Codex\n`SSL_CERT_FILE` precedence.\n3. Thread generated CA bundle paths into child sandbox readable roots,\nincluding debug sandbox execution, so the exported env vars work inside\nsandboxed commands.\n4. Remove only Codex-generated MITM CA bundle env when a child\nintentionally drops managed proxying for escalation or no-proxy retry.\n5. Document the managed CA bundle behavior and cover env injection,\nper-child bundle generation, sandbox readable roots, and no-proxy\ncleanup in tests.\n\n## Validation\n1. Ran `just test -p codex-network-proxy`.\n2. Ran `just test -p codex-protocol`.\n3. Ran `just fix -p codex-network-proxy -p codex-protocol`.\n4. Tried focused `codex-core` validation, but the crate currently fails\nto compile in `core/tests/suite/guardian_review.rs` because an existing\n`Op::UserInput` initializer is missing `additional_context`.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Eva Wong <evawong@openai.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-01T23:24:00Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/bca18cba40a601bc462b7079a06ae486e41a3afa","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/bca18cba40a601bc462b7079a06ae486e41a3afa","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/bca18cba40a601bc462b7079a06ae486e41a3afa/comments","author":{"login":"winston-openai","id":177672674,"node_id":"U_kgDOCpcR4g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/177672674?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/winston-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"b89bf1ef47240cff4d646caca6f8f9ca223c5ca4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/b89bf1ef47240cff4d646caca6f8f9ca223c5ca4","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/b89bf1ef47240cff4d646caca6f8f9ca223c5ca4"}]},{"sha":"b89bf1ef47240cff4d646caca6f8f9ca223c5ca4","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGI4OWJmMWVmNDcyNDBjZmY0ZDY0NmNhY2E2ZjhmOWNhMjIzYzVjYTQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Michael Bolin","email":"mbolin@openai.com","date":"2026-06-01T23:02:06Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-01T23:02:06Z"},"message":"Reject directory rollout paths for pathless side chats (#25661)\n\n## Why\n\nFixes openai/codex#20944.\n\nDesktop side chats are intentionally ephemeral and pathless. They can\nstill accept live turns while loaded, but after a reload there is no\npersisted rollout to resume. In the reported failure mode, Desktop could\nsend `$CODEX_HOME` as the resume/fork path for one of these pathless\nside chats.\n\n`thread/resume` and `thread/fork` prefer an explicit `path` over\n`threadId`, and rollout path lookup only checked that a candidate\nexisted. That let `$CODEX_HOME` pass as a rollout path, so the later\nrollout reader tried to open a directory and surfaced the low-level `Is\na directory` error.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Reject explicit rollout paths that resolve to a directory or other\nnon-file before attempting to read rollout history.\n- Make `codex_rollout::existing_rollout_path` return only plain or\ncompressed rollout candidates that are actual files.\n- Add an app-server regression test that creates an ephemeral fork, runs\na turn while the side thread is loaded, simulates reload, then verifies\nboth `thread/resume` and `thread/fork` reject `$CODEX_HOME` with `path\nis a directory` instead of the OS-level directory-read error.\n- Rebase over the `TestAppServer` rename and update the remaining stale\ntest harness call sites to use `TestAppServer` with `app_server` local\nvariables.\n\nRelevant code:\n\n- `thread-store/src/local/read_thread.rs` validates explicit rollout\npaths before rollout reading:\nhttps://github.com/openai/codex/blob/25b47c8f425d351aaba4baa955a8092064a1707b/codex-rs/thread-store/src/local/read_thread.rs#L146-L165\n- `rollout/src/compression.rs` now requires file metadata for plain and\ncompressed rollout candidates:\nhttps://github.com/openai/codex/blob/25b47c8f425d351aaba4baa955a8092064a1707b/codex-rs/rollout/src/compression.rs#L940-L950\n- The repro test covers the pathless ephemeral side-chat reload case:\nhttps://github.com/openai/codex/blob/25b47c8f425d351aaba4baa955a8092064a1707b/codex-rs/app-server/tests/suite/v2/thread_fork.rs#L774-L886\n\n## Verification\n\n- `just test -p codex-app-server\npathless_ephemeral_thread_rejects_codex_home_path_after_reload`","tree":{"sha":"1024b34205da24060e95e95b1cd5c55f3d3ad83b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/1024b34205da24060e95e95b1cd5c55f3d3ad83b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/b89bf1ef47240cff4d646caca6f8f9ca223c5ca4","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHg9vCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAYFMQAA8/jqtxZGAQ0migNUz4VUi1\nx4JFpsan3Fh9nSNoDI/2pAnvQfbvwUtce1gBQbk1D/ccGcrCqzJ1sLD51osjj2pn\njGWaUoBlo7jrqgrz4bwOVWa9x5zsMmX2MI5PdnG0dDbvhKdbnYsUNmSKCaOSa8b0\nSojHCEj6IVALKKqyxBrN9QKNlrzGclBi4v/4K6D8JnCXb0mltEtg3JkAm4yzWEJ7\nrxmH+Sf1D7aBPNLGR6z0k8h0IszyAFUPF7xIgsWZC232UqZbw5PUeX0c58Z1v/U3\nVqWzgB8uIb73p9RNn0LX4FKn4eJHn1cna7O1u7pqVTsvWl5UXJMrLfJN2r/panTr\nLX5vizxhPIFTEiuFOD/SKzeUxQU7hWMbIDW+Fd65oRm1xROn4PH0Qi+5vIV+mMzk\nU6xsI8ZfuYLNRAaOozVGjlM5/00uBPFHD7iESgXNVbdOkXO9HgGsBsvdUzBypMCh\nIzuFxdd03qDeqZ+qkDvUZjciE2TLbIEmxDUkBFEr0dQDNsQPZjel3t0cIG6dANxm\nMJNi03dSmWAvvBRDtmYXEUXFJ74nI0knCqFT8hYX2qkpJJ0/kdHdgYSfuoSBVIqB\nILDgNjX6Z8i6JG3alShj8r08PV+bZBQ0yRwUGphcMGkfkpjEKyo2KHXikMRAzJUt\nNJxa3DL7d7bb3JKlZbS+\n=ZP53\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 1024b34205da24060e95e95b1cd5c55f3d3ad83b\nparent 75a08def9808ed5b77b458d09c2fe99f2b52c433\nauthor Michael Bolin <mbolin@openai.com> 1780354926 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780354926 -0700\n\nReject directory rollout paths for pathless side chats (#25661)\n\n## Why\n\nFixes openai/codex#20944.\n\nDesktop side chats are intentionally ephemeral and pathless. They can\nstill accept live turns while loaded, but after a reload there is no\npersisted rollout to resume. In the reported failure mode, Desktop could\nsend `$CODEX_HOME` as the resume/fork path for one of these pathless\nside chats.\n\n`thread/resume` and `thread/fork` prefer an explicit `path` over\n`threadId`, and rollout path lookup only checked that a candidate\nexisted. That let `$CODEX_HOME` pass as a rollout path, so the later\nrollout reader tried to open a directory and surfaced the low-level `Is\na directory` error.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Reject explicit rollout paths that resolve to a directory or other\nnon-file before attempting to read rollout history.\n- Make `codex_rollout::existing_rollout_path` return only plain or\ncompressed rollout candidates that are actual files.\n- Add an app-server regression test that creates an ephemeral fork, runs\na turn while the side thread is loaded, simulates reload, then verifies\nboth `thread/resume` and `thread/fork` reject `$CODEX_HOME` with `path\nis a directory` instead of the OS-level directory-read error.\n- Rebase over the `TestAppServer` rename and update the remaining stale\ntest harness call sites to use `TestAppServer` with `app_server` local\nvariables.\n\nRelevant code:\n\n- `thread-store/src/local/read_thread.rs` validates explicit rollout\npaths before rollout reading:\nhttps://github.com/openai/codex/blob/25b47c8f425d351aaba4baa955a8092064a1707b/codex-rs/thread-store/src/local/read_thread.rs#L146-L165\n- `rollout/src/compression.rs` now requires file metadata for plain and\ncompressed rollout candidates:\nhttps://github.com/openai/codex/blob/25b47c8f425d351aaba4baa955a8092064a1707b/codex-rs/rollout/src/compression.rs#L940-L950\n- The repro test covers the pathless ephemeral side-chat reload case:\nhttps://github.com/openai/codex/blob/25b47c8f425d351aaba4baa955a8092064a1707b/codex-rs/app-server/tests/suite/v2/thread_fork.rs#L774-L886\n\n## Verification\n\n- `just test -p codex-app-server\npathless_ephemeral_thread_rejects_codex_home_path_after_reload`","verified_at":"2026-06-01T23:02:07Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/b89bf1ef47240cff4d646caca6f8f9ca223c5ca4","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/b89bf1ef47240cff4d646caca6f8f9ca223c5ca4","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/b89bf1ef47240cff4d646caca6f8f9ca223c5ca4/comments","author":{"login":"bolinfest","id":655869,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTg2OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/655869?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest","html_url":"https://github.com/bolinfest","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"75a08def9808ed5b77b458d09c2fe99f2b52c433","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/75a08def9808ed5b77b458d09c2fe99f2b52c433","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/75a08def9808ed5b77b458d09c2fe99f2b52c433"}]},{"sha":"75a08def9808ed5b77b458d09c2fe99f2b52c433","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDc1YTA4ZGVmOTgwOGVkNWI3N2I0NThkMDljMmZlOTlmMmI1MmM0MzM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Jeremy Rose","email":"172423086+nornagon-openai@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-01T22:49:54Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-01T22:49:54Z"},"message":"[codex] Publish release symbol artifacts (#25649)\n\n## Why\n\nProduction Codex binaries are stripped for distribution, which leaves\ncrashes and samples from released builds without the symbols needed for\nuseful stack traces. Publish symbols as separate release assets so\nproduction artifacts stay small while released builds remain\nsymbolicateable.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Add `.github/scripts/archive-release-symbols-and-strip-binaries.sh` to\npackage platform-native symbols into `codex-symbols-<artifact>.tar.gz`\nassets while stripping the corresponding Unix binaries before signing.\n- Build release binaries with full debug information before producing\ndistribution artifacts.\n- Publish macOS `.dSYM` bundles, Linux `.debug` files with\n`.gnu_debuglink`, and Windows `.pdb` files.\n- Strip Linux `bwrap` before computing its packaged-resource digest, but\nintentionally omit `bwrap` from symbol archives.\n- Preserve symbols artifacts in the unsigned macOS promotion flow.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Ran `shellcheck` and `bash -n` on\n`.github/scripts/archive-release-symbols-and-strip-binaries.sh`.\n- Parsed the modified workflow YAML files and ran `git diff --check`.\n- Built a macOS release smoke binary and verified that the archived\n`.dSYM` contains DWARF application source information and has the same\nUUID as the stripped production binary.\n- Built Linux smoke binaries and verified that the symbol archive\ncontains `codex.debug`, excludes `bwrap.debug`, leaves the expected\n`.gnu_debuglink` in `codex`, and does not mutate the separately stripped\n`bwrap` digest.\n- Staged a Windows smoke archive and verified that it contains the\nexpected `.pdb` file.","tree":{"sha":"d216f23a2e8c5629e11bed3449fcdbe3da8beb59","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/d216f23a2e8c5629e11bed3449fcdbe3da8beb59"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/75a08def9808ed5b77b458d09c2fe99f2b52c433","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHgySCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAhhkQAIQe72gLZcQOxRk/sr8CTu6x\ndWN+ts6YzOXXhIJXxWrWwVJM2XJPZIQ9WBIjNFFzq00XQDDqSRHD5/m1u34W1CJq\n+8iywBQdCUU54qsXDHFYvVvBrbEjCJkpoY/6YL2RaTTh9Q7pw6GO+wcv1ChxuNi7\nhzb47I6haiGWL89mSJUg6LJ/amO7NM/IQOWLnT94MnPqto+Ugw8JMaZGRPbI1+w4\n5wP9iqbk8NsWvB9q0igsNy2l39goYzp7xKy/ZeNbjHeKMlDDUsK6Z+xGtkfWHuTJ\nAseMBp0JubazUPxrd3JvtAh9Na+HBosdmoEIHZOs2JdNBTmKQ1nh477jwCbe8T/b\nm7QAmKCSnK3CXMw3YS/UNn/jfF1Uh8fq+pywlH6wzboi7ODc6mckZcHfWXE4oGpr\ngYlTiyXsfSUYpsOjlsAoSkA18X74kHWiHGoi/vSzU3jnB9arvudpnreB/q+Zmh5v\n5Ah9w5R7iLeNLD5t62zhvQd+b9MijoXzOI6bBIe5KEcy6odlI+SlTBo2hl4XlzIa\nmzTTeXB//0zWX/7imDlWAHFTTN95vJWyKRbLj/8T/M4XwU/PT547V/70VLggUQ4s\nuY5UNq0tUqM+B5W2gSpb5AwcLXPtWAISHIyYUmChgZslLbHAh73SYEuFg2/K5RGe\nwZaaBg4hi6nzZH1vylH0\n=krxH\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree d216f23a2e8c5629e11bed3449fcdbe3da8beb59\nparent 4e540b107690989ea20832f85cd7f121492f5b74\nauthor Jeremy Rose <172423086+nornagon-openai@users.noreply.github.com> 1780354194 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780354194 -0700\n\n[codex] Publish release symbol artifacts (#25649)\n\n## Why\n\nProduction Codex binaries are stripped for distribution, which leaves\ncrashes and samples from released builds without the symbols needed for\nuseful stack traces. Publish symbols as separate release assets so\nproduction artifacts stay small while released builds remain\nsymbolicateable.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Add `.github/scripts/archive-release-symbols-and-strip-binaries.sh` to\npackage platform-native symbols into `codex-symbols-<artifact>.tar.gz`\nassets while stripping the corresponding Unix binaries before signing.\n- Build release binaries with full debug information before producing\ndistribution artifacts.\n- Publish macOS `.dSYM` bundles, Linux `.debug` files with\n`.gnu_debuglink`, and Windows `.pdb` files.\n- Strip Linux `bwrap` before computing its packaged-resource digest, but\nintentionally omit `bwrap` from symbol archives.\n- Preserve symbols artifacts in the unsigned macOS promotion flow.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Ran `shellcheck` and `bash -n` on\n`.github/scripts/archive-release-symbols-and-strip-binaries.sh`.\n- Parsed the modified workflow YAML files and ran `git diff --check`.\n- Built a macOS release smoke binary and verified that the archived\n`.dSYM` contains DWARF application source information and has the same\nUUID as the stripped production binary.\n- Built Linux smoke binaries and verified that the symbol archive\ncontains `codex.debug`, excludes `bwrap.debug`, leaves the expected\n`.gnu_debuglink` in `codex`, and does not mutate the separately stripped\n`bwrap` digest.\n- Staged a Windows smoke archive and verified that it contains the\nexpected `.pdb` file.","verified_at":"2026-06-01T22:49:55Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/75a08def9808ed5b77b458d09c2fe99f2b52c433","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/75a08def9808ed5b77b458d09c2fe99f2b52c433","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/75a08def9808ed5b77b458d09c2fe99f2b52c433/comments","author":{"login":"nornagon-openai","id":172423086,"node_id":"U_kgDOCkb3rg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/172423086?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nornagon-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/nornagon-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nornagon-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nornagon-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nornagon-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nornagon-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nornagon-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nornagon-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nornagon-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nornagon-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nornagon-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"4e540b107690989ea20832f85cd7f121492f5b74","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4e540b107690989ea20832f85cd7f121492f5b74","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/4e540b107690989ea20832f85cd7f121492f5b74"}]},{"sha":"4e540b107690989ea20832f85cd7f121492f5b74","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDRlNTQwYjEwNzY5MDk4OWVhMjA4MzJmODVjZDdmMTIxNDkyZjViNzQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Felipe Coury","email":"felipe.coury@openai.com","date":"2026-06-01T22:41:22Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-01T22:41:22Z"},"message":"fix(tui): clarify footer shortcut overlay hints (#25625)\n\n## Why\n\nThe TUI shortcut overlay used static labels for `Tab` and `Ctrl+C`, even\nthough both keys change behavior while a task is running. That made the\nvisible help misleading: idle `Tab` submits rather than queues, and\nactive-turn `Ctrl+C` interrupts rather than exits.\n\nCloses #25531.\nCloses #25564.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Pass task-running state into the shortcut overlay renderer.\n- Render `Tab` as `submit message` while idle and `queue message` while\nwork is running.\n- Render `Ctrl+C` as `exit` while idle and `interrupt` while work is\nrunning.\n- Add snapshot coverage for the active-work shortcut overlay and update\nidle overlay snapshots.\n\n## How to Test\n\n1. Start Codex and open the shortcut overlay with `?` while no task is\nrunning.\n2. Confirm the overlay shows `tab to submit message` and `ctrl + c to\nexit`.\n3. Start a task, then open or keep the shortcut overlay visible while\nwork is running.\n4. Confirm the overlay shows `tab to queue message` and `ctrl + c to\ninterrupt`.\n5. Type a follow-up prompt during active work and press `Tab`; confirm\nit queues rather than submitting immediately.\n\nTargeted tests:\n\n- `just test -p codex-tui footer_snapshots`\n- `just test -p codex-tui footer_mode_snapshots`\n\n## Validation Notes\n\n`just test -p codex-tui` currently has two unrelated guardian\nfeature-flag test failures on this base:\n\n-\n`app::tests::update_feature_flags_disabling_guardian_clears_manual_review_policy_without_history`\n-\n`app::tests::update_feature_flags_disabling_guardian_clears_review_policy_and_restores_default`\n\n`just argument-comment-lint codex-rs/tui/src/bottom_pane/footer.rs`\ncould not run locally because the prebuilt wrapper requires `dotslash`;\nthe touched Rust diff was manually inspected for opaque positional\nliterals.","tree":{"sha":"6f77665ac93478355889653a998c58a16224eec7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/6f77665ac93478355889653a998c58a16224eec7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/4e540b107690989ea20832f85cd7f121492f5b74","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHgqSCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAEEMQAI7D8XifB/pu97G3b7k7YaBb\ngTu1GUwAaFGJZtIkTkDIMt2ywbi6DWQIc5o7Nlj6entSl85tyKxmKvLeFssbzhEm\nvH09f7hunQea9G1r2QcSD63RxySq/Ya0mf0kJrwfxewS0YEXcKU5SzJqzUbqqYqG\nOkRXqsRKQidF+jp2aOXQnpgoPOXvefuzHUMfTN2n0xOE6AAzdaa1ZPuuWxp/UKnM\nMidKBYo+giyf9I2vrdyaLWx1W7OZTFz8Y22NHWzbt+t8ibIURYq6HR+QEkvAZGHQ\nljohSCZFt1t8bVvOysnHrARfwm4PoPuvjOoBlE6DmIKEsEDyWcucrw0OgcFlWmqs\nCeLqVFwwLSTiHt62tYp7WOJF9bs5i6AMDMAajXZKi+fkFUvBIvAFIJe+W2UGBfAw\ndeSukeyPnsnlqU9C5E7IQAkXHYEDt7On2EYDOa+378Nf8Em1W0yDdZPTYPidAXF1\nDK8HbgHyaKVA1NJQPc2LDwov0jYXkfIB1ZfVfTzKeotBoQrfc6jZ3kFHPZRzzhKg\n/ZyY/ON2fREpA9fIvnn+qnkMokPcY9N81K7BvI2MHm0gR8Dwut60oYSehx9vr6JR\nqUwUqNbKrpAIX4I32JTCmQyKbmOaRZdKj+HTfNBYs0aT7+IPaZnJSm7OLnFde6r8\n7vi6Wq82SW4Q2NDCuw6O\n=z+t4\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 6f77665ac93478355889653a998c58a16224eec7\nparent 8d720feb698341c9a1599253d5e903cd99c603cb\nauthor Felipe Coury <felipe.coury@openai.com> 1780353682 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780353682 -0300\n\nfix(tui): clarify footer shortcut overlay hints (#25625)\n\n## Why\n\nThe TUI shortcut overlay used static labels for `Tab` and `Ctrl+C`, even\nthough both keys change behavior while a task is running. That made the\nvisible help misleading: idle `Tab` submits rather than queues, and\nactive-turn `Ctrl+C` interrupts rather than exits.\n\nCloses #25531.\nCloses #25564.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Pass task-running state into the shortcut overlay renderer.\n- Render `Tab` as `submit message` while idle and `queue message` while\nwork is running.\n- Render `Ctrl+C` as `exit` while idle and `interrupt` while work is\nrunning.\n- Add snapshot coverage for the active-work shortcut overlay and update\nidle overlay snapshots.\n\n## How to Test\n\n1. Start Codex and open the shortcut overlay with `?` while no task is\nrunning.\n2. Confirm the overlay shows `tab to submit message` and `ctrl + c to\nexit`.\n3. Start a task, then open or keep the shortcut overlay visible while\nwork is running.\n4. Confirm the overlay shows `tab to queue message` and `ctrl + c to\ninterrupt`.\n5. Type a follow-up prompt during active work and press `Tab`; confirm\nit queues rather than submitting immediately.\n\nTargeted tests:\n\n- `just test -p codex-tui footer_snapshots`\n- `just test -p codex-tui footer_mode_snapshots`\n\n## Validation Notes\n\n`just test -p codex-tui` currently has two unrelated guardian\nfeature-flag test failures on this base:\n\n-\n`app::tests::update_feature_flags_disabling_guardian_clears_manual_review_policy_without_history`\n-\n`app::tests::update_feature_flags_disabling_guardian_clears_review_policy_and_restores_default`\n\n`just argument-comment-lint codex-rs/tui/src/bottom_pane/footer.rs`\ncould not run locally because the prebuilt wrapper requires `dotslash`;\nthe touched Rust diff was manually inspected for opaque positional\nliterals.","verified_at":"2026-06-01T22:41:22Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4e540b107690989ea20832f85cd7f121492f5b74","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/4e540b107690989ea20832f85cd7f121492f5b74","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4e540b107690989ea20832f85cd7f121492f5b74/comments","author":{"login":"fcoury-oai","id":272635208,"node_id":"U_kgDOEEAVSA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/272635208?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/fcoury-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"8d720feb698341c9a1599253d5e903cd99c603cb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8d720feb698341c9a1599253d5e903cd99c603cb","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/8d720feb698341c9a1599253d5e903cd99c603cb"}]},{"sha":"8d720feb698341c9a1599253d5e903cd99c603cb","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDhkNzIwZmViNjk4MzQxYzlhMTU5OTI1M2Q1ZTkwM2NkOTljNjAzY2I","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif-oai","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-01T22:24:41Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-01T22:24:41Z"},"message":"Move tool search metadata onto ToolExecutor (#25684)\n\nDeferred tools need to be searchable even when they are not implemented\ninside `codex-core`. Extension-provided tools can be registered for\nlater discovery, but the search metadata path was still owned by\ncore-specific runtime hooks, which meant the shared `ToolExecutor`\nabstraction could not describe how a deferred extension tool should\nappear in `tool_search`.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Move `ToolSearchEntry` and `ToolSearchInfo` into `codex-tools` and\nre-export them from the shared tools crate.\n- Add a default `ToolExecutor::search_info` implementation that derives\nloadable tool-search metadata from function and namespace specs.\n- Forward search metadata through extension adapters and exposure\noverrides while keeping custom search text/source metadata for dynamic,\nMCP, and multi-agent tools.\n- Remove the old core-local `tool_search_entry` module now that search\nmetadata lives with the shared executor APIs.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Added `deferred_extension_tools_are_discoverable_with_tool_search`\ncoverage in `core/src/tools/spec_plan_tests.rs`.","tree":{"sha":"ea1e7e39a973dd36668ad0b27c13a13b79613f1d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/ea1e7e39a973dd36668ad0b27c13a13b79613f1d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/8d720feb698341c9a1599253d5e903cd99c603cb","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHgapCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAAyEQAJbVXEsZ4A3Fa8hGW76VRzzZ\nFphg30dMC9kVThWkG0EKTJWvsoTulRm4b5+evwFPtS9IKwtz2t7O9FvYFV3ZY3dU\n+Bl6kPntxSZ3OG/8YwLLl8ogdn21QzKR++Nz/jAFe3MXXrIHO+5m4njZ6fcILE5g\nXEqYJdIwDNcxVlt7v33FOTnspw4DWK1yC/VaZnZis5AOzXkKLWIviEV7MgmsTYuG\nrLxQMOAEXoZ2+8lThhJ5KYWyel+Sx2Z7N9udGw/6wRvV8ITIUafBEEx9Xn3TJCbc\nT3OH2ynU4xAHBG5y9waX9bD1mE25HWcPVmujUaCv0A1DrHG/QliWW1ZRb8cfeukP\n5KLCSFwzPmCtMjMf3mMGABLqnLWeVSGNKadgI12ISB7CRXXrUm4l82JAqFec6xh7\n8I7tfI1bjcj1dAgIb7Z6BEEKl7wpLTh+MHgf0d7QYunREfPnNex6NvQVHjSWSjkO\np25JBgsTcjwXI34mxmGwk1dE7P6/o4Cl/7HqXeIwpg1eYCamsVBLQrWURtkfG/N9\nqQAewnA9uTYui31w5lvrAEsMdVQVgVFVRuPAUt6aGlqI0Xoqpn/rbAihx74A90u8\nEwJ04fpHK6tXh+oIhKjrOxTVwGHeVFBEBd3A8Iaf4w+UW+va6vvextxJ6Fi6sqde\nHfJQMKLblPAPhRz7bju3\n=YTAj\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree ea1e7e39a973dd36668ad0b27c13a13b79613f1d\nparent 8ee49a2f74e9c352c45420bc97676a56fdd4992f\nauthor jif-oai <jif@openai.com> 1780352681 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780352681 +0200\n\nMove tool search metadata onto ToolExecutor (#25684)\n\nDeferred tools need to be searchable even when they are not implemented\ninside `codex-core`. Extension-provided tools can be registered for\nlater discovery, but the search metadata path was still owned by\ncore-specific runtime hooks, which meant the shared `ToolExecutor`\nabstraction could not describe how a deferred extension tool should\nappear in `tool_search`.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Move `ToolSearchEntry` and `ToolSearchInfo` into `codex-tools` and\nre-export them from the shared tools crate.\n- Add a default `ToolExecutor::search_info` implementation that derives\nloadable tool-search metadata from function and namespace specs.\n- Forward search metadata through extension adapters and exposure\noverrides while keeping custom search text/source metadata for dynamic,\nMCP, and multi-agent tools.\n- Remove the old core-local `tool_search_entry` module now that search\nmetadata lives with the shared executor APIs.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Added `deferred_extension_tools_are_discoverable_with_tool_search`\ncoverage in `core/src/tools/spec_plan_tests.rs`.","verified_at":"2026-06-01T22:24:41Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8d720feb698341c9a1599253d5e903cd99c603cb","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/8d720feb698341c9a1599253d5e903cd99c603cb","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8d720feb698341c9a1599253d5e903cd99c603cb/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"8ee49a2f74e9c352c45420bc97676a56fdd4992f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8ee49a2f74e9c352c45420bc97676a56fdd4992f","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/8ee49a2f74e9c352c45420bc97676a56fdd4992f"}]},{"sha":"8ee49a2f74e9c352c45420bc97676a56fdd4992f","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDhlZTQ5YTJmNzRlOWMzNTJjNDU0MjBiYzk3Njc2YTU2ZmRkNDk5MmY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Michael Bolin","email":"mbolin@openai.com","date":"2026-06-01T22:14:03Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-01T22:14:03Z"},"message":"Fix stale TestAppServer rename in plugin_list test (#25705)\n\n## Why\n\n#25701 renamed the app-server test harness to `TestAppServer`, but it\nraced with #25681, which added a new `plugin_list` test call site still\nusing the old `McpProcess` name. Once both changes met on `main`,\napp-server test builds failed before running the suite because\n`McpProcess` no longer exists in that scope.\n\nThis PR fixes that CI break by updating the remaining stale call site to\nthe renamed helper.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Replaced the `McpProcess::new(...)` use in\n`codex-rs/app-server/tests/suite/v2/plugin_list.rs` with\n`TestAppServer::new(...)`.\n- Renamed the local variable from `mcp` to `app_server` at the same call\nsite to match the helper rename.\n\nRelevant code:\nhttps://github.com/openai/codex/blob/aadd9c999b4e0789f7afb2b9b8cc43000bb47e86/codex-rs/app-server/tests/suite/v2/plugin_list.rs#L234-L246\n\n## Verification\n\nNot run locally; this is a compile fix for the app-server test harness\nrename.","tree":{"sha":"9feee39534d97af24b00c5b254e5c47615c36d81","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/9feee39534d97af24b00c5b254e5c47615c36d81"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/8ee49a2f74e9c352c45420bc97676a56fdd4992f","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHgQrCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAVuQQAFoeToly/QMCLKCPkY01dNRl\nRF10LuTPNtDVRWO6oUU1sUUxa6HXzv7paeX+tu8SbrYUTmbLTjH/3Ig3huCUGVIE\nE6OK+YJrGuBYsd09Ohcg+gDdYnZRfh2G2Vl8Hf123w9qn0TN5PKJP3Z3joe6sia9\nRgXZkaPL5HsB3ly5BF2LxhiIYQd3BRtLzjhjxumgBqkuAEo/gs9YwvZzGW8U8EH0\nOOhBQ6Fpw1BzxQJtrfic/mHz0WZRWAGNc2T2/ico7r34+qFoec7CqMay06NglekU\nOKsTu8STKNl/Aj16DG+WdMDQcniWgYYUdl7MjevEzbMn9fG5sFLKt8fLXmyT7J76\nLAjHyaxGIB/UOrX2MtKfZyGmPvfolByVx937mROLWdF38Q7NRKZ6kuFc+K6/OmA5\nmAeUQXrFlUr5S/IGxqo+R/M/KRPCjOZljRJsVwF3/zMoK5SsRfzF3H3crGCIjyVZ\nhFXBha6ApZ11dvrnJx3JJHIVkiqACroPW7ox1kswN7A1lLD8XrFtC6D5Nx3Bkedx\n7R2zx3uP7xjBZcrANRSf/bkk6xS3UjegXZeKBCtffKFttcagm8LC0WRwIj+xVkYC\nQE5wwzTvVetY3Lbz18EZVLzRhaIdoDXf0X1N12bMz9I22O/wr3bkadQ0zK0ByNYU\nikdMe1PEcopPJ+iyAh3V\n=dlOE\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 9feee39534d97af24b00c5b254e5c47615c36d81\nparent b3c415703452dc068f8e68265ee72c7887a7d1c1\nauthor Michael Bolin <mbolin@openai.com> 1780352043 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780352043 -0700\n\nFix stale TestAppServer rename in plugin_list test (#25705)\n\n## Why\n\n#25701 renamed the app-server test harness to `TestAppServer`, but it\nraced with #25681, which added a new `plugin_list` test call site still\nusing the old `McpProcess` name. Once both changes met on `main`,\napp-server test builds failed before running the suite because\n`McpProcess` no longer exists in that scope.\n\nThis PR fixes that CI break by updating the remaining stale call site to\nthe renamed helper.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Replaced the `McpProcess::new(...)` use in\n`codex-rs/app-server/tests/suite/v2/plugin_list.rs` with\n`TestAppServer::new(...)`.\n- Renamed the local variable from `mcp` to `app_server` at the same call\nsite to match the helper rename.\n\nRelevant code:\nhttps://github.com/openai/codex/blob/aadd9c999b4e0789f7afb2b9b8cc43000bb47e86/codex-rs/app-server/tests/suite/v2/plugin_list.rs#L234-L246\n\n## Verification\n\nNot run locally; this is a compile fix for the app-server test harness\nrename.","verified_at":"2026-06-01T22:14:04Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8ee49a2f74e9c352c45420bc97676a56fdd4992f","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/8ee49a2f74e9c352c45420bc97676a56fdd4992f","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8ee49a2f74e9c352c45420bc97676a56fdd4992f/comments","author":{"login":"bolinfest","id":655869,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTg2OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/655869?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest","html_url":"https://github.com/bolinfest","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"b3c415703452dc068f8e68265ee72c7887a7d1c1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/b3c415703452dc068f8e68265ee72c7887a7d1c1","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/b3c415703452dc068f8e68265ee72c7887a7d1c1"}]},{"sha":"b3c415703452dc068f8e68265ee72c7887a7d1c1","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGIzYzQxNTcwMzQ1MmRjMDY4ZjhlNjgyNjVlZTcyYzc4ODdhN2QxYzE","commit":{"author":{"name":"sayan-oai","email":"sayan@openai.com","date":"2026-06-01T22:04:11Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-01T22:04:11Z"},"message":"[codex] enable parallel standalone web search calls (#25702)\n\n## Summary\n- opt the extension-backed standalone `web.run` tool into parallel tool\nexecution\n- update the existing extension registration test to assert that the\ntool advertises parallel-call support\n\n## Why\nThe standalone web-search API endpoint now supports parallel requests.\nThe extension executor still inherited the shared serial default,\ncausing multiple `web.run` calls to acquire the exclusive runtime lock.\n\n## Impact\nModels that emit multiple standalone web-search calls can now execute\nthem concurrently when model-level parallel tool calls are enabled.\n\n## Validation\n- `just fmt`\n- `just test -p codex-web-search-extension`\n- `git diff --check origin/main...HEAD`","tree":{"sha":"a839c009373fe68d05744f2f34d0286fd472694e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/a839c009373fe68d05744f2f34d0286fd472694e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/b3c415703452dc068f8e68265ee72c7887a7d1c1","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHgHbCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAyscQACxeWqXzBWIA4T1ZbwDxntfr\npTP0wqIh0DPIs8Fsog40B/x4I6D4Hs91+QgtD1csBsTYao3Khsf3FfoRx2bnN81G\nz/np6KgvT4/CQuKGoQ7X7tHSzr23+YsMA18HX7egRYiPz2GX47BiGioguT0KBB/s\ncb+8wFJupFFnkGQtipPdhGvRoeQJgLREzc8VZcgaH3HAN16s8vzZ4CLbhts6cU48\nLIpWnwzKY9M7K7LSwKUJQ/cRmeb4PLb5kfnd4v7BGE2ydlXUKVPFkbg12r0qcgCA\nTyOb6wUt/jTArAWw5a6latljoAzKoXYfhIQ2SDgbuGuJVcGwyxIkxwVz6wlwh4xk\njh96DSziOHuQd6eFUYBrcSHKEr88ySD2UgdvotbPoO3XOhWBZa7cG1s8lGAIQEX2\n2SipI4FvSftk/JRa6iVc1fSqb7V2G/gN49zlx7AZL6VdtZ0V2k4R3RU1oEGYIBDh\nRI6W8cp9H2XCpuQ5dWYnXRnBS1Ltk8gsmMspOaS9Ho4g29r+uYnTC3e1SeHStqj9\nlTmv3VfToEz16fxs7OUw/I1m0q22SrHhq/xlkQ717y7k/i8fR7KQY0hSIQ6RJK3I\n2PYR1Afg+QrY/77Yn1uEVq57NPDq6OiOY55+hOtDNazlG2PaAD3583RgKl5WltYQ\ndWEZfzQYRBPyOmI63xYS\n=U3Q6\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a839c009373fe68d05744f2f34d0286fd472694e\nparent 6536841d894b3425e3dcf638c9b64678a4db8177\nauthor sayan-oai <sayan@openai.com> 1780351451 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780351451 -0700\n\n[codex] enable parallel standalone web search calls (#25702)\n\n## Summary\n- opt the extension-backed standalone `web.run` tool into parallel tool\nexecution\n- update the existing extension registration test to assert that the\ntool advertises parallel-call support\n\n## Why\nThe standalone web-search API endpoint now supports parallel requests.\nThe extension executor still inherited the shared serial default,\ncausing multiple `web.run` calls to acquire the exclusive runtime lock.\n\n## Impact\nModels that emit multiple standalone web-search calls can now execute\nthem concurrently when model-level parallel tool calls are enabled.\n\n## Validation\n- `just fmt`\n- `just test -p codex-web-search-extension`\n- `git diff --check origin/main...HEAD`","verified_at":"2026-06-01T22:04:12Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/b3c415703452dc068f8e68265ee72c7887a7d1c1","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/b3c415703452dc068f8e68265ee72c7887a7d1c1","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/b3c415703452dc068f8e68265ee72c7887a7d1c1/comments","author":{"login":"sayan-oai","id":244841968,"node_id":"U_kgDODpf98A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/244841968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/sayan-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"6536841d894b3425e3dcf638c9b64678a4db8177","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6536841d894b3425e3dcf638c9b64678a4db8177","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/6536841d894b3425e3dcf638c9b64678a4db8177"}]},{"sha":"6536841d894b3425e3dcf638c9b64678a4db8177","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDY1MzY4NDFkODk0YjM0MjVlM2RjZjYzOGM5YjY0Njc4YTRkYjgxNzc","commit":{"author":{"name":"Michael Bolin","email":"mbolin@openai.com","date":"2026-06-01T21:49:38Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-01T21:49:38Z"},"message":"fix: rename McpServer to TestAppServer (#25701)\n\nThis PR brought to you via VS Code rather than Codex...\n\n- opened `codex-rs/app-server/tests/common/mcp_process.rs`\n- put the cursor on `McpServer`\n- hit `F2` and renamed the symbol to `TestAppServer`\n- went to the file tree\n- hit enter and renamed `mcp_process.rs` to `test_app_server.rs`\n- ran **Save All Files** from the Command Palette\n- ran `just fmt`\n\nThe End\n\n(Admittedly, most of the local variables for `TestAppServer` are still\nnamed `mcp`, though.)","tree":{"sha":"ca1ae3e0bfc935ccf7f744dd6fea218e45a52927","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/ca1ae3e0bfc935ccf7f744dd6fea218e45a52927"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/6536841d894b3425e3dcf638c9b64678a4db8177","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHf5yCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAyOsQAAmqqtppYrWRkhNLHN0Zfxl7\nPPYfDngnfnHFjvmD5KNs+fbGcwftf6kAUnGjFXp1ze3m/B1Gfw60pJjyhJxVBUXW\nSD48pQuNQSpkyKc4W3hWVizSGohIHZy5oMcXd/OCvik4hZlwVkG4fDgEPRCB9T9r\ndm8R8cfV+UIUO0mgUwwM2QCQET1CI3lEB8cUIdKYJQH2elvg2YujuA1T675biD2L\nkXy9goQsjTosC6lzrj73uzM9iH0oTjUy+7C2JYQ2RLr8t4Mcuwym1o+SxX/epzIy\nEcGeIACWlQo0sMugdZt59PzkUhSzds4JYhZRtyFfpX2YvV9IMjtiS1GKmOhuM/ZU\nB4QQEHTagRWwIGm/EA3zlXioC32Dl/v43O/6tjrEBC8d07l1t627Q7+0dc/8LDUl\nBy91OMy6y4/25vBD2Es8NR5NNNblAo7Dcgu++60c2WC3EQGHaAT9YsUOIxXZrhcE\nI5ADoVbnBotmkWAfX4XIdOvA7SFIzMiFePNC+2Xkl9UpyVYJBXwq6iwfwEgPFn7g\nS9ZY0gpvF69ONGgCNB8jcqIktbzN8vqDAuub72QSf5V8Lx/SFbbit+zB9A6mQZ4U\nmezKOnzt3cZYuDTkJyzMFq7apuC3nwDmUJWupN2oL09zzsKthyVCANbOeNyGvhZL\nxawDho7jvrCaeAO5W9oc\n=vGsv\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree ca1ae3e0bfc935ccf7f744dd6fea218e45a52927\nparent 6ae99fd35ffdc318508fb80062fda0b9ff53579d\nauthor Michael Bolin <mbolin@openai.com> 1780350578 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780350578 +0000\n\nfix: rename McpServer to TestAppServer (#25701)\n\nThis PR brought to you via VS Code rather than Codex...\n\n- opened `codex-rs/app-server/tests/common/mcp_process.rs`\n- put the cursor on `McpServer`\n- hit `F2` and renamed the symbol to `TestAppServer`\n- went to the file tree\n- hit enter and renamed `mcp_process.rs` to `test_app_server.rs`\n- ran **Save All Files** from the Command Palette\n- ran `just fmt`\n\nThe End\n\n(Admittedly, most of the local variables for `TestAppServer` are still\nnamed `mcp`, though.)","verified_at":"2026-06-01T21:49:39Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6536841d894b3425e3dcf638c9b64678a4db8177","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/6536841d894b3425e3dcf638c9b64678a4db8177","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6536841d894b3425e3dcf638c9b64678a4db8177/comments","author":{"login":"bolinfest","id":655869,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTg2OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/655869?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest","html_url":"https://github.com/bolinfest","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"6ae99fd35ffdc318508fb80062fda0b9ff53579d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6ae99fd35ffdc318508fb80062fda0b9ff53579d","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/6ae99fd35ffdc318508fb80062fda0b9ff53579d"}]},{"sha":"6ae99fd35ffdc318508fb80062fda0b9ff53579d","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDZhZTk5ZmQzNWZmZGMzMTg1MDhmYjgwMDYyZmRhMGI5ZmY1MzU3OWQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"xl-openai","email":"xl@openai.com","date":"2026-06-01T21:27:18Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-01T21:27:18Z"},"message":"fix: Deduplicate installed local and remote curated plugins (#25681)\n\n## Summary\n- Deduplicate installed `openai-curated` and `openai-curated-remote`\nplugin conflicts by feature flag.\n- Prefer remote when remote plugins are enabled; otherwise prefer local,\nwhile preserving one-sided installs.\n\n## Testing\n- `just fmt`\n- `git diff --check`\n- Targeted `just test` was blocked locally because `cargo-nextest` is\nnot installed.","tree":{"sha":"b385ce99f4667d0cc144185cdc397828e2492afd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/b385ce99f4667d0cc144185cdc397828e2492afd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/6ae99fd35ffdc318508fb80062fda0b9ff53579d","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHfk2CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA0oMQAEYDa684tAeELhWWbyba1P2y\nbyTzYqVw3yOEHppo3dffify81riLUjsHp8wn7pvKdf2MrFg/Npxz94YTeeTFeT5E\nSy8S7nV3qh2CSOTFeFCWLYO/jEeuB30c7LkR9J49nTSpgKaffFMnKQxWwQVgEpEI\nIdRoM/XKTFthu5vnegLTCi+G81VqHRHX0vD89kk/kyHwtkSXOaykUqrS3IJomgus\n8sve75ppG3cEMOynUlPiWXjxes6DkEjhNzMG4V6bBsdeuslapMiMKn+XAclDUUCa\n57DL0QSHzzYgyc5hqXtLQSh9qoohH18YS+JTNuOwuN81Dq01Jsk3HKt5FlVLY+MG\nbasqkL9i3BkxiOFreMGE0ZIMR4VstZU1TJgkt8F9yeIm1hJmC18a1hzqs2g6vJqe\nthvR/ebEOAoFWPyjvspZ3g4vx8zi54SJ6BtFDqV7AEr37OcngL51HHx2/4PZz2f/\nRQzvlj71KNAUQDPtiasbrLozjU/Xnw6yIiIHdoz4UeXbU/2vRHvzhzp/xYQXW3p7\nvSZ6D+XeoA57cFdf2l4BUxbeQ7NF/H+CWt5n44Eb1IM3cltdocd4h3dF3Tdz5kyf\nseLy78HLLEP9HQ5Q0qxHyoLWcyvQcN8G8IILTlQnP8M7Qy5hkQomIm/X+FMcIXv8\nIW5eww8er0xkuxmX5K7e\n=77Kh\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree b385ce99f4667d0cc144185cdc397828e2492afd\nparent 433ac84102cbb6203180e5b5cd55645d117a74c7\nauthor xl-openai <xl@openai.com> 1780349238 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780349238 -0700\n\nfix: Deduplicate installed local and remote curated plugins (#25681)\n\n## Summary\n- Deduplicate installed `openai-curated` and `openai-curated-remote`\nplugin conflicts by feature flag.\n- Prefer remote when remote plugins are enabled; otherwise prefer local,\nwhile preserving one-sided installs.\n\n## Testing\n- `just fmt`\n- `git diff --check`\n- Targeted `just test` was blocked locally because `cargo-nextest` is\nnot installed.","verified_at":"2026-06-01T21:27:18Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6ae99fd35ffdc318508fb80062fda0b9ff53579d","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/6ae99fd35ffdc318508fb80062fda0b9ff53579d","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6ae99fd35ffdc318508fb80062fda0b9ff53579d/comments","author":{"login":"xl-openai","id":184293535,"node_id":"U_kgDOCvwYnw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/184293535?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/xl-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"433ac84102cbb6203180e5b5cd55645d117a74c7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/433ac84102cbb6203180e5b5cd55645d117a74c7","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/433ac84102cbb6203180e5b5cd55645d117a74c7"}]},{"sha":"433ac84102cbb6203180e5b5cd55645d117a74c7","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDQzM2FjODQxMDJjYmI2MjAzMTgwZTViNWNkNTU2NDVkMTE3YTc0Yzc","commit":{"author":{"name":"Adam Perry @ OpenAI","email":"anp@openai.com","date":"2026-06-01T21:05:54Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-01T21:05:54Z"},"message":"Add Python version compatibility guidance (#25690)\n\n## Why\n\nPython contributions in this repository should target the declared\nPython 3 runtime instead of carrying Python 2 compatibility patterns\nforward. When compatibility across Python 3 point releases matters,\ncontributors need a consistent source of truth for the minimum supported\nversion.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Added Python development guidance to `AGENTS.md` stating that the\nrepository uses Python 3+ and should not use the `__future__` module.\n- Documented that contributors should check the nearest `pyproject.toml`\n`requires-python` field when evaluating Python 3 point-release\ncompatibility.\n\n## Testing\n\nNot run (guidance-only change).","tree":{"sha":"977c8e9630f9fbff9c83e69a234d609cb7e06fc9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/977c8e9630f9fbff9c83e69a234d609cb7e06fc9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/433ac84102cbb6203180e5b5cd55645d117a74c7","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHfQyCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjicQAC6AXw8Pr+TjsXY83J1nQ6yV\n1UfGGQ9GXES7ooLQ4t+9Bl42p/HaSswlgrGgEbycj7O0LgTD4IvJyQgSEWi9iwki\nBJw2Yc7LgPatLfQatjfNKPNcPAmz/pOV/io41sWc1DGhHGQbVnGDA9KDcJmHgKGw\nLM71ViIYuem58l0aI7XRWdmaOOd0qFiyUtos2Uuy4ouIv7xN5RtKWT1j7t8ET7Z+\n4JuYtA4BRFo7Mr/65JRHLL4F5sP1Dci1xR4qV1Blqr+zXJN1n7PMJkvzzjqkI1uz\n/6U/GChe8zs17+TBLGRB80eTyzI+rbfyTy9q378Fj4C95m+HHoSaNsE9ruoJmBU5\n+V0Z4wF6a5lEmnNZun/Jldu4s7yPQ9SJgSJ4PBuFlLTUvgEWTHNzMRoeCV2tAX3b\n1RKDQBMusRXcodyK7MVHufTkUL162k5uf4G58CDWwFlLJy2ggtUo/PaEJgZFAP10\nXH3vfO6/gSo4MXJWyjWDFm3d/ayIb7GRiO5WT9YWcTJPLgEdvbh25fwQg4EYZuMy\nFwnyHSXmvNxGq/rnnu3ENJUkqXGSiM5060rusJXeIIDVGWJ625rxrjEckkAQNRFR\n40N+PjCFtuxg+x1qUQQmW8JNsiqPNZkkck+Y+k4ymUSCC4KkkrMZGwjUCWlo3SDD\ny+3w2W4ihUB26swGfc/j\n=TbQs\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 977c8e9630f9fbff9c83e69a234d609cb7e06fc9\nparent f0e15b916ff0aa56f25d0b8a9e519a39c297b9f1\nauthor Adam Perry @ OpenAI <anp@openai.com> 1780347954 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780347954 -0700\n\nAdd Python version compatibility guidance (#25690)\n\n## Why\n\nPython contributions in this repository should target the declared\nPython 3 runtime instead of carrying Python 2 compatibility patterns\nforward. When compatibility across Python 3 point releases matters,\ncontributors need a consistent source of truth for the minimum supported\nversion.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Added Python development guidance to `AGENTS.md` stating that the\nrepository uses Python 3+ and should not use the `__future__` module.\n- Documented that contributors should check the nearest `pyproject.toml`\n`requires-python` field when evaluating Python 3 point-release\ncompatibility.\n\n## Testing\n\nNot run (guidance-only change).","verified_at":"2026-06-01T21:05:55Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/433ac84102cbb6203180e5b5cd55645d117a74c7","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/433ac84102cbb6203180e5b5cd55645d117a74c7","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/433ac84102cbb6203180e5b5cd55645d117a74c7/comments","author":{"login":"anp-oai","id":286154589,"node_id":"U_kgDOEQ5fXQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/286154589?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/anp-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"f0e15b916ff0aa56f25d0b8a9e519a39c297b9f1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f0e15b916ff0aa56f25d0b8a9e519a39c297b9f1","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/f0e15b916ff0aa56f25d0b8a9e519a39c297b9f1"}]},{"sha":"f0e15b916ff0aa56f25d0b8a9e519a39c297b9f1","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGYwZTE1YjkxNmZmMGFhNTZmMjVkMGI4YTllNTE5YTM5YzI5N2I5ZjE","commit":{"author":{"name":"sayan-oai","email":"sayan@openai.com","date":"2026-06-01T21:01:30Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-01T21:01:30Z"},"message":"[codex] Generalize deferred nested tool guidance (#25689)\n\n## Summary\n- describe omitted code-mode tools as deferred nested tools instead of\nMCP/app tools\n- update the prompt-description assertion to match\n\n## Why\nDeferred dynamic tools are also callable through `tools` and\ndiscoverable in `ALL_TOOLS`, so the previous MCP/app-specific wording\nwas too narrow.\n\n## Validation\n- `just fmt`\n- `just test -p codex-code-mode`\n- `git diff --check`","tree":{"sha":"219a2965a7d17ce99a50b159ab5aea9d821f650c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/219a2965a7d17ce99a50b159ab5aea9d821f650c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/f0e15b916ff0aa56f25d0b8a9e519a39c297b9f1","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHfMqCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAALK4QAJzuyuLTW1rtMHfWpH0e5R0C\nJ0RtBV6z7G3DiBk9DKZDNCTww5OphYzBlkZ69lLETsFk/y65hxtZ2pMABCDLMiLQ\n5LkTu+6sPQ1MkRA+B1oQysc2HjayUclFZX1FR0ZGqOEubiJ3GmYeoR1NnSgc7TVP\nPpc0GVuBE572y2K5N6N6zhcLMS6ILNBFgxi6CeRLfjmpIV9h0zOUHGLD8l/ggGWL\n0mb/aMvriaPSbiNpmUAIz8EnJ7ti56sBJ4Yv6cC4xORRPe/QLWaCa6gLaircZvt7\ne7eJROsYVL11vtqDeSORP22uA1eFshMxwv3KK2hTASXu/+YqGPaAHwv0qxdlkqZE\nDowOUGBFvCwBNYcHJKuJPXtIZLPXdg/YOyTDkQmRU9H1536SLVcvLY1S1V6r4eEH\nHgODuRofN3UhrtR6dwJZaFIWnTsH/N4tZGszzBUt75/RTUdpyOF33bMQ1XwYOU/2\nLEnbT5P5DX3qIZVy0hyjpxOHefIQEDUlTm+EwKX209Yyt2c/yqmK8/Lee28h6rge\nv1eXGN9HNmaaD78CiLX2ERK0g6PmYV069P4N5ogriNn2FXncsAnhPptLRATI1zWK\nYov7iWM3ffV1PhOEWtziXToHBt2bsks63wNc28grWENQCB5Z5xSkVf/7dgH6qD+e\nwToCdtBtcW/XslSfUpap\n=UFk4\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 219a2965a7d17ce99a50b159ab5aea9d821f650c\nparent 7c285f9e9c85b4b9c3819210564fc039e9b5304a\nauthor sayan-oai <sayan@openai.com> 1780347690 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780347690 +0000\n\n[codex] Generalize deferred nested tool guidance (#25689)\n\n## Summary\n- describe omitted code-mode tools as deferred nested tools instead of\nMCP/app tools\n- update the prompt-description assertion to match\n\n## Why\nDeferred dynamic tools are also callable through `tools` and\ndiscoverable in `ALL_TOOLS`, so the previous MCP/app-specific wording\nwas too narrow.\n\n## Validation\n- `just fmt`\n- `just test -p codex-code-mode`\n- `git diff --check`","verified_at":"2026-06-01T21:01:31Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f0e15b916ff0aa56f25d0b8a9e519a39c297b9f1","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/f0e15b916ff0aa56f25d0b8a9e519a39c297b9f1","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f0e15b916ff0aa56f25d0b8a9e519a39c297b9f1/comments","author":{"login":"sayan-oai","id":244841968,"node_id":"U_kgDODpf98A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/244841968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/sayan-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/gists{/g