T20:54:25Z"},"message":"Add rollout compression histograms (#25680)\n\n## Summary\n\nStacked on #25679. Add histogram telemetry for rollout compression\nruntime, per-file compression time, byte sizes, and compression ratio.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Emit `codex.rollout_compression.run.duration_ms` tagged by final run\nstatus.\n- Emit `codex.rollout_compression.file.duration_ms` tagged by file\noutcome.\n- Emit source and compressed byte histograms for compression\ncandidates/results.\n- Emit `codex.rollout_compression.file.compression_ratio` for successful\ncompressions, recorded as integer basis points.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just fmt`\n- `just test -p codex-rollout`\n- `just fix -p codex-rollout`","tree":{"sha":"e6afa081933afb7a36a7dd77b3a0065eb99ec4bb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/e6afa081933afb7a36a7dd77b3a0065eb99ec4bb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/7c285f9e9c85b4b9c3819210564fc039e9b5304a","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHfGBCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAE5oQAIqtpBMKvjA/WokH3JAhy16K\nxVJq69BsyTRdrZi3msc1pn1b1OhH0zcJodhKSY290jFWDSm7ocxhukLBPEBr9R6a\n91vQKtmIqhtqA08lgESdDpMxuf0IlDJBzl8wDp58Z3Nom3UDzE9H83TmE9IHCBHm\naV6V2ZFwXmiA5cpWk0pXbc2NRP4TKMPV65GlfsxjqWT/OwULyJEfFnJpFRkWp9x0\nWjGuZRk2HoeAu7Tzu/5qQ9KQUc8GcFPJo26Q04ncSdKbo/47PNp+8iyow8oFDvnr\nJDUqed+oMLoqAf15cxehJlY/wAsAJjmCpgYLgfXVMpBzQslvDbbMdLvqPncSt7BC\nLCpPinWKPtlgdUnGtUPHEyC4PL9JRoBgohDmM13+IGfWPd09ub1U24yqp0OmDcdr\nqB9eQ9OdMSNM2bdREFF6HeqkWTBfPQ44cBUtWjj7PO59zTjjzP3kf88D2k2ubCaP\nXCEin/sjvmR6WiZ9L+Y/ahRWRmg/bhu5nD0Fp03yxFJUaVNJWk956D2IuzS5UQx5\nzAaFx2/Ymb5neBf4d8oONA7AYeHHpgpd9H+LSkUuuM4c702XaHJemYcpLjVkhmnG\n0L/+c0mvulDpHtJDjZMsROy7wW9FmdjH1UrQ0N/oK/KZtibeK90i5h/sasW7H8m2\nMJAWi2oia5f3Ma6scIY9\n=D7qO\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree e6afa081933afb7a36a7dd77b3a0065eb99ec4bb\nparent a29a5b08615d2d965dc4e6a90405a70d99306d26\nauthor jif-oai <jif@openai.com> 1780347265 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780347265 +0200\n\nAdd rollout compression histograms (#25680)\n\n## Summary\n\nStacked on #25679. Add histogram telemetry for rollout compression\nruntime, per-file compression time, byte sizes, and compression ratio.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Emit `codex.rollout_compression.run.duration_ms` tagged by final run\nstatus.\n- Emit `codex.rollout_compression.file.duration_ms` tagged by file\noutcome.\n- Emit source and compressed byte histograms for compression\ncandidates/results.\n- Emit `codex.rollout_compression.file.compression_ratio` for successful\ncompressions, recorded as integer basis points.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just fmt`\n- `just test -p codex-rollout`\n- `just fix -p codex-rollout`","verified_at":"2026-06-01T20:54:26Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/7c285f9e9c85b4b9c3819210564fc039e9b5304a","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/7c285f9e9c85b4b9c3819210564fc039e9b5304a","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/7c285f9e9c85b4b9c3819210564fc039e9b5304a/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"a29a5b08615d2d965dc4e6a90405a70d99306d26","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a29a5b08615d2d965dc4e6a90405a70d99306d26","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/a29a5b08615d2d965dc4e6a90405a70d99306d26"}]},{"sha":"a29a5b08615d2d965dc4e6a90405a70d99306d26","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGEyOWE1YjA4NjE1ZDJkOTY1ZGM0ZTZhOTA0MDVhNzBkOTkzMDZkMjY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Adam Perry @ OpenAI","email":"anp@openai.com","date":"2026-06-01T20:36:16Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-01T20:36:16Z"},"message":"[codex] document out-of-line test module convention (#25682)\n\n## Why\n\nNew unit test modules should follow one consistent layout so\nimplementation files stay focused and test suites remain easy to locate,\nwithout creating cleanup churn in existing inline test modules.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Added `AGENTS.md` guidance requiring new test modules to use separate\nsibling `*_tests.rs` files with an explicit `#[path = \"..._tests.rs\"]`\nattribute.\n- Clarified that existing inline `#[cfg(test)] mod tests { ... }`\nmodules should not be moved solely to follow the new convention.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Ran `git diff --check`.","tree":{"sha":"2cf5c90ac1631a8ffad5619111db8f7489a7b523","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/2cf5c90ac1631a8ffad5619111db8f7489a7b523"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/a29a5b08615d2d965dc4e6a90405a70d99306d26","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHe1ACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAM94QAFPAEdcYIt5Vp91970DWmCpT\nEPkiHvTxTKaynRoQ+HFzdF/bHD8HTZU0d6WrWfSuyb4baNUhnjzSCskLny/MzwF7\nPCnWAdHyP4PMcQCLgsn2LEEvU7FJsbaE0PjWEpSJDVL4Rd2LbUzjweEYBt9OV8bi\n7J500Jw6R8oCASDRb6n1V62SVDwbDuvZIAwjUMwDawH4tgflV8hFcfsLdEQR33AR\nqnGyot9zqlkcRr0K+H5UtdGtTXhRA+2qCgSqXbbz22MJOuUbZ25qVlZ2rQ1sgjGQ\nICJG2fLaCIs/YeNvflE7DePbA93Efu+lbDD1S5YHm1PxLTLdeqHBNoc62OIUtmK9\nC0gLEVeCucRkc6iXbvldrN+8w+qhKivj3pLFSFOCJ8bY42HZ0K2cKmI5VOPaT3H2\n4ENsADBIaxdiq8eqoJU27TjPNOz72adrhPyzvYHxo6hTbYhmnOZVWD/rtF9OK39Z\naP8PKwgeMNXkIgnJ2G3skoPUDv8M/rFMSMF4dkExGixa+P8Z/HXiFfef0kh6xjx7\noywz0o8i/77qDqaKuNew/aYot0d34TFTV8Tn7j8emnOYheJ3CwOe9fx2MXUUdVG4\n5x/XvJa/L01loygnyWIIauedKXjqQ6xyDPTZ10BNGmBf1xjWOZUIHaMib3DAb8dq\ntHAmhLhW2lbUERywxSr6\n=/eSY\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 2cf5c90ac1631a8ffad5619111db8f7489a7b523\nparent 9f4fac8ec4e74318ae272afedd118fc635a1023d\nauthor Adam Perry @ OpenAI <anp@openai.com> 1780346176 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780346176 -0700\n\n[codex] document out-of-line test module convention (#25682)\n\n## Why\n\nNew unit test modules should follow one consistent layout so\nimplementation files stay focused and test suites remain easy to locate,\nwithout creating cleanup churn in existing inline test modules.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Added `AGENTS.md` guidance requiring new test modules to use separate\nsibling `*_tests.rs` files with an explicit `#[path = \"..._tests.rs\"]`\nattribute.\n- Clarified that existing inline `#[cfg(test)] mod tests { ... }`\nmodules should not be moved solely to follow the new convention.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Ran `git diff --check`.","verified_at":"2026-06-01T20:36:17Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a29a5b08615d2d965dc4e6a90405a70d99306d26","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/a29a5b08615d2d965dc4e6a90405a70d99306d26","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a29a5b08615d2d965dc4e6a90405a70d99306d26/comments","author":{"login":"anp-oai","id":286154589,"node_id":"U_kgDOEQ5fXQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/286154589?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/anp-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"9f4fac8ec4e74318ae272afedd118fc635a1023d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/9f4fac8ec4e74318ae272afedd118fc635a1023d","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/9f4fac8ec4e74318ae272afedd118fc635a1023d"}]},{"sha":"9f4fac8ec4e74318ae272afedd118fc635a1023d","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDlmNGZhYzhlYzRlNzQzMThhZTI3MmFmZWRkMTE4ZmM2MzVhMTAyM2Q","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif-oai","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-01T20:26:32Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-01T20:26:32Z"},"message":"Add rollout compression counters (#25679)\n\n## Summary\n\nAdd counter telemetry for the local rollout compression worker so we can\nsee when it runs, why it skips, and how individual file/materialization\npaths resolve.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Emit `codex.rollout_compression.run` with statuses for start,\ncompletion, failure, duplicate-run skip, and missing runtime skip.\n- Emit `codex.rollout_compression.file` outcomes for scanned,\ncompressed, skipped, and failed compression candidates.\n- Emit `codex.rollout_compression.temp_cleanup` and\n`codex.rollout_compression.materialize` counters for cleanup and\ndecompression paths.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just fmt`\n- `just test -p codex-rollout`\n- `just fix -p codex-rollout`","tree":{"sha":"46f9243e2f33a88757f3654b0179d4833548d7cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/46f9243e2f33a88757f3654b0179d4833548d7cd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/9f4fac8ec4e74318ae272afedd118fc635a1023d","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHer4CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAeQwQAFiHYFkGg1YVRlP7Y1F3hUiJ\n8mOTX+Js5cQCFE3Pv+Gt9lJ9Zvb9fBWWgc5OkfZr2NaJ1pMHHJo//otEbAZ2gOFh\nP1OSH7ST8wYo9xoKAzlNSmz3rMD+vpxy4+t62s2xiu3c+uGAm64wsFbLzBcYinnZ\nbOrdnWCoXjp6bSuRvH81XvckGx6v6CZ1K3h5p84TsDzL8o2YRL1WcekhHiwh0fuR\nucwBmu36gQ0qjasl+6RM5RnF8sXyPTBgX8Bfi+HAgOE5IlGH4RODJqr7Q9+ax2d1\noOIOWQTEPv52kzNNFKy5WP5jxXVwabDLN3GWQDYPWM+w1VnrafdRK8hH+OGc2ZRC\nUH2rtP70z+VKklNkikq+adf+U7St4y0njizhNItkt8q4vfv9xKmalhlCHme0b/tD\ntLaJY7W4bzvRH1+keYXcahIhx7ceHn6OhRI3/cBk8heuNcEBHXh/pezYyDhbIfRP\nJenreC9cUaZ8tXDsl/TXPfjdycWo+bVru2EhNEiLHWwrEyVuWHgUY2jJX4VZXL4G\nuK2r0mhHjeaTf1RtXqw5jEEpl6Cfg8/tNWxPCsj8WKDlofRdIMgDpr6FSqdUZyyR\ngVK/Vbrks990qeHTRYePNWOEdhpoTZ2be/Nx+qkHBLAzfLIuK7d1flj5wfZKn/IH\n+s8Bj334lGVQdNP/ccW1\n=8mZ4\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 46f9243e2f33a88757f3654b0179d4833548d7cd\nparent feb9eddc513c318adbda63bd953c1684deb6d8a3\nauthor jif-oai <jif@openai.com> 1780345592 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780345592 +0200\n\nAdd rollout compression counters (#25679)\n\n## Summary\n\nAdd counter telemetry for the local rollout compression worker so we can\nsee when it runs, why it skips, and how individual file/materialization\npaths resolve.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Emit `codex.rollout_compression.run` with statuses for start,\ncompletion, failure, duplicate-run skip, and missing runtime skip.\n- Emit `codex.rollout_compression.file` outcomes for scanned,\ncompressed, skipped, and failed compression candidates.\n- Emit `codex.rollout_compression.temp_cleanup` and\n`codex.rollout_compression.materialize` counters for cleanup and\ndecompression paths.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just fmt`\n- `just test -p codex-rollout`\n- `just fix -p codex-rollout`","verified_at":"2026-06-01T20:26:32Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/9f4fac8ec4e74318ae272afedd118fc635a1023d","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/9f4fac8ec4e74318ae272afedd118fc635a1023d","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/9f4fac8ec4e74318ae272afedd118fc635a1023d/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"feb9eddc513c318adbda63bd953c1684deb6d8a3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/feb9eddc513c318adbda63bd953c1684deb6d8a3","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/feb9eddc513c318adbda63bd953c1684deb6d8a3"}]},{"sha":"feb9eddc513c318adbda63bd953c1684deb6d8a3","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGZlYjllZGRjNTEzYzMxOGFkYmRhNjNiZDk1M2MxNjg0ZGViNmQ4YTM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Michael Bolin","email":"mbolin@openai.com","date":"2026-06-01T20:22:28Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-01T20:22:28Z"},"message":"refactor: hide shell override for zsh fork unified exec (#24980)\n\n## Why\n\nWhen unified exec is configured to launch through the zsh fork, local\ncommands should not let the model override the shell binary with the\n`shell` parameter. The configured zsh fork is the mechanism that makes\n`execv(2)` interception reliable, so exposing `shell` for local zsh-fork\nexecution would create a confusing API surface and undermine the\ncomposition.\n\nRemote environments are different: zsh-fork interception is local-only,\nso remote unified-exec calls must keep direct unified-exec behavior and\nstill expose `shell` when a remote environment can be selected.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Taught the `exec_command` schema builder to omit the `shell` parameter\nwhen requested.\n- Hid `shell` from the unified-exec tool schema only when zsh-fork\nunified exec applies to all selectable environments.\n- Kept `shell` visible when any remote environment can be targeted,\nbecause those calls run through direct unified exec.\n- Made unified exec choose the effective shell mode per selected\nenvironment: local environments keep zsh-fork mode, remote environments\nuse direct mode.\n- Left direct unified-exec behavior unchanged, including support for\nmodel-specified shells there.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Added schema coverage showing `exec_command` can hide `shell`.\n- Added planner coverage showing zsh-fork unified exec hides `shell` for\nlocal-only execution while direct unified exec still exposes it.\n- Added planner coverage showing `shell` remains visible when a remote\nenvironment is available.\n- Added handler coverage showing remote environments use direct\nunified-exec shell mode instead of zsh-fork mode.\n- Ran the focused `codex-core` shell-parameter and zsh-fork tests.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n---\n[//]: # (BEGIN SAPLING FOOTER)\nStack created with [Sapling](https://sapling-scm.com). Best reviewed\nwith [ReviewStack](https://reviewstack.dev/openai/codex/pull/24980).\n* #24982\n* #24981\n* __->__ #24980","tree":{"sha":"3812fff5b366489acc95c39350a92d60a2ca264c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/3812fff5b366489acc95c39350a92d60a2ca264c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/feb9eddc513c318adbda63bd953c1684deb6d8a3","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHeoECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAic0QAIiOcFUIyFBNcGZ0fkTLlpNu\nbPIS0Wor96vpUNK1Elp11sESDkE1v1rDjjm5vYZdmSdRDA/PM5YaycXgXudLbqf+\nweIyJ6CSWxpxTNUbkNPmTCkvj1RerF9tukE+tH3mQyvqT9oa5zNaXOKXwXuvmdZP\nfig/baYY3u6QyuEYKqjnsbIBn9/X1ckwnewhq8zUT095doWVUW79IKdZlMn4uG+k\nkFZzTOY0X4wmPg7l5wufoCQE+P8RhR1s1PyuohLJWLjXdLmySF3HbW02b5bi8IOm\n0ki1YU53XsG8z/9BbYINVeKTDn7cKqurbg3jTLYmec3HGHGQFYpkuJzyavl3i9JB\n6rO9Oq+BZ4bioQ0bqwDbl6CSFDn5g+ZO1FWLjVjuh05hSPgkFBJSPC0HCZaQXrQh\naPt3NSw1ZKfhDKq/HTvMY7aTkzwxT69lPuV4ofxVf5m9JT8TbUgF/H2Hry8GnGVv\nq/vJItIeg2vSm1B28f9juQpqEizu8AgW0jOEK5YlhglwebFkCcZ5PJJbqfIAGqkN\nTAA8j8MYVintJLWxSVC2SjIXYSPa0bBflH2JRXTGjQwQEYFSZm4JA/f4CKe+ppSO\nBkhh4bsmkk/KDyNsgMFO3tHC7F6XWySRHDcdqw4JY9WBSwd/3qQp2Gaae12/yn1Q\nD7JtDjrXDWYOJtShnNsY\n=NZY7\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 3812fff5b366489acc95c39350a92d60a2ca264c\nparent d6748f741a188f5f681c69d26c258c2a3a409f1b\nauthor Michael Bolin <mbolin@openai.com> 1780345348 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780345348 +0000\n\nrefactor: hide shell override for zsh fork unified exec (#24980)\n\n## Why\n\nWhen unified exec is configured to launch through the zsh fork, local\ncommands should not let the model override the shell binary with the\n`shell` parameter. The configured zsh fork is the mechanism that makes\n`execv(2)` interception reliable, so exposing `shell` for local zsh-fork\nexecution would create a confusing API surface and undermine the\ncomposition.\n\nRemote environments are different: zsh-fork interception is local-only,\nso remote unified-exec calls must keep direct unified-exec behavior and\nstill expose `shell` when a remote environment can be selected.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Taught the `exec_command` schema builder to omit the `shell` parameter\nwhen requested.\n- Hid `shell` from the unified-exec tool schema only when zsh-fork\nunified exec applies to all selectable environments.\n- Kept `shell` visible when any remote environment can be targeted,\nbecause those calls run through direct unified exec.\n- Made unified exec choose the effective shell mode per selected\nenvironment: local environments keep zsh-fork mode, remote environments\nuse direct mode.\n- Left direct unified-exec behavior unchanged, including support for\nmodel-specified shells there.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Added schema coverage showing `exec_command` can hide `shell`.\n- Added planner coverage showing zsh-fork unified exec hides `shell` for\nlocal-only execution while direct unified exec still exposes it.\n- Added planner coverage showing `shell` remains visible when a remote\nenvironment is available.\n- Added handler coverage showing remote environments use direct\nunified-exec shell mode instead of zsh-fork mode.\n- Ran the focused `codex-core` shell-parameter and zsh-fork tests.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n---\n[//]: # (BEGIN SAPLING FOOTER)\nStack created with [Sapling](https://sapling-scm.com). Best reviewed\nwith [ReviewStack](https://reviewstack.dev/openai/codex/pull/24980).\n* #24982\n* #24981\n* __->__ #24980","verified_at":"2026-06-01T20:22:29Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/feb9eddc513c318adbda63bd953c1684deb6d8a3","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/feb9eddc513c318adbda63bd953c1684deb6d8a3","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/feb9eddc513c318adbda63bd953c1684deb6d8a3/comments","author":{"login":"bolinfest","id":655869,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTg2OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/655869?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest","html_url":"https://github.com/bolinfest","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"d6748f741a188f5f681c69d26c258c2a3a409f1b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/d6748f741a188f5f681c69d26c258c2a3a409f1b","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/d6748f741a188f5f681c69d26c258c2a3a409f1b"}]},{"sha":"d6748f741a188f5f681c69d26c258c2a3a409f1b","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGQ2NzQ4Zjc0MWExODhmNWY2ODFjNjlkMjZjMjU4YzJhM2E0MDlmMWI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Michael Bolin","email":"mbolin@openai.com","date":"2026-06-01T20:01:36Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-01T20:01:36Z"},"message":"feat: gate unified exec zsh fork composition (#24979)\n\n## Why\n\n`shell_zsh_fork` and unified exec need to remain independently\ncontrollable for enterprise rollouts, but we also need a third mode that\ncomposes them. That composed mode is intended to preserve unified exec\ncommand lifecycle support while letting the zsh fork provide more\naccurate `execv(2)` interception.\n\nEnabling `unified_exec_zsh_fork` by itself is intentionally not\nsufficient. It is a composition gate, not a dependency-enabling\nshortcut:\n\n- `unified_exec` selects the PTY-backed unified exec tool.\n- `shell_zsh_fork` opts into the zsh fork backend.\n- `unified_exec_zsh_fork` only allows those two already-enabled modes to\nbe composed so local zsh unified exec commands can launch through the\nzsh fork.\n\nThis separation is deliberate. Enterprises and staged rollouts must be\nable to enable or disable unified exec and zsh-fork independently. If\n`unified_exec_zsh_fork` implied either dependency, then enabling one\nunder-development composition flag would silently activate a shell\nbackend that the configured feature set left disabled.\n\nThis PR introduces only the configuration and planning gate for that\ncomposition. Existing `shell_zsh_fork` behavior continues to use the\nstandalone shell tool unless the new composition feature is explicitly\nenabled alongside both dependencies.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Added the under-development feature flag `unified_exec_zsh_fork`.\n- Added `UnifiedExecFeatureMode` so the three input feature flags\ncollapse into `Disabled`, `Direct`, or `ZshFork` mode before tool\nplanning.\n- Updated tool selection so zsh-fork composition requires\n`unified_exec`, `shell_zsh_fork`, and `unified_exec_zsh_fork`.\n- Kept the existing standalone zsh-fork shell tool behavior when only\n`shell_zsh_fork` is enabled.\n- Updated config schema output for the new feature flag.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Added feature and tool-config coverage for the new gate.\n- Added planner coverage proving `shell_zsh_fork` remains standalone\nuntil composition is explicitly enabled.\n- Ran focused tests for `codex-features`, `codex-tools`, and the\naffected `codex-core` planner case.\n\n\n\n\n\n---\n[//]: # (BEGIN SAPLING FOOTER)\nStack created with [Sapling](https://sapling-scm.com). Best reviewed\nwith [ReviewStack](https://reviewstack.dev/openai/codex/pull/24979).\n* #24982\n* #24981\n* #24980\n* __->__ #24979","tree":{"sha":"03926ae5e7e3e49f32c764ed0fcb0b45444c8c64","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/03926ae5e7e3e49f32c764ed0fcb0b45444c8c64"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/d6748f741a188f5f681c69d26c258c2a3a409f1b","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHeUgCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAS/UQABpBmjWeH+lRHSNskGwG+HvL\nQ6lLcCe/PviAGSZZVY7vumpGPQKtRYCWNXPA7JvVBrn8M5XLSGjt0zKLf0FK3nrk\nFHcvgLOraLh5X4UiV2DkUouz1btGdW9ietrjaTgfab/WwIPsXSXIJvXa1kJQY/KB\n5ovEuRawwoW3++xNVINnzGJXUVip20ag/M5s1I0rhpUJspmI/AA0LIQpOhLIvMDm\ny5CidAp9c1fOSXVxPbLLFUQo/uXZilJk740iq8Jn4eqKHT3YBqgzDBLV36b3s81+\nuMEnH3/aTX1MsSIMxZqSg5lVwWCH1hcnGs2opJ2NF378IVbI0HLrFN4UCEzf4bpM\nTOgsgWQBPSGVqmwRy4uUFuW7G7nw5/MHNHG6fPFUjNYDkh8jI8cI6ZRq0DUwVktS\ncZ9d/TK7tqj6zzZ9vM/NuLejFkEfCjkBIcnxFBhc+GnOqtMRrq7bx1crrvj7jH8q\nKdHPwPfv3ZKrAMBtqzUePT18Xa/sad9NroM0o1HAi6cQyYqu9b2Roj7wG7fU1Ue0\ngVTbfYWWHdfutePsAPZVE0gmLXrVwSyyxRu5v2OrJKUTktLYXuV3Pj7yPqj9plR+\nIGb4CL/RjVWPslIJMMMOFjBx9+57pGGpLXV0mS4mKI9+M6LJG9bMQr80fPOrbp+B\nrvU3nmWSxSxLKLPRSTOH\n=HSKe\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 03926ae5e7e3e49f32c764ed0fcb0b45444c8c64\nparent 009e6c4817c6cf1a9795bb2a57e4f7c7f191f897\nauthor Michael Bolin <mbolin@openai.com> 1780344096 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780344096 -0700\n\nfeat: gate unified exec zsh fork composition (#24979)\n\n## Why\n\n`shell_zsh_fork` and unified exec need to remain independently\ncontrollable for enterprise rollouts, but we also need a third mode that\ncomposes them. That composed mode is intended to preserve unified exec\ncommand lifecycle support while letting the zsh fork provide more\naccurate `execv(2)` interception.\n\nEnabling `unified_exec_zsh_fork` by itself is intentionally not\nsufficient. It is a composition gate, not a dependency-enabling\nshortcut:\n\n- `unified_exec` selects the PTY-backed unified exec tool.\n- `shell_zsh_fork` opts into the zsh fork backend.\n- `unified_exec_zsh_fork` only allows those two already-enabled modes to\nbe composed so local zsh unified exec commands can launch through the\nzsh fork.\n\nThis separation is deliberate. Enterprises and staged rollouts must be\nable to enable or disable unified exec and zsh-fork independently. If\n`unified_exec_zsh_fork` implied either dependency, then enabling one\nunder-development composition flag would silently activate a shell\nbackend that the configured feature set left disabled.\n\nThis PR introduces only the configuration and planning gate for that\ncomposition. Existing `shell_zsh_fork` behavior continues to use the\nstandalone shell tool unless the new composition feature is explicitly\nenabled alongside both dependencies.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Added the under-development feature flag `unified_exec_zsh_fork`.\n- Added `UnifiedExecFeatureMode` so the three input feature flags\ncollapse into `Disabled`, `Direct`, or `ZshFork` mode before tool\nplanning.\n- Updated tool selection so zsh-fork composition requires\n`unified_exec`, `shell_zsh_fork`, and `unified_exec_zsh_fork`.\n- Kept the existing standalone zsh-fork shell tool behavior when only\n`shell_zsh_fork` is enabled.\n- Updated config schema output for the new feature flag.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Added feature and tool-config coverage for the new gate.\n- Added planner coverage proving `shell_zsh_fork` remains standalone\nuntil composition is explicitly enabled.\n- Ran focused tests for `codex-features`, `codex-tools`, and the\naffected `codex-core` planner case.\n\n\n\n\n\n---\n[//]: # (BEGIN SAPLING FOOTER)\nStack created with [Sapling](https://sapling-scm.com). Best reviewed\nwith [ReviewStack](https://reviewstack.dev/openai/codex/pull/24979).\n* #24982\n* #24981\n* #24980\n* __->__ #24979","verified_at":"2026-06-01T20:01:37Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/d6748f741a188f5f681c69d26c258c2a3a409f1b","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/d6748f741a188f5f681c69d26c258c2a3a409f1b","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/d6748f741a188f5f681c69d26c258c2a3a409f1b/comments","author":{"login":"bolinfest","id":655869,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTg2OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/655869?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest","html_url":"https://github.com/bolinfest","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"009e6c4817c6cf1a9795bb2a57e4f7c7f191f897","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/009e6c4817c6cf1a9795bb2a57e4f7c7f191f897","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/009e6c4817c6cf1a9795bb2a57e4f7c7f191f897"}]},{"sha":"009e6c4817c6cf1a9795bb2a57e4f7c7f191f897","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDAwOWU2YzQ4MTdjNmNmMWE5Nzk1YmIyYTU3ZTRmN2M3ZjE5MWY4OTc","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif-oai","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-01T19:55:44Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-01T19:55:44Z"},"message":"fix: deflake zsh-fork approval test (#25669)\n\nFixes this flake:\nhttps://github.com/openai/codex/actions/runs/26773809591/job/78919970410?pr=25659\n\nThis test is about zsh-fork subcommand approval behavior, not workspace\nsandboxing, so it now runs with `DangerFullAccess` to avoid macOS\nsandbox setup failures before the second subcommand approval.","tree":{"sha":"54a9352add74ae8a6961c20d32bbcb4ac0c0cc02","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/54a9352add74ae8a6961c20d32bbcb4ac0c0cc02"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/009e6c4817c6cf1a9795bb2a57e4f7c7f191f897","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHePACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAhH4QACjHh8ITLMuheP/s189owIyD\nN2i7/psERNZPjCWm05ssRRbxcXjHggclXMvVyTL5Y6eki25o014gZHA8GZDJ7k8+\ncjyzrm49TSLhMbsWDujw9q5k7+OzEHGu4uKeux9Kvny31W4zt/raN0Jk/ww6Ihv1\nSjAmHypj34Z+Kt+KxMtDuGc88snRFKq22i+EJxrfLT49yTzuXMz9B2ybmLZAGtyK\njlslIQt7JyJOF08E6U77Vl4A5Qgmbcw1ynbcIe5wT9LSaejqKt5yUfkw04UFcR+6\ni9UnBuHgYzl4VMq1s78716NdkwwVPy/kpd7RsCheWOqSUmIS6h0FPEWtgd8DzjFw\n/xHzU7zNNhm6CzveD4N3DIg/w8EP6X0zQk5AszfFUz5tNm2gpnfdDg46Eavx5D4Q\nL0WQtFq15Xp3BtMij3KQJzmbIyeiau48/8OtQydZ/zxiUnb3NV5WvsA+o6ZOVIgZ\nQ3MqrZmHYrThAoGMhq7Ghf3+e7EAdFDTu5y7kzkwk7TEESN7EIcoDvYCTJazYT5L\nHUdj3v9Onva7M436WlE7UxiA/hiDD1hN9mvD7HFosGv/fNCfurREBTyIufdBjUJY\nIcT446Lu4vvPppm+4Y5txlaFeGAHp9Amnq1i/5BtQfAGyXUn04OZ6nh4GrmIHOpg\nJpnadNyxlAwpTOIXC6fh\n=G1B7\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 54a9352add74ae8a6961c20d32bbcb4ac0c0cc02\nparent 53ac02356e5a7223d90b21253f3e4f6c592fb656\nauthor jif-oai <jif@openai.com> 1780343744 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780343744 +0200\n\nfix: deflake zsh-fork approval test (#25669)\n\nFixes this flake:\nhttps://github.com/openai/codex/actions/runs/26773809591/job/78919970410?pr=25659\n\nThis test is about zsh-fork subcommand approval behavior, not workspace\nsandboxing, so it now runs with `DangerFullAccess` to avoid macOS\nsandbox setup failures before the second subcommand approval.","verified_at":"2026-06-01T19:55:44Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/009e6c4817c6cf1a9795bb2a57e4f7c7f191f897","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/009e6c4817c6cf1a9795bb2a57e4f7c7f191f897","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/009e6c4817c6cf1a9795bb2a57e4f7c7f191f897/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/user