NbQWsYAgeL9UD2Dryr4aRvz8JPmv7oZgcRzNKd\nInPJZxoYqWdpoXjm0XqgQWjLZ3FrBzJjMn9493RX0Uk4SLhShisJ2LAlTi74vc30\nhBrM78iuB41EZCEh+D5E2MdA4MW3KRkdoj5yZi5D2FLe15agSNl54asldzWiUQRH\nUgOFWNfmupB3X2EVIW1eY3RGAfqnZBNItTU/mC6wV73tL7ol3d1c/lYNU+WqcLg6\nEKYLXkzIEzDvlr1whdpRL1vqacV75HYBTRXJk9kWHG/nCCfD3rCmJqL5MIKc6gDq\npmF/XqRED8Fs889Ue7CRPBZl7wnaArXXUetTYfj43VqtCNUi2A6e3PfTX2R3XoZV\n3oPVlZPWUob8VNCwx4zyO+D2VQAen625EsZ5SfJOFRtT16sgOZARxDnU8e4RtXHU\nsmmEetCsrbh5ZttaD5VDDMfA1UGlCQsUfteRIH6XvuVf3xbt8KrW9zwtW0m1c/jy\nxtqHGueKCOBlLIYzn0B3PLa8iJGihRKTcSXxwFeMaC+1Z+EpWuNxcl02CL0HBIgd\ng1axZVePcXr6OI6c1Qt79vp/N/7Z+yVWp4lh9GODhjwo/0iM0KdSHaWQWMKWGyxY\ngFmJ/JrqjMbFnlYaSEGB\n=UY3o\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree e33550ccfa0857cad28476a4ea821141c86e9a34\nparent f1609d9fb6ee42fdd8ef475992a09a5e2c082ef5\nauthor starr-openai <starr@openai.com> 1780340011 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780340011 -0700\n\nexec-server: canonicalize bound filesystem paths (#25149)\n\n## Summary\n- add executor filesystem canonicalization as a bound-path operation\n- route remote canonicalization through the exec-server filesystem RPC\nsurface\n- keep path normalization attached to the filesystem that owns the path\n\n## Stack\n- 2/5 in the skills path authority stack extracted from\nhttps://github.com/openai/codex/pull/25098\n- follows merged https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/25121\n\n## Validation\n- `cd\n/Users/starr/code/codex-worktrees/pr-25098-restack-review-pr1b/codex-rs\n&& just fmt`\n- Not run: tests/checks (not requested)\n- GitHub CI pending on rewritten head","verified_at":"2026-06-01T18:53:32Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/53ac02356e5a7223d90b21253f3e4f6c592fb656","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/53ac02356e5a7223d90b21253f3e4f6c592fb656","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/53ac02356e5a7223d90b21253f3e4f6c592fb656/comments","author":{"login":"starr-openai","id":176426273,"node_id":"U_kgDOCoQNIQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176426273?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/starr-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/starr-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/starr-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/starr-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/starr-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/starr-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/starr-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/starr-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/starr-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/starr-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/starr-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"f1609d9fb6ee42fdd8ef475992a09a5e2c082ef5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f1609d9fb6ee42fdd8ef475992a09a5e2c082ef5","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/f1609d9fb6ee42fdd8ef475992a09a5e2c082ef5"}]},{"sha":"f1609d9fb6ee42fdd8ef475992a09a5e2c082ef5","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGYxNjA5ZDlmYjZlZTQyZmRkOGVmNDc1OTkyYTA5YTVlMmMwODJlZjU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Won Park","email":"won@openai.com","date":"2026-06-01T18:51:15Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-01T18:51:15Z"},"message":"[codex-rs] auto-review model override  (#23767)\n\n## Why\n\nGuardian auto-review normally uses the provider-preferred review model\nwhen one is available. Some parent models need model-catalog metadata to\nselect a different review model while keeping older `/models` payloads\ncompatible when that metadata is absent.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Added optional `ModelInfo::auto_review_model_override` metadata to the\npublic model payload as a review-model slug.\n- Updated Guardian review model selection to prefer the catalog override\nwhen present, while preserving the existing provider preferred-model\npath and parent-model fallback when it is omitted.\n- Added focused Guardian coverage for override and no-override model\nselection.\n- Added an `auto_review` core integration suite test that loads override\nmetadata from a remote model catalog path and asserts the strict\nauto-review `/responses` request uses the catalog-selected review model.\n- Updated existing `ModelInfo` fixtures and local catalog constructors\nfor the new optional field.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `cargo test -p codex-protocol\nmodel_info_defaults_availability_nux_to_none_when_omitted`\n- `cargo test -p codex-core guardian_review_uses_`\n- `cargo test -p codex-core\nremote_model_override_uses_catalog_model_for_strict_auto_review --test\nall`\n- `just fix -p codex-protocol`\n- `just fix -p codex-core`\n- `just fmt`\n- `git diff --check`","tree":{"sha":"a019ff3a310b475cb002e9b991bb408d262de936","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/a019ff3a310b475cb002e9b991bb408d262de936"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/f1609d9fb6ee42fdd8ef475992a09a5e2c082ef5","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHdSjCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAskoQAJ3cG2umYcPzKeR7oIhc6ydW\ni4WTi+DSRRCihPgVLNVW7vyhcNPHcNmZZgFX1aQonx15ouzlC/AV0RSYsugVUlv/\nlB+UJ1IecgvyN7eRxv2hlYnyI8urWee376Li4s+jDdurJH6v40I9Erf84l3hxe2t\nPDh5miyH17lF2RY6Knmf0FQn4wMwErrEivIK6CMgSHprWSkaUBrwcZrPz5lj9uz4\no/f57ZmN9AY9CJ4qE83aAL9ukeKaMrTUt3LTwOs2c0+9bP6VUOPtrSfZIMWsoZ67\nx34fLCvmwYDd89eC8G+EIUcMGEVATsZZdKMBqrMvIZuywwHXRR0saFTXEkJp+yfE\nD71NzapH8ggC8m8m/lhAazmCwDUqhfbm+XeDbjgy2Go+ph5DuIeMsNcp/kAO68xD\nqnnwMTDWZd01Xa/s5S/th+XjnEKHYC4BQslWs7LaemwaAJOucIrO0jo45Mv+F8Oa\nU5dJScS13RbwPwprzC6TWPUuA9fds1k/j2e9KAv3IT7C+4UbExL8pGhoARZFcc6Y\nZd3QTzs4wU2y98EKO0BVakNonaHanMR+uIoT2eMGfuyXjBVWuDm0ByNAfPN1LvsG\nxdJm9stFqEiSc78ePnCzs3qavoPAPyZB/e6E7feaaD4wsjoz9mtj/qpMiButtRmm\ndWMRLwLbE1H41UwIam/2\n=Tu4Q\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a019ff3a310b475cb002e9b991bb408d262de936\nparent 281b416c441d3744c07c7c26aae73ee69dd39418\nauthor Won Park <won@openai.com> 1780339875 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780339875 -0700\n\n[codex-rs] auto-review model override  (#23767)\n\n## Why\n\nGuardian auto-review normally uses the provider-preferred review model\nwhen one is available. Some parent models need model-catalog metadata to\nselect a different review model while keeping older `/models` payloads\ncompatible when that metadata is absent.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Added optional `ModelInfo::auto_review_model_override` metadata to the\npublic model payload as a review-model slug.\n- Updated Guardian review model selection to prefer the catalog override\nwhen present, while preserving the existing provider preferred-model\npath and parent-model fallback when it is omitted.\n- Added focused Guardian coverage for override and no-override model\nselection.\n- Added an `auto_review` core integration suite test that loads override\nmetadata from a remote model catalog path and asserts the strict\nauto-review `/responses` request uses the catalog-selected review model.\n- Updated existing `ModelInfo` fixtures and local catalog constructors\nfor the new optional field.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `cargo test -p codex-protocol\nmodel_info_defaults_availability_nux_to_none_when_omitted`\n- `cargo test -p codex-core guardian_review_uses_`\n- `cargo test -p codex-core\nremote_model_override_uses_catalog_model_for_strict_auto_review --test\nall`\n- `just fix -p codex-protocol`\n- `just fix -p codex-core`\n- `just fmt`\n- `git diff --check`","verified_at":"2026-06-01T18:51:16Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f1609d9fb6ee42fdd8ef475992a09a5e2c082ef5","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/f1609d9fb6ee42fdd8ef475992a09a5e2c082ef5","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f1609d9fb6ee42fdd8ef475992a09a5e2c082ef5/comments","author":{"login":"won-openai","id":262224683,"node_id":"U_kgDOD6E7Kw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/262224683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/won-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"281b416c441d3744c07c7c26aae73ee69dd39418","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/281b416c441d3744c07c7c26aae73ee69dd39418","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/281b416c441d3744c07c7c26aae73ee69dd39418"}]},{"sha":"281b416c441d3744c07c7c26aae73ee69dd39418","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDI4MWI0MTZjNDQxZDM3NDRjMDdjN2MyNmFhZTczZWU2OWRkMzk0MTg","commit":{"author":{"name":"Adam Perry @ OpenAI","email":"anp@openai.com","date":"2026-06-01T18:50:23Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-01T18:50:23Z"},"message":"Check root Python script formatting in CI (#25165)\n\n## Why\n\nPython files under `scripts/` were not covered by the repository\nformatting recipe or the CI formatting job, so formatting drift could\nmerge unnoticed.\n\n## What\n\n- Add a dedicated `scripts/pyproject.toml` and `scripts/uv.lock` so\nroot-script formatting uses a locked Ruff version.\n- Extend `just fmt` to format root Python scripts and add\n`fmt-scripts-check` for CI.\n- Run `just fmt-scripts-check` from `.github/workflows/ci.yml`,\ninstalling `uv` through SHA-pinned `astral-sh/setup-uv` while retaining\nthe `uv` `0.11.3` pin.\n- Apply Ruff formatting to the root Python scripts, including\n`scripts/just-shell.py`, and extend\n`sdk/python/tests/test_artifact_workflow_and_binaries.py` to cover the\nroot formatting recipe.\n- Update `AGENTS.md` so agents run `just fmt` after code changes\nanywhere in the repository.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Extended the existing Python SDK workflow test to assert that `just\nfmt` includes root Python scripts.","tree":{"sha":"0fa995871278305088b68bc9bfb01ba1d9ea19e0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/0fa995871278305088b68bc9bfb01ba1d9ea19e0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/281b416c441d3744c07c7c26aae73ee69dd39418","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHdRvCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAHSIQAGVZJqhgrDoI3b1x29HgbLer\nd/eEUybOjvU5TAMUYhHU2lCyTPPktsVx3duH7zjNyzP/ahdF8GVvjc6o0yAz42IV\ngk5uuMZdi0zpKNc+6D2VY8Z/yurT9RgQ4pzhGYy41ElwP9qrrB/cXKVNHq+0iB2c\n4R8h4afC6XIPZHQs2VFhDfJx5gmARjZIxHshSZQWrCf+5fCb0HdRf4pf92aHQEyH\nlQ1IOP38nnrl5cIE1zNSOi5iTEDGWRdFQA54vbBJDOQHGWFz3eApq26G/w5ebF+V\nQFxsuk91ferJLWMe9oN3U1KCCwcqgirR4ZH9Ao7Xfghor0GKHfpgJeIBRjN5VdQi\nNCInbC0/D4AZldEtmEDt5fQH7AFqfBVp9aNVkVCkWBz/uCHIAcOLy1u3Zl/Yv6+Q\nNMXDeOIuRuoRtUpsHqDQikCXgX8wQ/RjxPc7+jt3Dip63+FSCqBA66Wic1x4TUDR\nSOQU/RWe9HqbUxM5R1tIOtzx/lkrT4hs2a8ngWTFt5tpW3lR166ejlGR9WnT64AN\ncO/pZEAVR7/acWrAwDupyMaOzjEnW9u9sBZQMR+Qb/a5iusO10iJERZ+aUpP9YvQ\nd0PHvaW27ZoDTzlqHR8Fh+gjPOHLK91oCkUBeLq9DxjMlbiXFinJXXuKEOY22Ms6\nSyGCEJUBSpzjRqJXMhS/\n=x3mh\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 0fa995871278305088b68bc9bfb01ba1d9ea19e0\nparent c3cdf3c00793252cd93dd9790679ee49d1bd40b3\nauthor Adam Perry @ OpenAI <anp@openai.com> 1780339823 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780339823 +0000\n\nCheck root Python script formatting in CI (#25165)\n\n## Why\n\nPython files under `scripts/` were not covered by the repository\nformatting recipe or the CI formatting job, so formatting drift could\nmerge unnoticed.\n\n## What\n\n- Add a dedicated `scripts/pyproject.toml` and `scripts/uv.lock` so\nroot-script formatting uses a locked Ruff version.\n- Extend `just fmt` to format root Python scripts and add\n`fmt-scripts-check` for CI.\n- Run `just fmt-scripts-check` from `.github/workflows/ci.yml`,\ninstalling `uv` through SHA-pinned `astral-sh/setup-uv` while retaining\nthe `uv` `0.11.3` pin.\n- Apply Ruff formatting to the root Python scripts, including\n`scripts/just-shell.py`, and extend\n`sdk/python/tests/test_artifact_workflow_and_binaries.py` to cover the\nroot formatting recipe.\n- Update `AGENTS.md` so agents run `just fmt` after code changes\nanywhere in the repository.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Extended the existing Python SDK workflow test to assert that `just\nfmt` includes root Python scripts.","verified_at":"2026-06-01T18:50:23Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/281b416c441d3744c07c7c26aae73ee69dd39418","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/281b416c441d3744c07c7c26aae73ee69dd39418","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/281b416c441d3744c07c7c26aae73ee69dd39418/comments","author":{"login":"anp-oai","id":286154589,"node_id":"U_kgDOEQ5fXQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/286154589?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/anp-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"c3cdf3c00793252cd93dd9790679ee49d1bd40b3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c3cdf3c00793252cd93dd9790679ee49d1bd40b3","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/c3cdf3c00793252cd93dd9790679ee49d1bd40b3"}]},{"sha":"c3cdf3c00793252cd93dd9790679ee49d1bd40b3","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGMzY2RmM2MwMDc5MzI1MmNkOTNkZDk3OTA2NzllZTQ5ZDFiZDQwYjM","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif-oai","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-01T18:46:54Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-01T18:46:54Z"},"message":"Throttle repeated rollout compression runs (#25659)\n\n## Why\n\n[#25089](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/25089) introduced the\nbackground worker that compresses cold archived rollouts, and\n[#25654](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/25654) made that pass\nfaster once it starts. But the worker still deleted\n`rollout-compression.lock` on successful exit, so the existing six-hour\nstaleness window only helped with overlapping or crashed workers. Each\nnew local thread-store initialization could immediately rescan archived\nrollouts even if a full pass had just finished.\n\nThis change keeps the existing marker around long enough to throttle\nredundant reruns. The worker is still best-effort, but it no longer does\nrepeated startup scans when nothing new is eligible for compression.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Replace the drop-scoped `CompressionLock` with a\n`CompressionRunMarker` that claims the existing\n`.tmp/rollout-compression.lock` path and leaves it in place after\nsuccess.\n- Reuse the existing six-hour staleness window to block both overlapping\nstarts and immediate reruns, while still letting a stale marker be\nreclaimed.\n- Update the worker docs and debug logging to describe the new \"already\nrunning or recently ran\" behavior.\n- Extend the rollout compression tests to assert that a successful run\nleaves the marker behind and that a fresh marker suppresses a new run.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-rollout`","tree":{"sha":"efca84bdaa0eb5e4c40c76f23fd59011e1fa3adf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/efca84bdaa0eb5e4c40c76f23fd59011e1fa3adf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/c3cdf3c00793252cd93dd9790679ee49d1bd40b3","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHdOeCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAFwUQAJa10t5YqF+i4bJoQFtwbbw1\nPLa73O5gCNGQ4T+QJ10yfFWWMPxpFBIQJkMF+jS9sjOOSXj4Q+8d79Y/Kk8lCPLh\ncc9GBqrBsKz9KEtzqC2/SAPYhMBPQwaxsqy/oxBqqzqTy0rWIAmE5EvYSZ20s5Tv\nTEiGrfdZeABHvfzWLfHQZs8G8z/Zd+6AllC3AjoQoJRcOaT44McKGzwqOY5P+vFr\nBBNd0fhJJtRW2cxTLejo28hQwb2DCBBcqa13grkdpWt3F2xOX5dSvdstOeFjSXK0\nVgvmcsBUfY7Vp9yHBqkzTvGC1cIOPlNjO25tS1JGk1iYG0FNiBUueWqpCMpZIv+I\nGxkOHep4HXU7pGO8IIO0xmWgjCiX2W+6vZCOJ/iEXIyYEgO4EUCr4jCVyetPlVD5\nNd67/v52/YJwuVu+Fz9uhZ1yZPOL7h09RX/G4Ru+clVnLhVp6yZ4pb9QfXoRbs31\nU8qiEqj+znNfRpbjtM/myKke8NF5+VWdjwP0xsrKIXtappDEt4tYgyHalPJBQ3wI\nHt+MGCHrUZ6hO9QEGq8UcR4QVkv3vA7J3s8iQT2WsuTXKz5vFfbwrpbJH25/bIl3\nx4lurbGSNotkCUg70IekwmeQdHKORttaHi1tzavYiw0/YQkLrVbMdDVASG7sj+7v\n8E4/e6W4vZpUb391b+9n\n=8H7z\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree efca84bdaa0eb5e4c40c76f23fd59011e1fa3adf\nparent ba2b67f9cda954bcdda43c2a65ac58e807b996bd\nauthor jif-oai <jif@openai.com> 1780339614 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780339614 +0200\n\nThrottle repeated rollout compression runs (#25659)\n\n## Why\n\n[#25089](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/25089) introduced the\nbackground worker that compresses cold archived rollouts, and\n[#25654](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/25654) made that pass\nfaster once it starts. But the worker still deleted\n`rollout-compression.lock` on successful exit, so the existing six-hour\nstaleness window only helped with overlapping or crashed workers. Each\nnew local thread-store initialization could immediately rescan archived\nrollouts even if a full pass had just finished.\n\nThis change keeps the existing marker around long enough to throttle\nredundant reruns. The worker is still best-effort, but it no longer does\nrepeated startup scans when nothing new is eligible for compression.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Replace the drop-scoped `CompressionLock` with a\n`CompressionRunMarker` that claims the existing\n`.tmp/rollout-compression.lock` path and leaves it in place after\nsuccess.\n- Reuse the existing six-hour staleness window to block both overlapping\nstarts and immediate reruns, while still letting a stale marker be\nreclaimed.\n- Update the worker docs and debug logging to describe the new \"already\nrunning or recently ran\" behavior.\n- Extend the rollout compression tests to assert that a successful run\nleaves the marker behind and that a fresh marker suppresses a new run.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-rollout`","verified_at":"2026-06-01T18:46:56Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c3cdf3c00793252cd93dd9790679ee49d1bd40b3","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/c3cdf3c00793252cd93dd9790679ee49d1bd40b3","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c3cdf3c00793252cd93dd9790679ee49d1bd40b3/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"ba2b67f9cda954bcdda43c2a65ac58e807b996bd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ba2b67f9cda954bcdda43c2a65ac58e807b996bd","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/ba2b67f9cda954bcdda43c2a65ac58e807b996bd"}]},{"sha":"ba2b67f9cda954bcdda43c2a65ac58e807b996bd","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGJhMmI2N2Y5Y2RhOTU0YmNkZGE0M2MyYTY1YWM1OGU4MDdiOTk2YmQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Adam Perry @ OpenAI","email":"anp@openai.com","date":"2026-06-01T18:45:07Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-01T18:45:07Z"},"message":"[codex] Consolidate shared prompts in codex-prompts (#25151)\n\n## Why\n\n`codex_core` is consistently a bottleneck for incremental builds during\niteration. The simplest fix is to make the crate smaller.\n\n## Summary\n\n`codex-core` owns several reusable prompt renderers and static prompt\nassets, which makes the crate harder to split apart.\n\nRename `codex-review-prompts` to `codex-prompts` and move shared review,\ngoal, permissions, compaction, realtime, hierarchical AGENTS.md, and\n`apply_patch` prompts into it. Move prompt-only tests and update\nconsumers and `CODEOWNERS`.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-prompts -p codex-apply-patch`\n- `just test -p codex-core prompt_caching`\n- Bazel builds for the affected crates","tree":{"sha":"b31f44e0244039cd254ab0b6d02d0402768c823c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/b31f44e0244039cd254ab0b6d02d0402768c823c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/ba2b67f9cda954bcdda43c2a65ac58e807b996bd","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHdMzCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAynAQAKay966ErtPCFKNym6/spGq4\nPcZAqgvBX0VjjI1VTNSdqklPdAhALKPeZnjuBMB/aA4issKqBlLY5UIMisXanXLr\n9X+ylbfOoIOLfwYKhx+qBFn3BsdZ8qmQ3QsEQKgW/vbXDTrzxZmCr83/d+kaen7O\n2eTEYySkecAJtGOBT6yR532fNhMqw94T7GrzkZJlKnpr+F/Wh+cdxedak0AfaPaE\nWiwLSvf1pJVgPWbSGxB1e0ofATSwB9UuvQNrh99+1VK6TMjCL2ehwPnwf70EXbtK\nvI7g8XC6tCa7VVf2/w16u2ml2woPa6+kPE45VfcgR/WLJhoQ2yWXXkJ8M2MuzPEv\nlnqrBI5qPJCkTLxrTutsda0Sr1t1PmQqgL5aUofgLLp5XGL81XXE4W5bWrEkvxqu\nshn2411SGG9ybqbuWZgdYN43A+7bd2v0iPRMI/89YYqdHcESN9yBvQEpKycboOr5\n2u/KXRlqtPiU/KNLq4R20wnPmnMjzZATi6ymdlwdesk7iNu+svfMu2FyB9y+vb+T\noctr1OQ3mY1fArHgnbL3i+9Qu+t0rXbhUVIUJRjeWQVoa32tKISbEnklgHISTNN/\ng4/p2O6CUJK4Jpvng5fKvNJcuIwGy4HpUE6zqTjzO0IEYA3e+dhU3XyFArl/uCXS\nKZGbcL27CTQri4p9MY0g\n=1gU3\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree b31f44e0244039cd254ab0b6d02d0402768c823c\nparent 88c7a4ff074df9e2161c947ca6d91bf824b9d6e6\nauthor Adam Perry @ OpenAI <anp@openai.com> 1780339507 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780339507 +0000\n\n[codex] Consolidate shared prompts in codex-prompts (#25151)\n\n## Why\n\n`codex_core` is consistently a bottleneck for incremental builds during\niteration. The simplest fix is to make the crate smaller.\n\n## Summary\n\n`codex-core` owns several reusable prompt renderers and static prompt\nassets, which makes the crate harder to split apart.\n\nRename `codex-review-prompts` to `codex-prompts` and move shared review,\ngoal, permissions, compaction, realtime, hierarchical AGENTS.md, and\n`apply_patch` prompts into it. Move prompt-only tests and update\nconsumers and `CODEOWNERS`.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-prompts -p codex-apply-patch`\n- `just test -p codex-core prompt_caching`\n- Bazel builds for the affected crates","verified_at":"2026-06-01T18:45:08Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ba2b67f9cda954bcdda43c2a65ac58e807b996bd","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/ba2b67f9cda954bcdda43c2a65ac58e807b996bd","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ba2b67f9cda954bcdda43c2a65ac58e807b996bd/comments","author":{"login":"anp-oai","id":286154589,"node_id":"U_kgDOEQ5fXQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/286154589?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/anp-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"88c7a4ff074df9e2161c947ca6d91bf824b9d6e6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/88c7a4ff074df9e2161c947ca6d91bf824b9d6e6","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/88c7a4ff074df9e2161c947ca6d91bf824b9d6e6"}]},{"sha":"88c7a4ff074df9e2161c947ca6d91bf824b9d6e6","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDg4YzdhNGZmMDc0ZGY5ZTIxNjFjOTQ3Y2E2ZDkxYmY4MjRiOWQ2ZTY","commit":{"author":{"name":"iceweasel-oai","email":"iceweasel@openai.com","date":"2026-06-01T18:26:36Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-01T18:26:36Z"},"message":"[codex] Make justfile recipes Windows-aware (#24983)\n\n## Summary\n\nMake the root `justfile` usable from Windows without maintaining a\nseparate Windows copy of most recipes.\n\nThe repo recipes previously assumed POSIX shell behavior for things like\nvariadic argument forwarding (`\"$@\"`) and stderr redirection\n(`2>/dev/null`). That made common workflows such as `just fmt`, `just\ntest`, and `just log` unreliable from Windows. This PR introduces a\nsmall cross-platform shell adapter so recipes can stay mostly unified\nwhile still expanding the few shell-specific constructs correctly on\nmacOS/Linux and Windows.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Add `scripts/just-shell.py` as the configured `just` shell adapter.\n  - On Unix it invokes `sh -cu`.\n- On Windows it invokes `pwsh -CommandWithArgs` so arguments containing\nspaces are preserved.\n- Add portable recipe placeholders:\n- `{args}` expands to `\"$@\"` on Unix and the equivalent PowerShell\nforwarded-args expression on Windows.\n- `{stderr-null}` expands to the platform-specific stderr suppression\nused by `fmt`.\n- Convert most variadic one-line recipes to the unified `{args}` form,\nincluding `codex`, `exec`, `file-search`, `app-server-test-client`,\n`fix`, `clippy`, `bench`, `mcp-server-run`, `write-app-server-schema`,\nand `argument-comment-lint-from-source`.\n- Keep genuinely shell-specific recipes split or Unix-only for now,\nincluding recipes backed by `.sh` scripts or recipes whose bodies are\nmore than simple command forwarding.\n- Add a Windows `just install` path that installs PowerShell via\n`winget` when `pwsh` is not available, then runs the same basic Rust\nsetup steps.\n- Update the SDK test that validates the root `fmt` recipe so it\nrecognizes the new portable stderr placeholder.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just --summary`\n- `just --dry-run fmt`\n- `just --dry-run bench-smoke`\n- `just --dry-run codex foo \"bar binky\" baz`\n- `just --dry-run write-hooks-schema`\n- `just --dry-run bazel-lock-update`\n- `just --dry-run argument-comment-lint-from-source -- \"foo bar\"`\n- `git diff --check -- justfile scripts/just-shell.py\nsdk/python/tests/test_artifact_workflow_and_binaries.py`\n- Verified Windows argv preservation through `scripts/just-shell.py`\nwith arguments containing spaces.\n- `uv run --frozen --project sdk/python --extra dev pytest\nsdk/python/tests/test_artifact_workflow_and_binaries.py::test_root_fmt_recipe_formats_rust_and_python_sdk`","tree":{"sha":"6687a238d29f8e3b599a07a251b9c21c7aa87449","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/6687a238d29f8e3b599a07a251b9c21c7aa87449"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/88c7a4ff074df9e2161c947ca6d91bf824b9d6e6","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHc7cCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAltEQAE24m00jEWK42SGJtNl5RkRA\nZ/AU+FkW+2wVgKp9UCF3+LdnAomRHHm056LZp9OCBGF67InlJOKIsDCl2HJWDjuR\nUWzZTawynitolf2nI08TiMgtudgnwWkYnp4DwRk+24cDUMCXf8uTnMaW+mCnYyn9\nj1cVDOSbTmwkhdYo0zULGJidlhDKsPxKlG9EJJNB/EQn5TX3GQ8nl4mLCTTOuPfW\nr/xllwtAuojuSiXKi5HfDZ4KWk17KvEB5ZDOyeCJf7n3DzUlsileMQFBU2cFqk2A\nH2Cjj6UyxmhSNSWD+Kz+lg0gAy2i3HsX/iQNqjdDuvqECBQQo1W5FniBpratmiLN\nCn2Kn5oO3bZhuNOrQO7JiE4ObqJ/bNeaVgd64b1Jb+gLUP+/X/jlw2rQ3s2kyNoj\naHf/tmSMPo6dU54VCz5ItBIXSSQE2DF4n0//FtdIM289nO1lGmmh4ZilLdmfU1ll\niNndTf9REpWauEvZzx86x0KrPWEVOiahw8Su7LXDa0eNRgpvCFKJYuFjbv/jY9DM\net6zxohz7cYztlnRb/eoccbtX3YDqINCfv2OagWvvNE6gtNW/Sptyug7ncKfJ19N\nUjyApxcP6EBuPugocbaK7l3ag2pYDxzVPp1KOAkI8UxKx9vDAO40wZGmbrwxcBxm\nGaRlmUENFLqm5KuUBhfg\n=fEEk\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 6687a238d29f8e3b599a07a251b9c21c7aa87449\nparent 9756316d89968945212cd5f958b2b972c77c9e09\nauthor iceweasel-oai <iceweasel@openai.com> 1780338396 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780338396 -0700\n\n[codex] Make justfile recipes Windows-aware (#24983)\n\n## Summary\n\nMake the root `justfile` usable from Windows without maintaining a\nseparate Windows copy of most recipes.\n\nThe repo recipes previously assumed POSIX shell behavior for things like\nvariadic argument forwarding (`\"$@\"`) and stderr redirection\n(`2>/dev/null`). That made common workflows such as `just fmt`, `just\ntest`, and `just log` unreliable from Windows. This PR introduces a\nsmall cross-platform shell adapter so recipes can stay mostly unified\nwhile still expanding the few shell-specific constructs correctly on\nmacOS/Linux and Windows.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Add `scripts/just-shell.py` as the configured `just` shell adapter.\n  - On Unix it invokes `sh -cu`.\n- On Windows it invokes `pwsh -CommandWithArgs` so arguments containing\nspaces are preserved.\n- Add portable recipe placeholders:\n- `{args}` expands to `\"$@\"` on Unix and the equivalent PowerShell\nforwarded-args expression on Windows.\n- `{stderr-null}` expands to the platform-specific stderr suppression\nused by `fmt`.\n- Convert most variadic one-line recipes to the unified `{args}` form,\nincluding `codex`, `exec`, `file-search`, `app-server-test-client`,\n`fix`, `clippy`, `bench`, `mcp-server-run`, `write-app-server-schema`,\nand `argument-comment-lint-from-source`.\n- Keep genuinely shell-specific recipes split or Unix-only for now,\nincluding recipes backed by `.sh` scripts or recipes whose bodies are\nmore than simple command forwarding.\n- Add a Windows `just install` path that installs PowerShell via\n`winget` when `pwsh` is not available, then runs the same basic Rust\nsetup steps.\n- Update the SDK test that validates the root `fmt` recipe so it\nrecognizes the new portable stderr placeholder.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just --summary`\n- `just --dry-run fmt`\n- `just --dry-run bench-smoke`\n- `just --dry-run codex foo \"bar binky\" baz`\n- `just --dry-run write-hooks-schema`\n- `just --dry-run bazel-lock-update`\n- `just --dry-run argument-comment-lint-from-source -- \"foo bar\"`\n- `git diff --check -- justfile scripts/just-shell.py\nsdk/python/tests/test_artifact_workflow_and_binaries.py`\n- Verified Windows argv preservation through `scripts/just-shell.py`\nwith arguments containing spaces.\n- `uv run --frozen --project sdk/python --extra dev pytest\nsdk/python/tests/test_artifact_workflow_and_binaries.py::test_root_fmt_recipe_formats_rust_and_python_sdk`","verified_at":"2026-06-01T18:26:37Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/88c7a4ff074df9e2161c947ca6d91bf824b9d6e6","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/88c7a4ff074df9e2161c947ca6d91bf824b9d6e6","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/88c7a4ff074df9e2161c947ca6d91bf824b9d6e6/comments","author":{"login":"iceweasel-oai","id":234057055,"node_id":"U_kgDODfNtXw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/234057055?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/iceweasel-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"9756316d89968945212cd5f958b2b972c77c9e09","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/9756316d89968945212cd5f958b2b972c77c9e09","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/9756316d89968945212cd5f958b2b972c77c9e09"}]},{"sha":"9756316d89968945212cd5f958b2b972c77c9e09","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDk3NTYzMTZkODk5Njg5NDUyMTJjZDVmOTU4YjJiOTcyYzc3YzllMDk","commit":{"author":{"name":"charlesgong-openai","email":"charlesgong@openai.com","date":"2026-06-01T18:04:21Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-01T18:04:21Z"},"message":"Preserve plugin app manifest order (#25491)\n\n## Summary\n- Preserve app declaration order when loading plugin .app.json files.\n- Keep plugin connector summaries in plugin app order after connector\nmetadata is merged and filtered.\n- Add regression coverage for .app.json order and connector summary\norder.\n\n## Validation\n- just fmt\n- just test -p codex-chatgpt\nconnectors_for_plugin_apps_returns_only_requested_plugin_apps\n- just test -p codex-core-plugins\neffective_apps_preserves_app_config_order\n- just fix -p codex-core-plugins (passes with existing clippy\nlarge_enum_variant warning in core-plugins/src/manifest.rs)\n- just fix -p codex-chatgpt\n- just bazel-lock-update\n- just bazel-lock-check","tree":{"sha":"8478fc70ca0659e725460682a51991d381e73c2e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/8478fc70ca0659e725460682a51991d381e73c2e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/9756316d89968945212cd5f958b2b972c77c9e09","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHcmlCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAbSgQAD3BeXoKlD6vCI2ZzwrB+CIa\n2fmxUDfWG8prxto/5x6HGNz8Yf0Tr2aWZtJ1fPA2e66dk1H7hEbMORXXbjJq9aCJ\nFoc/dJSPOauTYM/V2vONcyMT5wGSIE7fqyAnzzaksj38vq+Dcf7w11ROSLCDAqbn\nnnKc+bB+9M+H2jfW3mtmZJUH2kA496ofr1VW+g6qbrjRDJ4enVWascm6B86AFDbH\nf3ObLhCrbDAPN3JRipWk4dMCp3sSBobpREt4QEai4VZu6Yl3OqSLXGYKOnaVfbpl\nA8Ao8v1i9FA7FFJA/CLDgfwJ3SJYTC40IB1xCJ8cVO3KtzIZ1Zz5/D4J1hdHw2Gw\n1WL4lOMdQ+DEJhvxscLIAhLYU1/bm8o03ARw05rBkgZ5V5SRu2K6F5wnHoIR4Rgc\njxVHvyJpHN0G6zBSYsuQHjdtrScvbRpyjpGGJU4oJ+/tWiRWocZiDeO3n/85SOyF\nkVzfuxH8PFFjA/oX6wNOO/2Ne4K5TiWGQCSFVLhijTjZrzwsdYODUtIBXoli+zvi\nCxqOobmusP63CZI6lcpSByS4/riaw0CLdbMA+ICNHljwMXMOY1X4YKjD+drijo/Q\njW2IOpdLU5GdkjFq7zKrHSNLNnwEXNmafL2s0LnYAj03518z1HPIuCA6YL/dJS6S\nxEJTdkyhJs5wVBTqWysm\n=Jawf\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 8478fc70ca0659e725460682a51991d381e73c2e\nparent 6ddb747e7687e9e6e3a2482631028c07ddc89cb6\nauthor charlesgong-openai <charlesgong@openai.com> 1780337061 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780337061 -0700\n\nPreserve plugin app manifest order (#25491)\n\n## Summary\n- Preserve app declaration order when loading plugin .app.json files.\n- Keep plugin connector summaries in plugin app order after connector\nmetadata is merged and filtered.\n- Add regression coverage for .app.json order and connector summary\norder.\n\n## Validation\n- just fmt\n- just test -p codex-chatgpt\nconnectors_for_plugin_apps_returns_only_requested_plugin_apps\n- just test -p codex-core-plugins\neffective_apps_preserves_app_config_order\n- just fix -p codex-core-plugins (passes with existing clippy\nlarge_enum_variant warning in core-plugins/src/manifest.rs)\n- just fix -p codex-chatgpt\n- just bazel-lock-update\n- just bazel-lock-check","verified_at":"2026-06-01T18:04:22Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/9756316d89968945212cd5f958b2b972c77c9e09","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/9756316d89968945212cd5f958b2b972c77c9e09","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/9756316d89968945212cd5f958b2b972c77c9e09/comments","author":{"login":"charlesgong-openai","id":200841148,"node_id":"U_kgDOC_iXvA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/200841148?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/charlesgong-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"6ddb747e7687e9e6e3a2482631028c07ddc89cb6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6ddb747e7687e9e6e3a2482631028c07ddc89cb6","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/6ddb747e7687e9e6e3a2482631028c07ddc89cb6"}]},{"sha":"6ddb747e7687e9e6e3a2482631028c07ddc89cb6","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDZkZGI3NDdlNzY4N2U5ZTZlM2EyNDgyNjMxMDI4YzA3ZGRjODljYjY","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif-oai","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-01T17:57:11Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-01T17:57:11Z"},"message":"[codex] Rename multi-agent v2 assign_task to followup_task (#25636)\n\n## Summary\n\nRenames the MultiAgentV2 turn-triggering tool from `assign_task` to\n`followup_task` so the exposed tool name better describes sending an\nadditional task to an existing agent.\n\nThis updates the tool spec, handler/module names, registry wiring,\ndefault multi-agent v2 usage hints, and tests. Rollout trace\nclassification keeps accepting legacy `assign_task` events so older\ntraces still reduce correctly, while docs show the new tool name.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- `just test -p codex-core followup_task`\n- `just test -p codex-core -E\n'test(multi_agent_feature_selects_one_agent_tool_family) |\ntest(multi_agent_v2_can_use_configured_tool_namespace) |\ntest(code_mode_only_can_expose_namespaced_multi_agent_v2_as_normal_tools)'`\n- `just test -p codex-rollout-trace`\n- `just fix -p codex-core`\n- `just fix -p codex-rollout-trace`\n\nNotes: `just fmt` ran `cargo fmt` but failed in the Python ruff phase\nbecause the local environment could not resolve `hatchling>=1.27.0` from\nthe configured internal registry. A full `just test -p codex-core` also\nhit unrelated environment-sensitive integration failures involving\nmissing spawned test binaries/sandbox behavior; the changed multi-agent\nspec/handler tests passed in the filtered runs above.","tree":{"sha":"77fbd676a8633d20d0bcbcf8a6f3e4f7b676eebd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/77fbd676a8633d20d0bcbcf8a6f3e4f7b676eebd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/6ddb747e7687e9e6e3a2482631028c07ddc89cb6","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHcf3CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAGMcQAJ4WaUr+t6g19E2LXF5Pszm4\nwJ2BeudSWrkzYFzVh+pB3Q9jlY50uOmhDzsU1zyRp1S6j7c6zFhoirgN+Rx7n6kt\nospGQxikZ08VDxq3/QQCIgs9N4SwCx7phMGs4rZQ2IbSPTdzm2ZSgMZqg311C0cP\ngPG2pIQezOse3nmKlHg2CmZdecTuV/bhhhBz9myRIMnrKEZxEOpgDqaQ0tvHRvm2\n87iH9nZ3N9ZcTKI3k7CT659fAXa4mgV48Er+EM3injvktrB4yDMMDcygyj/KJonI\nR15AYAkXCuQ2JlTEAPuDbyGezQdPNrNAWtXUeZ3zmVIJlF1JxgB+BIbv6SCa9RxA\nfUdQ6APUXK39BPDG9z2Ff8Y1qCeQ2UEtGV3gBALKF0yBvxA2yKHdqGMO1KTahEOl\nd37crb4tzYLYmdK2Et+U33WU/VwFoFDvQtNriQrCZkOghGBOgcncMdTo3oUOvJeN\nwpNSXyi5/v35Z4jn++32ClnlmUg6VmLIB4k/iNHYzwE55mcKz50Fxq5H7YGFScGh\nljaawcQyA9Qe8/TI4Lg24q9xNQFi3G5mQHte2njdgHzbSLtf1Kd1Y69vnMYh/crO\nEN5Vu9v5O//1LmBVrQ34jwiyMIancTPQ9pTqih76B9O6fcucqQLDwHpWMBI/BGsh\nhiK8NwNOxFwJcI3S6Vj+\n=ncSn\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 77fbd676a8633d20d0bcbcf8a6f3e4f7b676eebd\nparent fb94703b21571a577ba52efa5f7303946ef3cecd\nauthor jif-oai <jif@openai.com> 1780336631 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780336631 +0200\n\n[codex] Rename multi-agent v2 assign_task to followup_task (#25636)\n\n## Summary\n\nRenames the MultiAgentV2 turn-triggering tool from `assign_task` to\n`followup_task` so the exposed tool name better describes sending an\nadditional task to an existing agent.\n\nThis updates the tool spec, handler/module names, registry wiring,\ndefault multi-agent v2 usage hints, and tests. Rollout trace\nclassification keeps accepting legacy `assign_task` events so older\ntraces still reduce correctly, while docs show the new tool name.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- `just test -p codex-core followup_task`\n- `just test -p codex-core -E\n'test(multi_agent_feature_selects_one_agent_tool_family) |\ntest(multi_agent_v2_can_use_configured_tool_namespace) |\ntest(code_mode_only_can_expose_namespaced_multi_agent_v2_as_normal_tools)'`\n- `just test -p codex-rollout-trace`\n- `just fix -p codex-core`\n- `just fix -p codex-rollout-trace`\n\nNotes: `just fmt` ran `cargo fmt` but failed in the Python ruff phase\nbecause the local environment could not resolve `hatchling>=1.27.0` from\nthe configured internal registry. A full `just test -p codex-core` also\nhit unrelated environment-sensitive integration failures involving\nmissing spawned test binaries/sandbox behavior; the changed multi-agent\nspec/handler tests passed in the filtered runs above.","verified_at":"2026-06-01T17:57:12Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6ddb747e7687e9e6e3a2482631028c07ddc89cb6","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/6ddb747e7687e9e6e3a2482631028c07ddc89cb6","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6ddb747e7687e9e6e3a2482631028c07ddc89cb6/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"fb94703b21571a577ba52efa5f7303946ef3cecd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/fb94703b21571a577ba52efa5f7303946ef3cecd","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/fb94703b21571a577ba52efa5f7303946ef3cecd"}]},{"sha":"fb94703b21571a577ba52efa5f7303946ef3cecd","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGZiOTQ3MDNiMjE1NzFhNTc3YmE1MmVmYTVmNzMwMzk0NmVmM2NlY2Q","commit":{"author":{"name":"starr-openai","email":"starr@openai.com","date":"2026-06-01T17:55:52Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-01T17:55:52Z"},"message":"exec-server: add environment path refs (#25121)\n\n## Summary\n- add public `codex_exec_server::EnvironmentPathRef`\n- bind an absolute path to its owning executor filesystem\n- keep path operations in the next review slice\n\n## Stack\n- 1/5 in the skills path authority stack extracted from\nhttps://github.com/openai/codex/pull/25098\n\n## Validation\n- `cd /Users/starr/code/codex-worktrees/pr-25098-restack4/codex-rs &&\njust fmt`\n- GitHub CI pending on rewritten head","tree":{"sha":"c36fa5bb471c74c4442602bf1b48c09a020127a4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/c36fa5bb471c74c4442602bf1b48c09a020127a4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/fb94703b21571a577ba52efa5f7303946ef3cecd","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHceoCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAOmIQABLDJWz5iulWbcUkM9OhkFl3\n80lLi2xwwZecS7XQsh97sqbur4Bxq3S8yHWrUAI2swWV4RZXAg58KpcuqnhBZBZM\n7bjLNQfvn+EbcOPnSl2dLu0AGsQkQ6ekcS5ekZVESmYcYoFuR1AVKMLUPJmeFWoQ\nWXyMsFt4DFebWDCq18Tt7d4zcfkth3cpkvx8gRWeKEiPedh4x+eue0nz81yHsCej\nEj5S2XseQMqzzF7HKve7eLp24qWPbTzwG+J58UKON6K2LIWAbgEgpl211ec9ve+4\nzoQkA77mFnqYsAZRgOurXCc/7wemgrim2WktMEVSqsiCHHRQaQk01dXy9Xwha6YO\nTq3a1ebvdS59RPSDYn0u8ank2UWcjlS9CcTM2iPSrJBtOZL8AbJhYNJmUX0II/vq\nYga48Fv+UBMoxdv/ZQIKlvwZPqKCLEET+dlp0HZFrv7k/pU6UhYCj8giVDMwQqEj\ndA15Ds0zpiTZi6z5ZxMJnY+cF5kWbftMPWVZ5YWWgwNp+E9lF58sm7v+gtKJOrRf\n9YSfTDRYRwbhvabpbNpPU2Y/s2/i5qqi6ZqfIdxMSui/28U+HrgtxPb64lsYlNa5\nSvXVtqsnMWTlJSxFHpNcQapL6aneHDiZIH+qkhYwBYJbMYzM1NNvqUADNHsV2dPq\nrDDhGwNymoadtSBg+MMm\n=2WW0\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree c36fa5bb471c74c4442602bf1b48c09a020127a4\nparent 917a9a41a3b463fefc50fad51d653ff7f4243701\nauthor starr-openai <starr@openai.com> 1780336552 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780336552 -0700\n\nexec-server: add environment path refs (#25121)\n\n## Summary\n- add public `codex_exec_server::EnvironmentPathRef`\n- bind an absolute path to its owning executor filesystem\n- keep path operations in the next review slice\n\n## Stack\n- 1/5 in the skills path authority stack extracted from\nhttps://github.com/openai/codex/pull/25098\n\n## Validation\n- `cd /Users/starr/code/codex-worktrees/pr-25098-restack4/codex-rs &&\njust fmt`\n- GitHub CI pending on rewritten head","verified_at":"2026-06-01T17:55:53Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/fb94703b21571a577ba52efa5f7303946ef3cecd","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/fb94703b21571a577ba52efa5f7303946ef3cecd","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/fb94703b21571a577ba52efa5f7303946ef3cecd/comments","author":{"login":"starr-openai","id":176426273,"node_id":"U_kgDOCoQNIQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176426273?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/starr-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/starr-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/starr-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/starr-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/starr-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/starr-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/starr-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/starr-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/starr-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/starr-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/starr-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"917a9a41a3b463fefc50fad51d653ff7f4243701","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/917a9a41a3b463fefc50fad51d653ff7f4243701","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/917a9a41a3b463fefc50fad51d653ff7f4243701"}]},{"sha":"917a9a41a3b463fefc50fad51d653ff7f4243701","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDkxN2E5YTQxYTNiNDYzZmVmYzUwZmFkNTFkNjUzZmY3ZjQyNDM3MDE","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif-oai","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-01T17:54:52Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-01T17:54:52Z"},"message":"Parallelize cold rollout compression (#25654)\n\n## Why\n\n[#25089](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/25089) added the\nbackground worker for compressing cold archived rollouts, but the worker\nstill processed files effectively one at a time: each compression job\nwas sent to `spawn_blocking` and then awaited before the next file\nstarted. On machines with a backlog of archived rollouts, that makes\ncatch-up slower than it needs to be even though the actual compression\nwork already runs off the async runtime.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Queue rollout compression work in a `JoinSet` while directory\ntraversal continues.\n- Cap the worker at two in-flight compression jobs so it can overlap\ncompression without turning the background task into unbounded blocking\nwork.\n- Drain pending jobs before returning, including the\n`read_dir.next_entry()` error path, so every launched job still\ncontributes to the final `compressed`, `skipped`, and `failed` stats.\n- Treat task join failures the same way as compression failures in the\nworker's warning and failure accounting.","tree":{"sha":"ffc38d0c0dff583d2b8b27c3fdee9666e8734de5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/ffc38d0c0dff583d2b8b27c3fdee9666e8734de5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/917a9a41a3b463fefc50fad51d653ff7f4243701","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHcdsCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAdUoQAAE5TBNa7bvtwxgo4TiJEBdX\nmYRW0+t3Z2J8DkVMRhEPIq3WMUayZmVh4d70EH0pWlQuA7s3G/TCgmQnsaoaY1ic\n6HWqIB1Q+53mJJ4GoEXt4pJ+OJgg5NmVQAA/O+uJO4FHcWq5GaGV5IRi+8Mjngs/\nAD/BsT2BnERiZRvnGPXEdn/JsjH5iO54EsL9Evt69aW7RPHvCU0XIRM8MmQG+wMt\n5Zgx8zPxH+GRkC682H+E6yzmN0eZlHl3PY8MYS6d684Ff1CfA7Vx3W0n3Tj/rLo2\nwVu9LjPFtjGAl+aaNZM9EU+SGNcySbIa2aa1n5dvmZQ97x/lpcvKfY5Bb1MKBWxD\nu+ZABzLODO/Qclt3dK0eSeADQsB3fx7IvAJzmNlqSmfXMk8doSC5eIdlkqyyM0Dx\nH4TddpCk08TkhCvuOyEedJ2f4OSs8ZUd3FH1NdWasSQjiv1uDmGPCeNGMQgvQcLJ\nYjNJ35z+8I7ePV0zW0d5AQimh/Lk+mkDOF/0fHSuPnd4tYWjq7P7cULKefV7/5Sv\nKDg9YzM/1b9GUS9rvUqtucWHwINScpk/+ka6h+E5ERPnOOFwFr6ZYKlSWldHfjFv\nLbt+Iu+n5k+xnRdySbjGWJTP9znG+9jg0jMXvICl1WrIISL/NuspO/TcxnkxpqzB\nxkUh/1mG5BkP0DLz0vYP\n=Vlex\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree ffc38d0c0dff583d2b8b27c3fdee9666e8734de5\nparent e6eb462f07ae44f4bcb5280f16a516a355c4f2c5\nauthor jif-oai <jif@openai.com> 1780336492 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780336492 +0200\n\nParallelize cold rollout compression (#25654)\n\n## Why\n\n[#25089](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/25089) added the\nbackground worker for compressing cold archived rollouts, but the worker\nstill processed files effectively one at a time: each compression job\nwas sent to `spawn_blocking` and then awaited before the next file\nstarted. On machines with a backlog of archived rollouts, that makes\ncatch-up slower than it needs to be even though the actual compression\nwork already runs off the async runtime.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Queue rollout compression work in a `JoinSet` while directory\ntraversal continues.\n- Cap the worker at two in-flight compression jobs so it can overlap\ncompression without turning the background task into unbounded blocking\nwork.\n- Drain pending jobs before returning, including the\n`read_dir.next_entry()` error path, so every launched job still\ncontributes to the final `compressed`, `skipped`, and `failed` stats.\n- Treat task join failures the same way as compression failures in the\nworker's warning and failure accounting.","verified_at":"2026-06-01T17:54:52Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/917a9a41a3b463fefc50fad51d653ff7f4243701","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/917a9a41a3b463fefc50fad51d653ff7f4243701","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/917a9a41a3b463fefc50fad51d653ff7f4243701/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-o